// Content for The Family Map (node g57, ages 22+, Chapter 7) — NEW v2 build to GDD 57 (mechanic-embodying), the
// full-circle callback to My Family Garden (g03): in India you don't just marry a person, you join a family. 84
// researched, India-grounded scenarios across web-you-join → kind-boundaries → couple-team → respect-both-ways →
// when-it-turns-harmful → tools-and-help, each encoded as one of the shared v2 play actions (branch /
// strike-rewrite / sort / reflect / match / spot / role-play) — no binary "tap the right card". Lead: branch (your
// move), strike-rewrite (bust the myth), sort. Six modes: the web you join (map the extended family and your new
// place; BOTH partners join each other's families), kind boundaries (respectful limits that protect the couple
// without rejecting anyone; busts "family always knows best" / "interference is love" / "a good bahu never says
// no"), couple as a team (the couple is the primary team; a united, kind front; refuse triangulation; decide
// together, then face family as one), respect both ways (honour elders & culture while keeping your own voice;
// respect is not obedience and flows BOTH ways), when it turns harmful (dowry is illegal under the Dowry
// Prohibition Act 1961; coercive in-law control, threats & dowry harassment are abuse, not friction → Respect at
// Home g56 + help), tools & help. Even-handed and warm; NEVER "cut them off" as a default; honours the value
// placed on family while equipping couples to set kind limits. Links Equal Partners (g55) for the load and Respect
// at Home (g56) where dynamics become abusive. Builds on My Family Garden (g03). India: joint families and in-law
// ties are central and a leading source of marital strain; expectations fall heaviest on the daughter-in-law
// (sons-in-law increasingly adjust too); dowry is illegal; abuse routes to 181, 112 and a counsellor. gameId
// "family-map".
import type { V2GameConfig, Scenario } from "./v2-schema";

const SCENARIOS: Scenario[] = [
  {"id":"fm-001","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"You marry a person, not a family.\"","myth":{"un":"You marry a person, not a family.","re":"In India especially, marrying someone means joining their wider family and being joined to yours.","why":"A partnership lives inside an extended web of relationships."},"relearn":"Marriage joins two families, not just two people; that web is real either way.","persona":"Pooja","source":"you join a family"},
  {"id":"fm-002","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: part of the family web you're joining, or not your concern?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Your partner's parents and siblings"},{"id":"b","text":"A stranger on the street"},{"id":"c","text":"The relatives who'll be at every function"},{"id":"d","text":"A celebrity you follow online"},{"id":"e","text":"Your partner's grandparents and close cousins"},{"id":"f","text":"A neighbour you've never spoken to"}],"bins":[{"id":"web","label":"Your new web","valence":"pos"},{"id":"not","label":"Not your web","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"web","b":"not","c":"web","d":"not","e":"web","f":"not"},"relearn":"Your partner's close family becomes part of your everyday web; strangers and celebrities don't.","persona":"any","source":"mapping the web"},
  {"id":"fm-003","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"You've just married into a big joint family and feel lost about who's who.","options":[{"text":"Get curious: ask your partner to map the family and its unspoken rules","consequence":"You start to find your footing and your place.","outcome":"oriented","best":true},{"text":"Stay quiet and hope you'll figure it out without asking","consequence":"Mapping the family together finds your place faster than guessing."}],"debrief":"Understanding the web, and your place in it, is the first step to navigating it.","relearn":"Map the family and its unspoken rules together; that's how you find your place.","persona":"Pooja","source":"finding your place"},
  {"id":"fm-004","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each part of the new web to what it really is.","pairs":[{"left":"Your in-laws","right":"Your partner's parents, now family"},{"left":"Your partner's siblings","right":"New brothers or sisters-in-law"},{"left":"The extended relatives","right":"The wider circle at every function"},{"left":"Your partner's grandparents","right":"Elders to honour and get to know"},{"left":"Their cousins your age","right":"Possible friends within the family"}],"relearn":"In-laws, siblings-in-law and the extended relatives are the parts of the family web you join.","persona":"any","source":"who's who"},
  {"id":"fm-005","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"It's only the wife who has to adjust to a new family.\"","myth":{"un":"It's only the wife who has to adjust to a new family.","re":"Both partners join each other's families; increasingly sons-in-law adjust too, and that's healthy.","why":"Joining a family goes both ways, not just one."},"relearn":"Both partners join each other's families; adjusting isn't a one-way, wife-only job.","persona":"Karthik","source":"both ways"},
  {"id":"fm-006","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you're not just gaining a partner, you're gaining a whole web, with a place in it that's yours to shape. How does that land?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["It's a lot","Makes sense","Mine to shape"],"affirm":"Seeing the whole web, and that your place in it is yours to shape, is where navigating it begins.","relearn":"Your place in the new family web is yours to shape, not just inherit.","persona":"any","source":"your place to shape"},
  {"id":"fm-007","cat":"web-you-join","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two myths about joining a family — the lines that aren't true.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Building new relationships over time","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Having to instantly love everyone","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Learning the family's rhythms and ways","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Being owed everyone's full trust on day one","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Letting closeness grow at its own pace","trick":false}],"why":"Instant love and day-one trust are the myths; warmth and trust are built slowly, over time.","relearn":"Joining a family is about building relationships over time, not instant, automatic love.","persona":"any","source":"real vs myth"},
  {"id":"fm-008","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"Your partner's family does things very differently from how you grew up.","options":[{"text":"Treat the differences as things to learn, not as wrong","consequence":"You stay open and adapt without losing yourself.","outcome":"open","best":true},{"text":"Decide their way is wrong because it's not what you're used to","consequence":"Labelling their way wrong, instead of learning it, starts needless conflict."}],"debrief":"Different isn't wrong; family customs vary, and learning them beats judging them.","relearn":"Different family ways are things to learn, not proof that one side is wrong.","persona":"Sneha","source":"different not wrong"},
  {"id":"fm-009","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each new in-law tie to a warm way to begin it.","pairs":[{"left":"A reserved mother-in-law","right":"Small, genuine gestures over time"},{"left":"A talkative father-in-law","right":"Listen and ask about his stories"},{"left":"A guarded sibling-in-law","right":"Patience, no forcing closeness"},{"left":"A warm, busy aunt","right":"A quick call to stay in touch"},{"left":"A shy younger cousin-in-law","right":"A light, friendly hello first"}],"relearn":"Each new relationship starts best with patience and small, genuine gestures, not forced closeness.","persona":"any","source":"starting the ties"},
  {"id":"fm-010","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A good marriage means the two families merge into one with no differences.\"","myth":{"un":"A good marriage means the two families merge into one with no differences.","re":"Two families staying distinct, with their own ways, can still be close and respectful.","why":"Closeness doesn't require erasing every difference between families."},"relearn":"Families can stay distinct and still be close; merging into sameness isn't the goal.","persona":"any","source":"distinct yet close"},
  {"id":"fm-011","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a realistic hope for the new family web, or an unfair expectation?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Building warmth over years"},{"id":"b","text":"Everyone agreeing on everything at once"},{"id":"c","text":"Mutual respect from the start"},{"id":"d","text":"Becoming everyone's favourite instantly"},{"id":"e","text":"Getting to know each relative slowly"},{"id":"f","text":"Erasing your own family's ways to fit in"}],"bins":[{"id":"real","label":"Realistic","valence":"pos"},{"id":"unfair","label":"Unfair expectation","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"real","b":"unfair","c":"real","d":"unfair","e":"real","f":"unfair"},"relearn":"Warmth over time and mutual respect are realistic; instant agreement and being everyone's favourite aren't.","persona":"Pooja","source":"realistic hopes"},
  {"id":"fm-012","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: finding your place doesn't mean shrinking to fit, it means taking up your fair space in the web. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","Taking my space","Not shrinking"],"affirm":"Finding your place means taking up your fair space in the family, not shrinking yourself to fit.","relearn":"Finding your place means taking your fair space, not shrinking to fit the family.","persona":"any","source":"not shrinking"},
  {"id":"fm-013","cat":"web-you-join","type":"role-play","hook":"A relative asks how you're settling into the family. You want to be warm and honest.","setup":"Answer warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Still learning everyone's ways, but I'm glad to be part of this family.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Fine, I guess.\""}],"relearn":"A warm, honest answer builds the new ties: glad to be here, and still learning.","persona":"Sneha","source":"settling in"},
  {"id":"fm-014","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"You've been so focused on being accepted that you've forgotten to know them as people.","options":[{"text":"Get curious about them as individuals, not just as 'the in-laws'","consequence":"Real relationships start to form.","outcome":"curious","best":true},{"text":"Keep performing the 'perfect' new spouse to win approval","consequence":"Performing perfection just exhausts you; curiosity is what builds real ties."}],"debrief":"In-laws are individuals to know, not just roles to impress; curiosity builds real bonds.","relearn":"Get to know in-laws as people, not just roles to win over.","persona":"any","source":"as people"},
  {"id":"fm-015","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Setting a boundary with family means you're rejecting them.\"","myth":{"un":"Setting a boundary with family means you're rejecting them.","re":"A boundary is about protecting the relationship, not ending it; you can say no and still love them.","why":"Boundaries protect closeness; they don't destroy it."},"relearn":"A boundary protects the relationship; saying no kindly isn't rejection.","persona":"Pooja","source":"boundaries protect"},
  {"id":"fm-016","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Family always knows best, so you should just do as they say.\"","myth":{"un":"Family always knows best, so you should just do as they say.","re":"Elders deserve respect, but you and your partner get to decide your own life together.","why":"Respecting elders doesn't mean handing them every decision."},"relearn":"Respect elders, but the couple still decides their own life; 'they know best' isn't a rule to obey blindly.","persona":"Pooja","source":"knows best myth"},
  {"id":"fm-017","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: the couple's own call to make, or genuinely the wider family's to decide?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"When you two have children"},{"id":"b","text":"The menu for a shared family festival"},{"id":"c","text":"How you spend your own salary"},{"id":"d","text":"A joint family ritual everyone shares"},{"id":"e","text":"Which schools or careers you two choose"},{"id":"f","text":"Hosting the annual family puja together"}],"bins":[{"id":"couple","label":"Couple's call","valence":"neutral"},{"id":"family","label":"Shared family call","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"couple","b":"family","c":"couple","d":"family","e":"couple","f":"family"},"relearn":"Your children, salary and your own paths are the couple's call; genuinely shared rituals can be decided together.","persona":"any","source":"whose call"},
  {"id":"fm-018","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Your in-laws drop by unannounced often, and you and your partner never get private time.","options":[{"text":"Agree a kind boundary together and set it warmly, e.g. a heads-up call first","consequence":"You get privacy without anyone feeling shut out.","outcome":"bounded","best":true},{"text":"Say nothing and quietly grow resentful","consequence":"Silence just breeds resentment that leaks out later."}],"debrief":"A kind, clear boundary, set together, protects the couple without rejecting anyone.","relearn":"Set kind boundaries together and warmly; silence turns into resentment.","persona":"Pooja","source":"kind boundary"},
  {"id":"fm-019","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"match","hook":"Match a harsh way to set a limit with its kinder version.","pairs":[{"left":"“Stop interfering in our lives.”","right":"“We love your input; this one's ours.”"},{"left":"“You're always here.”","right":"“We'd love a heads-up before visits.”"},{"left":"“Mind your own business.”","right":"“We'll ask you for advice on this.”"},{"left":"“Stop controlling everything.”","right":"“We'd like to choose this as a couple.”"},{"left":"“Leave us alone for once.”","right":"“We'd love a quiet evening, just us two.”"}],"relearn":"The same boundary can be said with warmth instead of harshness.","persona":"any","source":"kinder version"},
  {"id":"fm-020","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Interference is just love, so you have to accept all of it.\"","myth":{"un":"Interference is just love, so you have to accept all of it.","re":"Concern can come from love and still cross a line; you can receive the love and decline the overreach.","why":"You can honour the love behind it and still keep the boundary."},"relearn":"Care and overreach can both be true; accept the love, keep the boundary.","persona":"Sneha","source":"love and limit"},
  {"id":"fm-021","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two walls that just shut people out, not the kind boundaries.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“We'll decide this together, and tell you once we have.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Cold silence and avoiding them for weeks","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“We love visits, just call first.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Cutting off all contact after one small argument","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“This one's ours to decide, with love.”","trick":false}],"why":"Cold weeks of silence and cutting off after one small row are walls; a kind boundary names the limit warmly.","relearn":"A kind boundary is warm and clear; cold cut-offs and silent freeze-outs are walls, not boundaries.","persona":"any","source":"boundary not wall"},
  {"id":"fm-022","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a boundary said with warmth, 'we love you, and this is ours to decide', is the strongest kind. Make sense?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Makes sense","Warm and firm","I'll try it"],"affirm":"The strongest boundary pairs warmth with clarity: love them, and still hold the line.","relearn":"The strongest boundary is warm and firm together: 'we love you, and this is ours.'","persona":"any","source":"warm and firm"},
  {"id":"fm-023","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"A relative keeps pushing for a decision you and your partner aren't ready to make.","options":[{"text":"Buy time kindly: 'we hear you, we'll decide together and let you know'","consequence":"You hold the boundary without a fight.","outcome":"held","best":true},{"text":"Cave just to end the discomfort","consequence":"Buying time kindly holds the boundary; caving to end discomfort trades your real choice for a moment's peace."}],"debrief":"You can hold a boundary kindly under pressure without caving or fighting.","relearn":"Hold the line kindly under pressure: 'we'll decide together and tell you.'","persona":"Karthik","source":"holding under push"},
  {"id":"fm-024","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a healthy boundary, or actually shutting family out unkindly?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Asking for a call before visits"},{"id":"b","text":"Blocking their number out of spite"},{"id":"c","text":"Keeping your finances your own"},{"id":"d","text":"Refusing to ever see them again over a small slight"},{"id":"e","text":"Saying yes to many family things, no to a few"},{"id":"f","text":"Going silent for months to punish them"}],"bins":[{"id":"healthy","label":"Healthy boundary","valence":"pos"},{"id":"unkind","label":"Unkindly shutting out","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"healthy","b":"unkind","c":"healthy","d":"unkind","e":"healthy","f":"unkind"},"relearn":"Asking for notice, keeping finances, and saying yes-and-sometimes-no are healthy; spite-blocking and silent punishment aren't.","persona":"any","source":"healthy vs shut-out"},
  {"id":"fm-025","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"role-play","hook":"Your mother-in-law offers strong opinions on how you should run your kitchen. You want to be warm but clear.","setup":"Say it kindly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I love learning your recipes, Ma, and I'll run the kitchen my own way too.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Please just let me do it myself.\""}],"relearn":"You can welcome the warmth and still hold your own way, in the same kind sentence.","persona":"Pooja","source":"kitchen boundary"},
  {"id":"fm-026","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A good daughter-in-law never says no to family.\"","myth":{"un":"A good daughter-in-law never says no to family.","re":"Respect and a kind 'no' can coexist; saying no to overreach doesn't make you a bad bahu.","why":"Self-respect and family respect aren't opposites."},"relearn":"A kind 'no' is compatible with respect; never saying no isn't the measure of a good bahu.","persona":"Pooja","source":"kind no"},
  {"id":"fm-027","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Your partner's family expects you to drop your own plans whenever they call.","options":[{"text":"Lovingly hold some plans as yours while saying yes to many family things too","consequence":"You stay connected and keep a self.","outcome":"balanced","best":true},{"text":"Cancel everything of your own, every time, to avoid upset","consequence":"Cancelling everything every time erases you and breeds resentment."}],"debrief":"You can say yes to family often and still keep some plans as your own.","relearn":"Keep some plans your own; saying yes always, at your own cost, erases you.","persona":"Sneha","source":"keep a self"},
  {"id":"fm-028","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: boundaries aren't built once, they're re-set gently, again and again, as people test them. Ready for that?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Ready","Again and again","That's real"],"affirm":"Boundaries are maintained, not set once; re-stating them gently over time is normal and healthy.","relearn":"Boundaries are re-set gently over time, not built once and forgotten.","persona":"any","source":"re-set gently"},
  {"id":"fm-029","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"In a disagreement with family, you should always side with your own parents.\"","myth":{"un":"In a disagreement with family, you should always side with your own parents.","re":"Your partner and you are the primary team; you decide together, then face the wider family as one.","why":"The couple is the core unit decisions run through."},"relearn":"The couple is the primary team; decide together first, not parents-first by default.","persona":"Karthik","source":"couple is the team"},
  {"id":"fm-030","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Your mother criticises your partner to you, hoping you'll agree and take her side.","options":[{"text":"Gently defend your partner and decline to be triangulated","consequence":"Your partner trusts you, and the family learns you're solid.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Join in the criticism to keep your mother happy","consequence":"Joining in teaches the family they can divide you."}],"debrief":"Don't let a relative triangulate you against your partner; the couple stands together.","relearn":"Refuse triangulation: defend your partner kindly rather than siding against them.","persona":"Karthik","source":"no triangulation"},
  {"id":"fm-031","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a united-front move, or something that quietly undermines the couple?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Agreeing your stance privately before family"},{"id":"b","text":"Letting family hear you blame your partner"},{"id":"c","text":"Backing your partner, debriefing later"},{"id":"d","text":"Making big calls with parents, not your partner"},{"id":"e","text":"Giving relatives one calm, shared answer"},{"id":"f","text":"Promising a relative something secretly"}],"bins":[{"id":"united","label":"United front","valence":"pos"},{"id":"undermine","label":"Undermines","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"united","b":"undermine","c":"united","d":"undermine","e":"united","f":"undermine"},"relearn":"Aligning, backing each other and one answer are a united front; blame or secret promises undermine it.","persona":"any","source":"united or not"},
  {"id":"fm-032","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A husband torn between his mother and his wife should just keep them both happy somehow.\"","myth":{"un":"A husband torn between his mother and his wife should just keep them both happy by pleasing each in turn.","re":"He doesn't have to choose sides; he stands with his partner as a team while still respecting his mother.","why":"Partnership-first isn't the same as disrespecting a parent."},"relearn":"He isn't 'torn': he stands with his partner as a team and respects his mother; both at once.","persona":"Karthik","source":"not torn"},
  {"id":"fm-033","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match a family-pressure moment to the couple-team response.","pairs":[{"left":"Relatives push a big decision on the spot","right":"'We'll talk and come back to you'"},{"left":"One partner is being singled out","right":"The other steps in to back them"},{"left":"Plans clash between two families","right":"The couple agrees its own plan first"},{"left":"A relative asks you to keep a secret","right":"You decline, keeping no side-deals"},{"left":"A parent runs your partner down","right":"You warmly close the wedge"}],"relearn":"The couple-team response: decide together, back each other, refuse secrets, give one kind united answer.","persona":"any","source":"team responses"},
  {"id":"fm-034","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"You and your partner disagree about a family matter, in front of the whole family.","options":[{"text":"Pause it: 'let's talk privately and come back', then resolve as a team","consequence":"You protect both the decision and the partnership.","outcome":"private-first","best":true},{"text":"Argue it out in front of everyone, taking sides","consequence":"Arguing in front of family invites everyone to pick a side."}],"debrief":"Disagree in private, decide as a team, present one answer; don't fight in front of family.","relearn":"Resolve couple disagreements privately, then face family as one team.","persona":"Sneha","source":"private then united"},
  {"id":"fm-035","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the couple is the new first team. That isn't disloyal to your parents, it's what marriage means. Sit right?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Sits right","New first team","Still respect parents"],"affirm":"Making the couple the primary team isn't disloyalty to parents; it's the core of a partnership.","relearn":"The couple becomes the first team, while still honouring parents; that isn't disloyalty.","persona":"any","source":"first team"},
  {"id":"fm-036","cat":"couple-team","type":"role-play","hook":"At dinner, a relative tries to get you to agree your partner is 'too modern'. You want to back your partner warmly.","setup":"Say warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I actually love that about them, we're figuring our life out together.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Hmm, maybe you're right.\""}],"relearn":"Backing your partner warmly in the room keeps the team solid and ends the wedge.","persona":"Karthik","source":"back them warmly"},
  {"id":"fm-037","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a decision the couple should make as a team, or one to share with the elders too?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"How you split chores and money"},{"id":"b","text":"Hosting a shared family puja"},{"id":"c","text":"Whether and when to have kids"},{"id":"d","text":"Planning a joint family holiday"},{"id":"e","text":"Where the two of you decide to live"},{"id":"f","text":"Organising a big family wedding together"}],"bins":[{"id":"couple","label":"Couple-team call","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shared","label":"Share with elders","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"couple","b":"shared","c":"couple","d":"shared","e":"couple","f":"shared"},"relearn":"Chores, money, kids and where you live are the couple's; shared pujas, joint holidays and a big wedding can be planned with elders too.","persona":"Pooja","source":"team vs shared"},
  {"id":"fm-038","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Keeping secrets from your partner to protect your family is loyalty.\"","myth":{"un":"Keeping secrets from your partner to protect your family is loyalty.","re":"The couple-team runs on honesty between you two; hidden family deals erode the trust the team needs.","why":"Transparency with your partner is what keeps the team strong."},"relearn":"The couple runs on honesty; hiding family matters from your partner weakens the team, not protects it.","persona":"any","source":"team honesty"},
  {"id":"fm-039","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Your family asks you to make a financial commitment without telling your partner.","options":[{"text":"Decline to hide it: 'we decide money together, I'll talk to them'","consequence":"Your partnership stays trustworthy and aligned.","outcome":"transparent","best":true},{"text":"Quietly agree and keep it from your partner","consequence":"A hidden money deal is exactly what breaks trust later."}],"debrief":"Big commitments go through the couple-team together, never hidden from your partner.","relearn":"Keep money and big commitments transparent between partners, not hidden for family.","persona":"Karthik","source":"no hidden deals"},
  {"id":"fm-040","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: 'we'll decide together and let you know' is the most useful sentence in a joint family. Worth memorising?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Worth it","Memorising it","So useful"],"affirm":"'We'll decide together and let you know' protects the couple-team kindly in almost any family pressure.","relearn":"One sentence carries the couple-team: 'we'll decide together and let you know.'","persona":"any","source":"the useful sentence"},
  {"id":"fm-041","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each couple-team habit to what it protects.","pairs":[{"left":"Aligning before family events","right":"Fewer surprises and public clashes"},{"left":"Debriefing afterward","right":"Repair and learning as a team"},{"left":"One united answer to pressure","right":"Trust that you've got each other"},{"left":"Keeping money decisions shared","right":"No hidden deals that break trust"},{"left":"A steady, repeatable team line","right":"No fresh fight at every demand"}],"relearn":"Aligning before, debriefing after, sharing money, one answer and a steady line are the habits that keep a couple solid in a big family.","persona":"any","source":"team habits"},
  {"id":"fm-042","cat":"couple-team","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that break the couple-team under family pressure.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Checking in privately before answering relatives","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Letting relatives split you by flattery","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Backing each other in the room","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Blaming your partner to look good","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Giving one calm, shared answer","trick":false}],"why":"Letting flattery split you and blaming your partner break the team; checking in, backing each other and a shared answer keep it.","relearn":"Stay a team: align privately and back each other; don't let flattery split you or blame your partner.","persona":"Sneha","source":"stay a team"},
  {"id":"fm-043","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Respecting elders means obeying them in everything.\"","myth":{"un":"Respecting elders means obeying them in everything.","re":"Respect means honouring and listening to elders; it doesn't mean surrendering every choice to them.","why":"You can deeply respect someone and still disagree."},"relearn":"Respect means honouring and listening, not obeying in everything; you can respect and still choose.","persona":"Pooja","source":"respect not obedience"},
  {"id":"fm-044","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"branch","hook":"An elder gives advice you disagree with, but you don't want to be disrespectful.","options":[{"text":"Thank them sincerely, consider it, then decide for yourselves","consequence":"You honour them and keep your own choice.","outcome":"honoured","best":true},{"text":"Either obey to avoid offence or dismiss them rudely","consequence":"Obeying or dismissing loses either the elder's respect or your own autonomy."}],"debrief":"You can receive elders' advice with real respect and still make your own decision.","relearn":"Honour the advice sincerely, then decide for yourselves; both can coexist.","persona":"Sneha","source":"honour then choose"},
  {"id":"fm-045","type":"match","hook":"Match each elder's offering to the respectful way to receive it.","pairs":[{"left":"Hard-won life wisdom","right":"Listen genuinely, take what fits"},{"left":"An outdated expectation","right":"Decline kindly, without scorn"},{"left":"A warm tradition","right":"Join in where it's meaningful to you"},{"left":"A worried warning","right":"Thank them, then weigh it yourself"},{"left":"A generous offer","right":"Accept warmly, or decline gently"}],"relearn":"Respect both ways means hearing wisdom, declining the outdated kindly, joining what's meaningful, weighing warnings and handling offers gracefully.","persona":"any","source":"receiving respectfully","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-046","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If you keep your own views, you're being a disrespectful, modern troublemaker.\"","myth":{"un":"If you keep your own views, you're being a disrespectful, modern troublemaker.","re":"Holding your own values respectfully is healthy; respect flows both ways between generations.","why":"Having a voice and showing respect aren't opposites."},"relearn":"Keeping your own values respectfully isn't disrespect; respect is meant to flow both ways.","persona":"Pooja","source":"voice and respect"},
  {"id":"fm-047","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: respect flowing both ways, or respect demanded only one way?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Elders' experience is valued"},{"id":"b","text":"Only the young must adjust, never elders"},{"id":"c","text":"The couple's choices are also respected"},{"id":"d","text":"Disagreement from the young is 'insolence'"},{"id":"e","text":"Both sides can own a mistake"},{"id":"f","text":"Elders are above every question"}],"bins":[{"id":"both","label":"Both ways","valence":"pos"},{"id":"one","label":"One way only","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"both","b":"one","c":"both","d":"one","e":"both","f":"one"},"relearn":"Valuing elders and the couple's choices, with apologies on both sides, is mutual; all the adjusting and silence on one side isn't.","persona":"any","source":"both ways or one","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-048","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the goal isn't to win against elders, it's a relationship where both generations feel respected. Resonate?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Resonates","Both respected","Not winning"],"affirm":"The aim is mutual respect across generations, not defeating the elders or being defeated by them.","relearn":"The goal is mutual respect across generations, not winning against elders.","persona":"any","source":"mutual respect"},
  {"id":"fm-049","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two that are fear dressed up as respect, not the real thing.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Listening because you value their experience","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Agreeing only because you're scared to speak","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Disagreeing politely and still being warm","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Going silent in dread of their anger","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Weighing their advice, then choosing","trick":false}],"why":"Scared agreement and dread-driven silence are just fear; valuing experience and warm disagreement are real respect.","relearn":"Real respect includes honest disagreement; silent fear isn't respect.","persona":"Sneha","source":"respect not fear","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-050","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"branch","hook":"Your in-laws follow a tradition that doesn't fit your beliefs, but want you to join.","options":[{"text":"Join the parts you can warmly, and opt out of the rest kindly","consequence":"You honour the bond without betraying yourself.","outcome":"warm-opt","best":true},{"text":"Either fake full belief or refuse the whole thing coldly","consequence":"Faking belief or refusing coldly loses either the bond or yourself."}],"debrief":"Take part in a tradition warmly where you can, and decline the rest respectfully.","relearn":"Join traditions where you can and opt out kindly; honour the bond and yourself.","persona":"Razia","source":"join and opt out"},
  {"id":"fm-051","type":"match","hook":"Match a respectful phrase to the situation it fits.","pairs":[{"left":"\"Thank you, that helps; we'll think it over.\"","right":"Receiving unsolicited advice"},{"left":"\"We see it differently, with respect.\"","right":"A genuine disagreement"},{"left":"\"We'd love to do it our way this time.\"","right":"A choice that's yours to make"},{"left":"\"We'll keep the heart of it, our version.\"","right":"A tradition you'll adapt"},{"left":"\"I'd still like to finish my thought.\"","right":"Being talked over"}],"relearn":"Respectful phrasing lets you receive advice, disagree, choose, adapt a custom and ask to be heard, all without contempt.","persona":"any","source":"respectful phrasing","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-052","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"In-laws can never really become close, loving family.\"","myth":{"un":"In-laws can never really become close, loving family.","re":"Many in-law bonds grow into genuine warmth and support over time, with patience on both sides.","why":"These relationships can become some of life's most supportive."},"relearn":"In-law bonds can grow into real, loving family with time and patience; the cynical version isn't fixed.","persona":"Pooja","source":"bonds can grow"},
  {"id":"fm-053","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: an elder who feels respected is far more open to your boundaries. Respect and boundaries work together. See it?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["I see it","They work together","Worth remembering"],"affirm":"Respect and boundaries reinforce each other: a respected elder is more open to your limits.","relearn":"Respect and boundaries reinforce each other; a respected elder hears your limits better.","persona":"any","source":"respect aids boundaries"},
  {"id":"fm-054","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"role-play","hook":"An elder shares strong advice about your career that you won't be taking. Be respectful and clear.","setup":"Respond warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Thank you for caring about my future, I've thought hard and I'm going my own way on this.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You don't understand my life, stop telling me what to do.\""}],"relearn":"Gratitude plus a clear, warm 'my own way' honours the elder and your autonomy at once.","persona":"Sneha","source":"career advice"},
  {"id":"fm-055","cat":"respect-both-ways","type":"branch","hook":"You catch yourself resenting your in-laws and writing them off entirely.","options":[{"text":"Stay open to building the bond, while keeping your boundaries","consequence":"Respect and warmth have room to grow.","outcome":"open","best":true},{"text":"Decide the relationship is hopeless and stop trying","consequence":"Writing them off guarantees the very distance you fear."}],"debrief":"Keep the door open to the bond even as you hold boundaries; don't write the relationship off.","relearn":"Hold boundaries and stay open to the bond; writing in-laws off ends what could grow.","persona":"any","source":"stay open"},
  {"id":"fm-056","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A little dowry is just tradition, so it's fine.\"","myth":{"un":"A little dowry is just tradition, so it's fine.","re":"Dowry is illegal in India, giving, taking and demanding it are all offences under the Dowry Prohibition Act, 1961.","why":"The law bans dowry whatever the custom is called."},"relearn":"Dowry, giving, taking or demanding, is illegal under the Dowry Prohibition Act, 1961, not just 'tradition'.","persona":"Razia","source":"dowry is illegal"},
  {"id":"fm-057","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Boundary problems and abuse from in-laws are the same thing.\"","myth":{"un":"Boundary problems and abuse from in-laws are the same thing.","re":"Normal friction is about limits and adjusting; abuse is a pattern of control, threats, dowry harassment or violence, and needs help.","why":"There's a clear line between everyday friction and abuse."},"relearn":"Everyday friction differs from abuse, a pattern of control, threats or dowry harassment; abuse needs help.","persona":"Reshma","source":"friction vs abuse"},
  {"id":"fm-058","type":"sort","persona":"Reshma","source":"friction or red flag","hook":"Sort: ordinary family friction to work through, or a red flag that needs help?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Disagreeing about visit frequency"},{"id":"b","text":"Demands for money or gifts under threat"},{"id":"c","text":"Differing festival customs"},{"id":"d","text":"Controlling your movements, phone or money"},{"id":"e","text":"A clash over how to spend a shared weekend"},{"id":"f","text":"Being threatened if you don't obey"}],"bins":[{"id":"friction","label":"Work-through friction","valence":"pos"},{"id":"redflag","label":"Red flag, get help","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"friction","b":"redflag","c":"friction","d":"redflag","e":"friction","f":"redflag"},"relearn":"Visit, custom and weekend clashes are friction; threats for money, control and intimidation are red flags needing help.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-059","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"branch","hook":"Your in-laws begin pressuring your family for money and gifts after the wedding.","options":[{"text":"Name it as dowry harassment, talk to your partner, and seek help","consequence":"You treat an illegal, serious harm seriously.","outcome":"named","best":true},{"text":"Pay quietly to keep the peace and tell no one","consequence":"Paying quietly to keep the peace usually just invites more demands."}],"debrief":"Post-wedding demands for money are dowry harassment, which is illegal; name it and get help.","relearn":"Post-wedding money demands are illegal dowry harassment; name it and seek help.","persona":"Razia","source":"name dowry harassment"},
  {"id":"fm-060","type":"spot","persona":"Reshma","source":"coercive control","hook":"Spot the two signs that in-law conflict has crossed into coercive control.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Disagreeing about how to host a festival","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Being cut off from your own money and friends","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Being threatened if you don't obey","trick":true},{"id":"d","text":"Differing tastes in food or routine","trick":false},{"id":"e","text":"Working out a fair share of chores","trick":false}],"why":"Festival clashes, differing tastes and sorting chores are normal; cutting you off from money and friends, and threats, are control.","relearn":"Being isolated from money and people, or threatened, is coercive control, not ordinary conflict.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-061","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"What happens inside the family is private, so no one should ever get help.\"","myth":{"un":"What happens inside the family is private, so no one should ever get help.","re":"Privacy never covers abuse; you have every right to seek help when control, threats or violence appear.","why":"Abuse isn't a private matter to be hidden."},"relearn":"Privacy doesn't cover abuse; you can always seek help when there's control, threats or violence.","persona":"Reshma","source":"not a private matter"},
  {"id":"fm-062","type":"match","persona":"Reshma","source":"help routes","hook":"Match each India help route to when it's for.","pairs":[{"left":"Women's Helpline 181","right":"In-law abuse or dowry harassment"},{"left":"Police / emergency 112","right":"Immediate danger or violence"},{"left":"Respect at Home (g56) + a counsellor","right":"Naming and planning around abuse"},{"left":"Women in distress 1091","right":"A woman who feels unsafe right now"},{"left":"Childline 1098","right":"A girl about to be married off"}],"relearn":"181, 1091, 112, 1098 and a counsellor are real routes when family conflict turns to abuse, dowry harassment or danger.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-063","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"branch","hook":"A friend confides that her in-laws control her every move and threaten her.","options":[{"text":"Believe her, tell her it's not okay, and share help options gently","consequence":"She feels supported and less alone.","outcome":"supported","best":true},{"text":"Tell her it's normal and she should just adjust","consequence":"Calling abuse 'normal adjusting' leaves her trapped."}],"debrief":"When someone describes control and threats, believe them and offer help, never 'just adjust'.","relearn":"Believe someone describing control and threats; offer help, don't tell them to adjust.","persona":"Razia","source":"believe and support"},
  {"id":"fm-064","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: kind boundaries handle the everyday, but control, threats or dowry demands aren't boundary problems, they need help. Clear?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Clear","That's different","Get help then"],"affirm":"Boundaries handle ordinary friction; control, threats and dowry demands are abuse that needs help, not negotiation.","relearn":"Control, threats and dowry demands aren't boundary problems; they're abuse that needs help.","persona":"Reshma","source":"beyond boundaries"},
  {"id":"fm-065","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Anti-dowry and cruelty laws are only ever misused, so they don't really protect anyone.\"","myth":{"un":"Anti-dowry and cruelty laws are only ever misused, so they don't really protect anyone.","re":"These laws exist to protect people from real, serious harm; misuse can occur, but the protections are genuine and important.","why":"Protections being imperfect doesn't make them fake."},"relearn":"Anti-dowry and cruelty laws offer real protection from serious harm, even though misuse is debated.","persona":"Reshma","source":"real protection"},
  {"id":"fm-066","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: when a home stops feeling safe, telling one trusted person is a strong first step, not a betrayal of the family. Sit right with you?","prompt":"What's your read?","options":["Sits right","Telling is a step","Not betrayal"],"affirm":"Speaking to one trusted person when home feels unsafe is a brave first move, not a betrayal of anyone.","relearn":"Telling one trusted person when home turns unsafe is a strong first step, never a betrayal.","persona":"Reshma","source":"telling isn't betrayal"},
  {"id":"fm-067","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"branch","hook":"You're unsure whether what you're going through at home 'counts' as serious enough.","options":[{"text":"Reach out anyway, a counsellor or 181 can help you make sense of it","consequence":"You get clarity and support without having to be certain.","outcome":"reached","best":true},{"text":"Wait until it's 'bad enough', alone","consequence":"Waiting until it's 'bad enough', alone, often means too long."}],"debrief":"You don't have to be certain it's 'serious enough' to reach out; help can start with uncertainty.","relearn":"You can seek help while still unsure; don't wait until it's 'bad enough'.","persona":"Reshma","source":"reach out anyway"},
  {"id":"fm-068","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"Before a big family visit, you want to avoid the usual blow-ups.","options":[{"text":"Run a two-minute couple check-in: agree your line on the likely topics","consequence":"You arrive aligned and calm.","outcome":"aligned","best":true},{"text":"Wing it and hope nothing comes up","consequence":"A quick check-in to agree your line keeps you aligned; winging it leaves you to be split in the moment."}],"debrief":"A two-minute pre-visit check-in, agreeing your line, prevents most family blow-ups.","relearn":"Align before visits with a quick couple check-in; don't wing the hard topics.","persona":"Pooja","source":"pre-visit check-in"},
  {"id":"fm-069","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each tool to the job it does.","pairs":[{"left":"The warm 'no'","right":"Decline without rejecting"},{"left":"The couple check-in","right":"Agree your line before family time"},{"left":"The repeatable team line","right":"Answer as one, every time"},{"left":"Knowing the family map","right":"Feel placed, not powerless"},{"left":"The help routes","right":"When friction becomes abuse"}],"relearn":"The warm no, the check-in, the team line, the map and the help routes are the core tools of navigating family kindly and safely.","persona":"any","source":"the toolkit"},
  {"id":"fm-070","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"A relative pushes you to justify a private decision. You want a warm, firm, repeatable line.","setup":"Use the line:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"We've thought about it and we're happy with our choice, thank you for caring.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Ugh, why do you always ask me that?\""}],"relearn":"A warm, firm, repeatable line ends the pressure without a fight, every time.","persona":"Karthik","source":"the repeatable line"},
  {"id":"fm-071","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a tool that protects the relationship, or a habit that quietly damages it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Agreeing your stance privately first"},{"id":"b","text":"Venting about in-laws to everyone but them"},{"id":"c","text":"A warm, clear 'no'"},{"id":"d","text":"Silent resentment that builds for months"},{"id":"e","text":"Backing each other in the room"},{"id":"f","text":"Cutting them off at the first clash"}],"bins":[{"id":"tool","label":"Protective tool","valence":"pos"},{"id":"damage","label":"Quietly damaging","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"tool","b":"damage","c":"tool","d":"damage","e":"tool","f":"damage"},"relearn":"Aligning privately, the warm no and team-backing protect the bond; gossip, silent resentment and snap cut-offs corrode it.","persona":"any","source":"tool or damage"},
  {"id":"fm-072","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"There's nothing you can actually do about family dynamics, you just endure them.\"","myth":{"un":"There's nothing you can actually do about family dynamics, you just endure them.","re":"You have real tools, alignment, kind boundaries, repeatable lines and help routes, that change the dynamic over time.","why":"Family dynamics are workable, not just endurable."},"relearn":"You're not powerless; alignment, boundaries, lines and help routes genuinely shift family dynamics over time.","persona":"any","source":"not powerless"},
  {"id":"fm-073","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you can't control how relatives act, but you can control your alignment, your boundaries and your warmth. Enough to start?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Enough","I can do that","Starting there"],"affirm":"You can't control relatives, but your alignment, boundaries and warmth are yours, and they're enough to start.","relearn":"Control what's yours, alignment, boundaries and warmth; that's enough to change the dynamic.","persona":"any","source":"what's yours"},
  {"id":"fm-074","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"After a tense family event, you and your partner feel raw and disconnected.","options":[{"text":"Debrief gently as a team: what worked, what you'd do differently","consequence":"You repair and get stronger for next time.","outcome":"repaired","best":true},{"text":"Blame each other for how it went","consequence":"Blaming each other turns the family's tension into your own."}],"debrief":"Debriefing kindly after family events repairs the couple and builds skill for next time.","relearn":"Debrief as a team after tense events; blame just imports the family's tension into the couple.","persona":"Karthik","source":"team debrief"},
  {"id":"fm-075","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match a tricky moment to the tool that fits it.","pairs":[{"left":"Unsolicited advice","right":"\"Thanks, we'll think it over.\""},{"left":"A surprise demand","right":"\"We'll decide together and tell you.\""},{"left":"A repeating nosy question","right":"One warm, repeatable line"},{"left":"A heated couple disagreement","right":"Settle it privately first"},{"left":"Signs of control or threats","right":"Reach 181 or a counsellor"}],"relearn":"Each moment has a tool: a warm deflect, the couple line, a repeatable line, private alignment, or a help route.","persona":"Reshma","source":"moment to tool"},
  {"id":"fm-076","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that won't sustain a lifelong family relationship.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Small, warm boundaries kept consistently","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"One huge confrontation to 'sort it all out'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Aligning as a couple again and again","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Going cold and silent for weeks at a time","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Assuming good intent where you can","trick":false}],"why":"One big blow-up and long cold silences rarely fix a lifelong relationship; consistent boundaries and alignment do.","relearn":"Sustainable family navigation is consistent small boundaries and alignment, not one big confrontation or going cold.","persona":"Sneha","source":"sustainable approach"},
  {"id":"fm-077","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you've mapped the web, learned the warm 'no', and the team line. The family map is yours now. Ready to use it?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Ready","It's mine now","Let's go"],"affirm":"With the web mapped, the warm no, the couple line and the help routes, you can navigate family with confidence.","relearn":"You hold the family map now: the web, the warm no, the couple line and help routes.","persona":"any","source":"the map is yours"},
  {"id":"fm-078","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"You want one principle to carry into every family situation from here.","options":[{"text":"Lead with warmth and clarity: honour them, protect us, get help if harmful","consequence":"You have a compass for the whole web.","outcome":"compass","best":true},{"text":"Try to please everyone, all the time, at any cost","consequence":"Pleasing everyone at any cost erases you and never ends."}],"debrief":"One principle carries the map: honour them, protect the couple, and get help if it turns harmful.","relearn":"Lead with warmth and clarity: honour them, protect us, get help if it turns harmful.","persona":"Pooja","source":"the one principle"},
  {"id":"fm-079","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"Your partner asks how you want to handle their family going forward. Set the tone as a team.","setup":"Say it as a team:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Let's stay warm with them, decide the big stuff together, and back each other every time.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's just deal with each thing as it blows up.\""}],"relearn":"Setting a shared tone, warm, aligned, mutually backed, beats lurching from blow-up to blow-up.","persona":"Karthik","source":"set the tone"},
  {"id":"fm-080","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two responses that drop your voice instead of keeping it.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Thank you, we'll weigh it and decide for ourselves.\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Obeying silently to avoid any friction","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Listening fully, then making your own call","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Saying a yes you don't mean to keep the peace","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"With respect, we see this differently.\"","trick":false}],"why":"Silent obedience and an unmeant yes drop your voice; thanking, listening and disagreeing kindly honour the elder and keep it.","relearn":"Honour the elder and keep your voice; silent obedience isn't the only respectful option.","persona":"Sneha","source":"honour and voice","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-081","type":"sort","persona":"Reshma","source":"couple or help","hook":"Sort: handle as a couple, or this needs outside help now?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Mismatched expectations about visits"},{"id":"b","text":"Threats to your safety"},{"id":"c","text":"Tense but ordinary disagreements"},{"id":"d","text":"Money demanded with intimidation"},{"id":"e","text":"Deciding how to split festival time"},{"id":"f","text":"Being cut off from your own family"}],"bins":[{"id":"couple","label":"Handle as a couple","valence":"pos"},{"id":"help","label":"Needs help now","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"couple","b":"help","c":"couple","d":"help","e":"couple","f":"help"},"relearn":"Visit mismatches, ordinary tension and festival timing are couple-level; threats, intimidating demands and isolation need help now.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-082","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful","type":"role-play","hook":"A relative hints that 'gifts' should keep coming from your family. You want to shut it down clearly.","setup":"Say it plainly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Dowry is illegal, and our families won't be doing that, let's leave it there.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Um, I'll ask them, maybe.\""}],"relearn":"Naming dowry as illegal and declining plainly shuts down the demand without leaving a door open.","persona":"Razia","source":"shut down dowry"},
  {"id":"fm-083","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a green-flag family habit to keep, or a pattern to change?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Talking issues through early and kindly"},{"id":"b","text":"Letting things fester silently"},{"id":"c","text":"Backing each other in the room"},{"id":"d","text":"Competing over whose family is 'right'"},{"id":"e","text":"Debriefing gently after a tense visit"},{"id":"f","text":"Keeping score of every past slight"}],"bins":[{"id":"keep","label":"Green-flag habit","valence":"pos"},{"id":"change","label":"Pattern to change","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"keep","b":"change","c":"keep","d":"change","e":"keep","f":"change"},"relearn":"Talking early, backing each other and debriefing are habits to keep; festering, family-vs-family scorekeeping and slight-counting need changing.","persona":"any","source":"keep or change"},
  {"id":"fm-084","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that slowly poison a lifelong family bond.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Repairing quickly after a clash","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Keeping score of every past slight","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Assuming good intent where you can","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Bringing up old grudges in every fight","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Saying sorry first when you've slipped","trick":false}],"why":"Scorekeeping and dragging up old grudges slowly poison the bond; quick repair and good-faith assumptions sustain it.","relearn":"Quick repair and good-faith assumptions sustain family bonds; keeping score and reviving old grudges erode them.","persona":"Pooja","source":"keep it healthy"},
  {"id":"fm-900","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If your mother and your wife clash, a good son backs his mother every time.\"","myth":{"un":"If your mother and your wife clash, a good son backs his mother every time.","re":"You're not picking a winner; you and your partner sort it as a team, then honour your mother kindly.","why":"Standing with your partner isn't disrespect to a parent."},"relearn":"You don't 'back' one over the other; the couple decides together, then honours the elder.","persona":"Karthik","source":"not a winner"},
  {"id":"fm-901","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Whatever the elders decide for the couple, the couple should just accept.\"","myth":{"un":"Whatever the elders decide for the couple, the couple should just accept.","re":"Elders' wishes are heard with respect, but the couple makes the final call on its own life together.","why":"The couple is the unit that lives with the decision."},"relearn":"Hear the elders, then the couple decides; respect doesn't mean handing over the final call.","persona":"any","source":"final call"},
  {"id":"fm-902","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A wife who backs her husband against his relatives is turning him against family.\"","myth":{"un":"A wife who backs her husband against his relatives is turning him against family.","re":"Backing your partner warmly in a tense room is being a team, not turning anyone against family.","why":"A united couple lowers conflict instead of stoking it."},"relearn":"Backing your partner is teamwork, not poisoning them against family.","persona":"any","source":"not poison"},
  {"id":"fm-903","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"It's fine to vent about your partner to your parents; they're family.\"","myth":{"un":"It's fine to vent about your partner to your parents; they're family.","re":"Routine venting to your parents hands them a one-sided story and quietly recruits them against your partner.","why":"Family then 'defends' you and the couple gets cornered."},"relearn":"Take couple problems to your partner first, not a running complaint to your parents.","persona":"Pooja","source":"venting recruits"},
  {"id":"fm-904","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A good daughter-in-law never disagrees with her husband in front of his family.\"","myth":{"un":"A good daughter-in-law should silently agree with whatever her husband says before his family.","re":"You can flag a disagreement gently in the room, or save it for later; silence isn't the only respectful option.","why":"A team has two voices, not one speaking for both."},"relearn":"You don't have to vanish your view in front of family; team it up, openly or later.","persona":"Pooja","source":"two voices"},
  {"id":"fm-905","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If relatives are around, a husband should let his wife handle them alone; it's her job.\"","myth":{"un":"If relatives are around, a husband should let his wife handle them alone; it's her job to manage his family.","re":"His family is a shared web you both joined; he stands beside her, he doesn't outsource the relatives to her.","why":"Both partners joined each other's families."},"relearn":"Managing his relatives isn't her solo job; he's beside her as a team.","persona":"Karthik","source":"not outsourced"},
  {"id":"fm-906","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Once you've decided something as a couple, you can still quietly undo it to please a relative.\"","myth":{"un":"Once you've decided something as a couple, you can still quietly undo it to please a relative.","re":"Quietly reversing a shared decision behind your partner's back breaks the trust the team runs on.","why":"A team needs the answer to stay the answer."},"relearn":"Don't secretly undo a joint decision to please family; reopen it together if needed.","persona":"any","source":"stays the answer"},
  {"id":"fm-907","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Letting your mother set the rules for your home keeps the peace.\"","myth":{"un":"Letting your mother set the rules for your home keeps the peace.","re":"The couple sets the rhythm of its own home; a peace built on handing that over breeds quiet resentment.","why":"Resentment is louder later than a kind boundary now."},"relearn":"The couple runs its own home; peace by surrender just stores up resentment.","persona":"Pooja","source":"own rhythm"},
  {"id":"fm-908","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A real man doesn't 'check with the wife'; he just decides.\"","myth":{"un":"A real man doesn't 'check with the wife' in front of family; he just decides on the spot.","re":"'Let us talk and get back to you' is strength, not weakness; deciding together is what a team does.","why":"Solo on-the-spot calls leave a partner exposed."},"relearn":"'We'll discuss and get back' is the strong move, not deciding alone to look decisive.","persona":"Karthik","source":"strong move"},
  {"id":"fm-909","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If your partner and your sister fall out, stay neutral and stay out of it.\"","myth":{"un":"If your partner and your sister fall out, the safest thing is to stay neutral and stay out of it.","re":"Silent 'neutrality' leaves your partner alone in the room; you can be fair to your sister and still stand with your partner.","why":"Fairness and teamwork aren't opposites."},"relearn":"Don't hide behind 'neutral'; back your partner while being fair to your sister.","persona":"Karthik","source":"not neutral"},
  {"id":"fm-910","cat":"couple-team","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Whoever's parents we're visiting, that partner gets to decide everything that week.\"","myth":{"un":"Whoever's parents we're visiting, that partner gets to decide everything that visit.","re":"You're a team in both houses; you still align as a couple even when you're guests in one side's home.","why":"Being on home turf doesn't dissolve the team."},"relearn":"Visiting one side's parents doesn't hand that partner solo control; you stay a team.","persona":"any","source":"both houses"},
  {"id":"fm-911","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Over chai, your father says your partner spends too much, hoping you'll grumble along.","options":[{"text":"Warmly close it: 'We manage our money together, Papa'","consequence":"Your father sees a solid couple and drops the wedge.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Grumble along to bond with your father","consequence":"It tells him he can keep chipping at your partner."}],"debrief":"Decline the wedge kindly; money is a couple matter, not a thing to bond over by complaining.","relearn":"Refuse the money wedge: close it warmly, keep the couple's finances the couple's.","persona":"Karthik","source":"money wedge"},
  {"id":"fm-912","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Relatives at a function demand on the spot when you two will 'finally' have a baby.","options":[{"text":"One united line: 'That's something we'll decide together, in our time'","consequence":"The couple stays the decider and the pressure has nowhere to go.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"You answer one way while your partner says another","consequence":"Two answers hand relatives a gap to push into."}],"debrief":"Kids are the couple's call; give one calm, shared answer rather than splitting.","relearn":"On having children, present one united answer; it's the couple's decision, not the room's.","persona":"any","source":"baby question"},
  {"id":"fm-913","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Your sister phones your partner directly to 'fix' a plan you two already agreed on.","options":[{"text":"Loop in together: 'Let's bring my partner in too, we decided this as a couple'","consequence":"The side-channel closes and the team stays intact.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Let your partner renegotiate it solo with your sister","consequence":"It reopens a settled decision behind your back."}],"debrief":"Close side-channels by looping in as a couple; don't renegotiate solo.","relearn":"Bring back-channel asks back to the couple together, rather than renegotiating solo.","persona":"any","source":"side channel"},
  {"id":"fm-914","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"At dinner your mother-in-law corrects your partner harshly; the table goes quiet, waiting on you.","options":[{"text":"Step in gently for your partner, then talk to her later","consequence":"Your partner isn't left alone and the elder keeps her dignity.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Stay quiet so you don't upset your mother-in-law","consequence":"It leaves your partner exposed and chips at trust."}],"debrief":"Back your partner in the room, handle the elder privately and kindly.","relearn":"Don't leave your partner alone under fire; back them now, address the elder kindly later.","persona":"any","source":"exposed at dinner"},
  {"id":"fm-915","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"A cousin pulls you aside with 'don't tell your partner, but...' and a juicy family complaint.","options":[{"text":"Decline: 'We don't keep these from each other, tell us both'","consequence":"You shut down a side-deal before it can split you.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Accept the secret to hear the gossip","consequence":"A 'don't tell your partner' secret is a wedge dressed as trust."}],"debrief":"'Don't tell your partner' is triangulation bait; keep no family secrets from your team.","relearn":"Refuse 'keep this from your partner' deals; the couple shares family matters, not hides them.","persona":"any","source":"dont tell"},
  {"id":"fm-916","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Your parents booked a big family trip and assume you'll both come; no one asked you two first.","options":[{"text":"Check in first: 'Let us look at our dates and confirm together'","consequence":"You answer as one and protect your own plans kindly.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Say yes instantly to avoid disappointing your parents","consequence":"A solo yes commits your partner to a plan they never saw."}],"debrief":"Pause to align as a couple before committing, rather than an auto-yes for them.","relearn":"Big plans go through the couple first: 'we'll check and confirm together', warmly.","persona":"Karthik","source":"booked trip"},
  {"id":"fm-917","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Mid-argument with your partner, your mother walks in and starts taking your side loudly.","options":[{"text":"Pause it: 'Thanks Ma, we'll sort this between us', and step away","consequence":"You keep the disagreement a couple matter and protect your partner.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Welcome your mother's backup to win the argument","consequence":"It turns a couple spat into a family front against your partner."}],"debrief":"Keep couple disagreements between the two of you, not a parent as reinforcement.","relearn":"Resolve couple conflicts privately; don't recruit a parent to outnumber your partner.","persona":"any","source":"reinforcement"},
  {"id":"fm-918","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Your in-laws want your salary handled 'the family way'; your partner looks at you, unsure.","options":[{"text":"Buy time: 'We'll talk about how we run our money and come back'","consequence":"The couple keeps its own money decisions and answers as one.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Agree on the spot so the in-laws are happy","consequence":"It hands over a couple decision just to keep the peace."}],"debrief":"How the couple runs its money is the couple's call; take it back to the team, kindly.","relearn":"Money systems are a couple decision; ask for time and decide together rather than surrender it.","persona":"Pooja","source":"salary the family way"},
  {"id":"fm-919","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"A relative keeps comparing your partner unfavourably to your bhabhi, watching for your reaction.","options":[{"text":"Warmly shut it: 'We're happy with how we do things, thanks'","consequence":"The comparison game stalls and your partner feels backed.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Half-agree to avoid seeming defensive","consequence":"It signals the relative can keep needling your partner."}],"debrief":"Decline comparison bait warmly; don't half-agree against your partner.","relearn":"Shut down 'compare to bhabhi' bait kindly; back your partner, don't trade insults.","persona":"any","source":"comparison bait"},
  {"id":"fm-920","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Two sets of parents want you both for the SAME festival day; each is calling you separately.","options":[{"text":"Decide together first, then each tells their parents the shared plan","consequence":"One agreed plan, delivered kindly to both sides, no tug-of-war.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Each of you just goes to your own parents this year","consequence":"Splitting on the day quietly says the couple comes second."}],"debrief":"Settle the clash as a couple, then both relay the same plan.","relearn":"Festival clashes: agree as a couple first, then each carries the shared answer to their parents.","persona":"any","source":"festival clash"},
  {"id":"fm-921","cat":"couple-team","type":"branch","hook":"Your father offers you money for a flat 'just between us, no need to tell your partner'.","options":[{"text":"Include your partner: 'That's so kind, Papa, let's all talk it through'","consequence":"A big commitment stays transparent and the couple decides as one.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Take it quietly and keep it from your partner","consequence":"A hidden money deal corrodes the couple's trust later."}],"debrief":"Big money decisions run through the couple openly, never as a hidden side-deal.","relearn":"Keep family money offers transparent; the couple decides together, not in secret.","persona":"Karthik","source":"flat money"},
  {"id":"fm-922","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each: a united-front move, or one that quietly undermines the couple?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Agreeing your answer privately before facing relatives"},{"id":"b","text":"Saying 'ask them, it's their fault' to relatives"},{"id":"c","text":"Backing your partner, debriefing later"},{"id":"d","text":"Promising a relative something behind their back"},{"id":"e","text":"Giving one calm answer together"},{"id":"f","text":"Letting family pit you two against each other"}],"bins":[{"id":"united","label":"United front","valence":"pos"},{"id":"undermine","label":"Undermines","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"united","b":"undermine","c":"united","d":"undermine","e":"united","f":"undermine"},"relearn":"Aligning, backing each other and one answer unite you; blame and secret deals undermine it.","persona":"any","source":"united or not 2"},
  {"id":"fm-923","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: which calls are the couple's own, and which are genuinely shared with elders?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Whether and when to have children"},{"id":"b","text":"Hosting the family's annual puja together"},{"id":"c","text":"How you two split money and chores"},{"id":"d","text":"Planning a big joint-family wedding"},{"id":"e","text":"Where the two of you live and work"},{"id":"f","text":"A shared ancestral-property arrangement"}],"bins":[{"id":"couple","label":"Couple's own call","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shared","label":"Share with elders","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"couple","b":"shared","c":"couple","d":"shared","e":"couple","f":"shared"},"relearn":"Kids, money/chores and where you live are the couple's; pujas, a joint wedding and shared property go with elders too.","persona":"Pooja","source":"team vs shared 2"},
  {"id":"fm-924","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each line: a team line that holds you together, or one that splits you?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"'We'll talk and get back to you together'"},{"id":"b","text":"'Honestly, blame, not me'"},{"id":"c","text":"'Let us decide this as a couple first'"},{"id":"d","text":"'Fine, whatever you all want is fine with me'"},{"id":"e","text":"'We're a team on this one'"},{"id":"f","text":"'Don't tell my partner, but I agree with you'"}],"bins":[{"id":"team","label":"Team line","valence":"pos"},{"id":"splits","label":"Splits the couple","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"team","b":"splits","c":"team","d":"splits","e":"team","f":"splits"},"relearn":"Lines that say 'we' and buy time keep the team; lines that blame your partner or cut a secret deal split you.","persona":"any","source":"team lines sort"},
  {"id":"fm-925","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a healthy way to handle a relative's complaint, or triangulation?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Bringing the complaint to your partner directly"},{"id":"b","text":"Agreeing with the relative behind their back"},{"id":"c","text":"Inviting you all to talk it out together"},{"id":"d","text":"Carrying secret messages between the sides"},{"id":"e","text":"Defending your partner kindly"},{"id":"f","text":"Letting the relative make you the go-between"}],"bins":[{"id":"healthy","label":"Healthy","valence":"pos"},{"id":"triangle","label":"Triangulation","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"healthy","b":"triangle","c":"healthy","d":"triangle","e":"healthy","f":"triangle"},"relearn":"Take complaints to your partner, talk openly, defend them; secret-siding and ferrying messages is triangulation.","persona":"any","source":"triangulation sort"},
  {"id":"fm-926","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a habit that keeps the couple solid in a big family, or one that wears it down?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A quick check-in before family events"},{"id":"b","text":"Springing surprise commitments on your partner"},{"id":"c","text":"Debriefing kindly after a tense visit"},{"id":"d","text":"Keeping a tally of who 'won' each clash"},{"id":"e","text":"Repeating one steady team line under pressure"},{"id":"f","text":"Going silent and stewing after a fight"}],"bins":[{"id":"keeps","label":"Keeps you solid","valence":"pos"},{"id":"wears","label":"Wears it down","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"keeps","b":"wears","c":"keeps","d":"wears","e":"keeps","f":"wears"},"relearn":"Check-ins, debriefs and a steady line keep you solid; ambushes, scorekeeping and silent stewing wear it down.","persona":"Karthik","source":"habits sort"},
  {"id":"fm-927","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: who hears it first when a family issue lands, partner or relative?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"You're upset by something your in-laws said"},{"id":"b","text":"Your aunt asks you to relay a complaint"},{"id":"c","text":"A big spending request from your parents"},{"id":"d","text":"Your cousin wants a secret about your partner"},{"id":"e","text":"A clash you feel about a ritual"},{"id":"f","text":"A relative baiting you to side against them"}],"bins":[{"id":"partner","label":"Partner first","valence":"pos"},{"id":"decline","label":"Decline / loop in","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"partner","b":"decline","c":"partner","d":"decline","e":"partner","f":"decline"},"relearn":"Hurt, big asks and ritual clashes go to your partner first; relayed complaints, secrets and side bait you decline.","persona":"Pooja","source":"who first sort"},
  {"id":"fm-928","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a kind united front, or a cold wall pretending to be one?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"'We've decided together, and we'd love your blessing'"},{"id":"b","text":"Stonewalling relatives with icy silence"},{"id":"c","text":"Holding the decision warmly, explaining once"},{"id":"d","text":"'Our way or we don't come at all'"},{"id":"e","text":"Honouring the elders while keeping your call"},{"id":"f","text":"Cutting off anyone who disagrees by default"}],"bins":[{"id":"kind","label":"Kind united front","valence":"pos"},{"id":"wall","label":"Cold wall","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"kind","b":"wall","c":"kind","d":"wall","e":"kind","f":"wall"},"relearn":"A united front holds the decision warmly and seeks blessing; icy silence, ultimatums and cutting people off are a cold wall.","persona":"any","source":"front vs wall"},
  {"id":"fm-929","cat":"couple-team","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each phone moment: as a couple, or react alone?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Saying 'let me check with my partner too' before agreeing"},{"id":"b","text":"Committing you both before asking your partner"},{"id":"c","text":"Telling a relative you'll both reply tomorrow"},{"id":"d","text":"Promising a yes to end the call fast"},{"id":"e","text":"Telling your partner about the call right after"},{"id":"f","text":"Hiding that the relative even called"}],"bins":[{"id":"couple","label":"As a couple","valence":"pos"},{"id":"alone","label":"React alone","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"couple","b":"alone","c":"couple","d":"alone","e":"couple","f":"alone"},"relearn":"Checking in, buying time and telling your partner keep calls shared; committing both or hiding the call cut them out.","persona":"any","source":"phone sort"},
  {"id":"fm-930","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each family-pressure moment to the couple-team response.","pairs":[{"left":"Relatives push a big decision on the spot","right":"'We'll talk and get back to you'"},{"left":"One partner is singled out at the table","right":"The other steps in to back them"},{"left":"Two families' plans clash on a date","right":"The couple agrees its own plan"},{"left":"A relative shares a 'don't tell' secret","right":"You decline, keeping no side-deals"},{"left":"Your parent vents about your partner","right":"You warmly close the wedge"}],"relearn":"The couple-team response: align, back each other, decline secrets, give one united answer.","persona":"any","source":"team responses 2"},
  {"id":"fm-931","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each couple-team signal to what it tells a partner.","pairs":[{"left":"A heads-up before a visit","right":"No ambush in the room"},{"left":"Sitting beside, not across","right":"We face family together"},{"left":"Saying 'we', not 'I'","right":"Decisions are ours"},{"left":"Defending them when absent","right":"Loyalty out of earshot"},{"left":"Naming their wins upward","right":"Proud of this team"}],"relearn":"Heads-ups, sitting together, saying 'we', defending them when absent and praising them upward are small signals that a partner isn't alone.","persona":"any","source":"team signals"},
  {"id":"fm-932","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each undermining move to the trust it damages.","pairs":[{"left":"Blaming your partner to relatives","right":"Their safety to be open with you"},{"left":"A secret deal behind their back","right":"Honesty the team runs on"},{"left":"Leaving them alone under fire","right":"The feeling you've got each other"},{"left":"Carrying messages between sides","right":"Being a couple, not a go-between"},{"left":"Auto-siding with your parents","right":"That the couple decides first"}],"relearn":"Blame, secrets, abandonment, message-carrying and parents-first each damage a specific thread of couple trust.","persona":"any","source":"undermine match"},
  {"id":"fm-933","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each tricky line a relative might say to a calm couple-team reply.","pairs":[{"left":"'Don't you agree your partner's too modern?'","right":"'I love that about them, actually'"},{"left":"'Decide right now, we can't wait'","right":"'We'll discuss and get back to you'"},{"left":"'Just keep this between us, beta'","right":"'We don't keep things from each other'"},{"left":"'Your bhabhi would never do that'","right":"'We're happy with our own way'"},{"left":"'Side with your own family, na'","right":"'We're a team; we'll sort it'"}],"relearn":"Each pressure line has a warm, united reply that backs your partner without a fight.","persona":"any","source":"reply match"},
  {"id":"fm-934","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each couple check-in question to what it sorts out before a family visit.","pairs":[{"left":"'What's the one thing we won't budge on?'","right":"Your shared non-negotiable"},{"left":"'What can we be flexible about?'","right":"Where you can happily give"},{"left":"'What's our line if they push kids?'","right":"A ready answer to the question"},{"left":"'Who steps in if one of us is cornered?'","right":"A plan to back each other"},{"left":"'When do we step out to regroup?'","right":"An exit to realign mid-visit"}],"relearn":"A quick pre-visit check-in sorts your non-negotiable, your flex and how you'll back each other.","persona":"Karthik","source":"checkin match"},
  {"id":"fm-935","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each scenario to whether it's the couple's call or a genuinely shared family decision.","pairs":[{"left":"When you two have children","right":"The couple decides, in its own time"},{"left":"Hosting the family's annual puja","right":"Planned together with the elders"},{"left":"How you split your salaries","right":"The couple's own money call"},{"left":"Planning a joint-family wedding","right":"Shared across both families"},{"left":"Where the two of you live","right":"Yours as a couple to decide"}],"relearn":"Kids, money and where you live are the couple's; pujas and joint weddings are shared with elders.","persona":"Pooja","source":"call match"},
  {"id":"fm-936","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each tense moment to the team move that defuses it.","pairs":[{"left":"A surprise demand at a function","right":"'We'll get back to you' together"},{"left":"A relative running your partner down","right":"A warm, firm defence"},{"left":"Being pulled into a secret","right":"Declining the side-deal"},{"left":"A clash blowing up at the table","right":"Stepping out to regroup privately"},{"left":"Both parents wanting the same day","right":"One agreed plan from the couple"}],"relearn":"Buy time, defend warmly, decline secrets, step out to regroup, and bring one agreed plan; each defuses a different squeeze.","persona":"any","source":"defuse match"},
  {"id":"fm-937","cat":"couple-team","type":"match","hook":"Match each 'choosing sides' worry to why standing as a team isn't that.","pairs":[{"left":"'Backing my wife betrays my mother'","right":"You can honour both at once"},{"left":"'A united front feels cold'","right":"It's warm; you still seek blessing"},{"left":"'Deciding together cuts elders out'","right":"You still hear their advice"},{"left":"'Defending my partner starts a war'","right":"It actually lowers the conflict"},{"left":"'Saying we'll decide later is rude'","right":"It's the kindest, steadiest reply"}],"relearn":"Standing as a team honours elders, stays warm, hears advice and lowers conflict; it isn't 'choosing sides'.","persona":"Karthik","source":"sides worry match"},
  {"id":"fm-938","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: deciding the big things together first, before looping anyone else in, is how a couple stays a team. Land for you?","prompt":"What's your read?","options":["Lands for me","Decide together first","Then loop family in"],"affirm":"Settling the major calls as a pair before involving relatives keeps the partnership steady and clear.","relearn":"A couple decides the big things together first, then loops family in; that order keeps the team strong.","persona":"any","source":"decide together first"},
  {"id":"fm-939","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: 'we'll decide together and let you know' might be the handiest line in a joint family. Worth memorising?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Worth it","I'll memorise it","So useful"],"affirm":"'We'll decide together and let you know' protects the couple-team kindly in almost any family pressure.","relearn":"One sentence carries the couple-team: 'we'll decide together and let you know.'","persona":"any","source":"useful sentence 2"},
  {"id":"fm-940","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: deciding privately, then giving family one calm answer, saves you both a hundred small fights. Notice that?","prompt":"How does that land?","options":["I notice it","Saves the fights","One calm answer"],"affirm":"Aligning in private and offering one calm answer spares the couple repeated public clashes.","relearn":"Decide privately, then present one calm answer; it heads off the small public fights.","persona":"any","source":"private then calm"},
  {"id":"fm-941","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: backing your partner in the room and being kind to your family aren't opposites. Ever felt forced to pick?","prompt":"Sit with it.","options":["Felt that pull","They aren't opposites","I can do both"],"affirm":"You can back your partner warmly and still honour your family; it was never a real either-or.","relearn":"Backing your partner and honouring family can both be true at once; it isn't either-or.","persona":"any","source":"not opposites"},
  {"id":"fm-942","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: refusing to carry secret messages between your partner and your family is a quiet act of loyalty. Agree?","prompt":"What comes up?","options":["I agree","Quiet loyalty","No more go-between"],"affirm":"Declining to be the family go-between keeps you a couple, not a messenger pulled both ways.","relearn":"Refusing to ferry secret messages keeps the couple a team instead of a divided go-between.","persona":"any","source":"go between reflect"},
  {"id":"fm-943","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a quick check-in before a family visit, even two minutes, can change the whole evening. Try it?","prompt":"Worth a try?","options":["I'll try it","Two minutes","Changes the evening"],"affirm":"A short pre-visit check-in aligns you both, so family pressure meets one steady couple, not a gap.","relearn":"A two-minute check-in before a visit aligns the couple and steadies the whole evening.","persona":"Karthik","source":"checkin reflect"},
  {"id":"fm-944","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: when family pressure rises, stepping out together to regroup isn't weakness, it's teamwork. Ring true?","prompt":"Does it ring true?","options":["Rings true","Regroup together","Not weakness"],"affirm":"Stepping out to regroup mid-pressure lets the couple realign and return as one, calm team.","relearn":"Stepping out together to regroup under pressure is a team move, not running away.","persona":"any","source":"regroup reflect"},
  {"id":"fm-945","cat":"couple-team","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: never making your partner choose publicly between you and their parents is its own kind of gift. Notice it?","prompt":"How does that sit?","options":["I notice it","It's a gift","No public choosing"],"affirm":"Not forcing a public choice between you and their parents spares your partner an impossible bind.","relearn":"Don't make your partner publicly choose between you and their parents; spare them that bind.","persona":"any","source":"no public choosing"},
  {"id":"fm-946","cat":"couple-team","type":"role-play","hook":"An aunt corners you alone to ask you to 'talk sense into' your wife about her job. You want to close the wedge gently.","setup":"Reply gently:","yourLine":[{"text":"'Her job's something we already decided together, auntie — I'm glad she has it.'","best":true},{"text":"'I'll see what I can do.'"}],"relearn":"Declining to be recruited against your partner, and naming that you decided together, shuts a wedge before it opens.","persona":"Karthik","source":"don't be recruited"},
  {"id":"fm-947","cat":"couple-team","type":"role-play","hook":"Relatives at a function want a yes about a plan right now. You and your partner haven't talked it over.","setup":"You say:","yourLine":[{"text":"'Let us talk it through and we'll get back to you together.'","best":true},{"text":"'Sure, fine, whatever you all think is best.'"}],"relearn":"'We'll talk and get back to you together' buys the couple time to decide as one team.","persona":"Karthik","source":"buy time line"},
  {"id":"fm-948","cat":"couple-team","type":"role-play","hook":"Your father is venting to you about your partner, clearly hoping you'll grumble along and take his side.","setup":"You reply, kindly:","yourLine":[{"text":"'I hear you, Papa, but we sort our own things out together; we're good.'","best":true},{"text":"'Yeah, honestly they do annoy me too sometimes.'"}],"relearn":"Decline to grumble along; a warm 'we sort it together' refuses the wedge without snubbing your father.","persona":"Karthik","source":"decline grumble"},
  {"id":"fm-949","cat":"couple-team","type":"role-play","hook":"A relative pulls you aside: 'Don't tell your partner, but I need you to do something quietly for the family.'","setup":"You answer:","yourLine":[{"text":"'We don't really keep things from each other, so let's all talk about it.'","best":true},{"text":"'Okay, I won't say anything, tell me.'"}],"relearn":"Refuse the 'don't tell your partner' secret; bringing it into the open keeps the couple a team.","persona":"any","source":"refuse secret line"},
  {"id":"fm-950","cat":"couple-team","type":"role-play","hook":"Your mother-in-law has just corrected your partner sharply at the table and everyone's gone quiet, looking at you.","setup":"You step in, gently:","yourLine":[{"text":"'We've actually talked about this and we're happy with how we do it.'","best":true},{"text":"(You say nothing and look at your plate.)"}],"relearn":"A gentle 'we're happy with how we do it' backs your partner without disrespecting the elder.","persona":"any","source":"step in line"},
  {"id":"fm-951","cat":"couple-team","type":"role-play","hook":"Both your parents and your in-laws are calling about the same festival day, each expecting you both.","setup":"You tell each side:","yourLine":[{"text":"'We're working out our plan as a couple and we'll confirm with everyone soon.'","best":true},{"text":"'Don't worry, I'll just come to you, we'll figure the rest out.'"}],"relearn":"One shared line to both sides keeps the couple deciding together, not split across two homes.","persona":"any","source":"festival line"},
  {"id":"fm-952","cat":"couple-team","type":"role-play","hook":"In front of the whole family, your partner says something you disagree with and everyone turns to you.","setup":"You say:","yourLine":[{"text":"'We see it a little differently; we'll talk it through and let you know.'","best":true},{"text":"'No, they've got it wrong, that's not what we agreed.'"}],"relearn":"Flag the difference gently and take it private; don't contradict your partner in front of family.","persona":"any","source":"disagree in room line"},
  {"id":"fm-952b","cat":"couple-team","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that quietly split the couple under family pressure.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Checking in privately before answering relatives","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Letting relatives split you with flattery","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Backing each other in the room","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Blaming your partner to win the family over","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Giving one calm, shared answer","trick":false}],"why":"Letting flattery split you and blaming your partner break the team; checking in, backing each other and a shared answer keep it.","relearn":"Stay a team: align privately and back each other; don't let flattery split you or blame your partner.","persona":"Sneha","source":"stay a team 2"},
  {"id":"fm-953","cat":"couple-team","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that triangulate the couple (a relative trying to split you).","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'Let's all sit and talk this out together'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'Don't tell your partner I said this, but...'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'We decided this as a couple, here's our plan'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'Just agree with me, we'll handle them later'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'I'll bring this up with both of you'","trick":false}],"why":"Asking you to keep a secret and to side against your partner are triangulation; open talk isn't.","relearn":"Triangulation: 'don't tell your partner' and 'side against them' are the wedge; open talk isn't.","persona":"any","source":"spot triangulation"},
  {"id":"fm-954","cat":"couple-team","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two replies that leave your partner exposed in front of the family.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'We're a team on this; we'll decide together'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'Honestly, that one's not my fault'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'Let's step out a moment and talk'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"(Silence, while a relative scolds your partner)","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'We've thought about it and we're happy'","trick":false}],"why":"Blaming your partner and staying silent while they're scolded both abandon them; teaming up and a shared answer back them.","relearn":"Don't expose your partner: blaming them or going silent under fire leaves them alone.","persona":"any","source":"spot exposed"},
  {"id":"fm-955","cat":"couple-team","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that hide a family matter from your own partner.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Telling your partner about the call right after","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Making a money promise behind their back","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Bringing a complaint to your partner directly","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Keeping a 'family-only' secret deal from them","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Looping your partner in on a tricky request","trick":false}],"why":"A secret money promise and a hidden 'family-only' deal keep your partner in the dark; telling and looping in keep it honest.","relearn":"Keep no family matter hidden; secret promises and 'family-only' deals erode the team.","persona":"any","source":"spot hidden"},
  {"id":"fm-956","cat":"couple-team","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two 'united front' moves that are actually a cold wall, not teamwork.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'We've decided together, and we'd love your blessing'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Freezing relatives out with icy silence","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Holding your decision warmly, explaining once","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'Our way or we just won't come at all'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Honouring the elders while keeping your call","trick":false}],"why":"Icy silence and an ultimatum are a cold wall that shuts family out; a warm decision and honouring elders are a real front.","relearn":"A united front stays warm and seeks blessing; silence and ultimatums are a wall.","persona":"any","source":"spot wall"},
  {"id":"fm-957","cat":"couple-team","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two phone-call moves that cut your partner out of a decision.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'Let me check with my partner too before I say yes'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Committing you both before asking them","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'We'll both reply to you tomorrow'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Hiding that the relative even called","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Telling your partner about the call right after","trick":false}],"why":"Committing both of you and hiding the call shut your partner out; checking first and telling them keep it a couple decision.","relearn":"Don't commit your partner or hide a call; check in and tell them, so decisions stay shared.","persona":"any","source":"spot phone"},
  {"id":"fm-958","cat":"couple-team","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two things you say to your parents that recruit them against your partner.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'We had a small disagreement; we're sorting it'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'You won't believe what they did this time'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'We're good, just figuring out our routine'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'You were right about them all along'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'We'll handle it between us'","trick":false}],"why":"Gossiping about your partner and 'you were right about them' enlist family against them; calm, contained updates don't.","relearn":"Don't recruit your parents against your partner; keep couple problems between you.","persona":"Pooja","source":"spot recruit"},
  {"id":"fm-990","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“A good bahu adjusts to everything; she never has a need of her own.”","myth":{"un":"A good bahu adjusts to everything; she never has a need of her own.","re":"Adjusting goes both ways, and having needs doesn't make you a bad bahu — it makes you a person.","why":"A home runs on mutual give-and-take, not one person erasing herself."},"relearn":"Adjusting goes both ways; having a need of your own doesn't make you a bad bahu.","persona":"Pooja","source":"never erasing"},
  {"id":"fm-991","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“If you set a limit with your parents, you're a disloyal son.”","myth":{"un":"If you set a limit with your parents, you're a disloyal son.","re":"Loyalty isn't doing everything they say; you can love and honour them and still hold a couple's limit.","why":"Honour and a clear limit live together; obedience isn't the test of love."},"relearn":"Loyalty isn't blind obedience; you can honour your parents and still hold a limit.","persona":"Karthik","source":"loyal not obedient"},
  {"id":"fm-992","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“If you keep any privacy from in-laws, you must be hiding something.”","myth":{"un":"If you keep any privacy from in-laws, you must be hiding something.","re":"A couple needing some private space is normal and healthy — privacy isn't secrecy or guilt.","why":"Closeness doesn't mean zero walls; every couple needs a little room of its own."},"relearn":"Privacy isn't secrecy; a couple needing some space of its own is normal and healthy.","persona":"Pooja","source":"space not secrecy"},
  {"id":"fm-993","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“Saying no to a relative once means they'll cut you off forever.”","myth":{"un":"Saying no to a relative once means they'll cut you off forever.","re":"A kind, occasional no rarely ends a real bond; most relationships absorb a respectful limit.","why":"Strong bonds survive a no; if one no ends everything, the bond was already strained."},"relearn":"A kind no rarely ends a real bond; most relationships hold a respectful limit fine.","persona":"Sneha","source":"no won't end it"},
  {"id":"fm-994","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“Keeping the peace means agreeing to everything elders ask.”","myth":{"un":"Keeping the peace means agreeing to everything elders ask.","re":"Real peace is honest, not silent; agreeing to everything just stores up resentment for later.","why":"Swallowed nos pile into bitterness; a kind limit now keeps the peace real."},"relearn":"Peace isn't silent agreement; swallowed nos turn into resentment later.","persona":"Pooja","source":"real peace"},
  {"id":"fm-995","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“A boundary should be dropped on people firmly, the harder the better.”","myth":{"un":"A boundary should be dropped on people firmly, the harder the better.","re":"A boundary lands best warm and clear — softness in tone, firmness in the line, not a slammed door.","why":"Warmth carries the limit further than harshness; you can be kind and still unmovable."},"relearn":"A boundary works best warm and clear, not harsh; firm line, kind tone.","persona":"Karthik","source":"warm and firm"},
  {"id":"fm-996","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“Once you set a boundary, you've handled it; it never needs repeating.”","myth":{"un":"Once you set a boundary, you've handled it; it never needs repeating.","re":"Boundaries get tested and need re-stating gently over time — that's upkeep, not failure.","why":"People forget and push again; a calm repeat is normal maintenance, not a defeat."},"relearn":"Boundaries need gentle re-stating over time; repeating one isn't failure, it's upkeep.","persona":"Pooja","source":"upkeep not failure"},
  {"id":"fm-997","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“If you don't pick up every call instantly, you don't love your family.”","myth":{"un":"If you don't pick up every call instantly, you don't love your family.","re":"Love isn't measured in instant availability; you can answer when you can and still care deeply.","why":"Constant availability burns you out; caring runs deeper than a ringtone."},"relearn":"Love isn't instant availability; you can call back when you can and still care deeply.","persona":"Sneha","source":"not a ringtone"},
  {"id":"fm-998","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“How you and your partner spend your own salary is the whole family's business.”","myth":{"un":"How you and your partner spend your own salary is the whole family's business.","re":"Your earnings are the couple's call; sharing generously is a choice, not an owed obligation.","why":"Generosity given freely is kindness; generosity demanded isn't a budget, it's pressure."},"relearn":"Your salary is the couple's call; you can give generously by choice, not by demand.","persona":"Pooja","source":"your call"},
  {"id":"fm-999","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“A boundary is a wall that shuts people out of your life.”","myth":{"un":"A boundary is a wall that shuts people out of your life.","re":"A boundary limits one behaviour while keeping the door open — it's a fence with a gate, not a wall.","why":"Walls end relationships; gates let love in while holding the line on what hurt."},"relearn":"A boundary is a gate, not a wall; it limits a behaviour without shutting the person out.","persona":"Pooja","source":"gate not wall"},
  {"id":"fm-1000","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“Whoever shouts loudest in the house gets to decide for the couple.”","myth":{"un":"Whoever shouts loudest in the house gets to decide for the couple.","re":"Volume isn't authority; the couple's life is theirs to decide, calmly, no matter who's loudest.","why":"A raised voice is pressure, not a verdict; you can stay calm and still keep your decision."},"relearn":"Volume isn't authority; the couple's decision stands calmly, however loud the room gets.","persona":"Karthik","source":"calm decides"},
  {"id":"fm-1001","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“Letting in-laws decide your festival visits avoids all conflict.”","myth":{"un":"Letting in-laws decide your festival visits avoids all conflict.","re":"Handing over every choice doesn't end conflict — it just hides your needs until they overflow.","why":"Buried needs resurface as resentment; a shared plan beats silent self-erasing."},"relearn":"Handing over every choice doesn't end conflict; it hides needs until they overflow.","persona":"Pooja","source":"plan not erase"},
  {"id":"fm-1002","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“If a limit upsets a relative even a little, you set it wrong.”","myth":{"un":"If a limit upsets a relative even a little, you set it wrong.","re":"A kind limit can still land as a small disappointment — that's allowed; their feelings aren't your fault.","why":"You can't control someone's reaction, only your kindness; mild upset isn't proof of cruelty."},"relearn":"A kind limit can still mildly disappoint; their reaction isn't proof you did it wrong.","persona":"Sneha","source":"mild upset is ok"},
  {"id":"fm-1003","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“A boundary set 'for now' isn't real; only a forever rule counts.”","myth":{"un":"A boundary set 'for now' isn't real; only a forever rule counts.","re":"Boundaries can flex with the season of life — a 'just for now' limit is real and completely valid.","why":"Needs change with newborns, jobs, health; a temporary limit is honest, not weak."},"relearn":"A boundary can be 'just for now' and still be real; limits flex with the season of life.","persona":"Pooja","source":"for-now is real"},
  {"id":"fm-1004","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"“Telling family your plan in advance is rude; just surprise them.”","myth":{"un":"Telling family your plan in advance is rude; just surprise them.","re":"A warm heads-up before a decision or visit is the kind move — it gives people time, not offence.","why":"Surprises breed friction; a little notice honours the relationship and lowers conflict."},"relearn":"A warm heads-up before plans isn't rude; it gives people time and lowers conflict.","persona":"Karthik","source":"heads-up is kind"},
  {"id":"fm-1005","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a kind way to hold a limit, or a cold cut-off that just shuts people out?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“We'd love a call before you drop by.”"},{"id":"b","text":"Ignoring every message for a month"},{"id":"c","text":"“We'll decide on the baby ourselves, with love.”"},{"id":"d","text":"Blocking them after one argument"},{"id":"e","text":"“Join us Sunday; weekdays we need our own time.”"},{"id":"f","text":"Cold silence so they 'get the hint'"}],"bins":[{"id":"kind","label":"Kind limit","valence":"pos"},{"id":"cold","label":"Cold cut-off","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"kind","b":"cold","c":"kind","d":"cold","e":"kind","f":"cold"},"relearn":"A kind limit names the line warmly and keeps the door open; silence and blocking are cut-offs, not boundaries.","persona":"Pooja","source":"kind vs cut-off"},
  {"id":"fm-1006","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: clearly the couple's own call, or genuinely a shared family decision?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"How you raise your own children"},{"id":"b","text":"Whose home the wedding rituals happen in"},{"id":"c","text":"What you do with your own salary"},{"id":"d","text":"A festival the whole joint family hosts"},{"id":"e","text":"Which city you two live and work in"},{"id":"f","text":"Planning a shared family pilgrimage"}],"bins":[{"id":"couple","label":"Couple's call","valence":"neutral"},{"id":"shared","label":"Shared family call","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"couple","b":"shared","c":"couple","d":"shared","e":"couple","f":"shared"},"relearn":"Your kids, salary and where you live are the couple's call; genuinely shared rituals are decided together.","persona":"any","source":"whose call"},
  {"id":"fm-1007","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: 'received the love, kept the limit', or just swallowed the overreach?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“Thanks Aunty, we've got the plan sorted ourselves.”"},{"id":"b","text":"Cancelling your trip because she frowned"},{"id":"c","text":"“Love your concern; this one's ours to decide.”"},{"id":"d","text":"Agreeing just so she'd stop pushing"},{"id":"e","text":"“We'll take your advice on board and choose together.”"},{"id":"f","text":"Saying yes while quietly seething"}],"bins":[{"id":"kept","label":"Kept the limit","valence":"pos"},{"id":"swallowed","label":"Swallowed it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"kept","b":"swallowed","c":"kept","d":"swallowed","e":"kept","f":"swallowed"},"relearn":"You can receive concern warmly and still hold the line; caving buries resentment.","persona":"Sneha","source":"love and limit"},
  {"id":"fm-1008","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a warm, clear way to say it, or a harsh version of the very same limit?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“We'd love a heads-up before visits.”"},{"id":"b","text":"“Stop barging in.”"},{"id":"c","text":"“We'll ask when we want advice on this.”"},{"id":"d","text":"“Mind your own business.”"},{"id":"e","text":"“This one's ours, and we love you.”"},{"id":"f","text":"“Stay out of our lives.”"}],"bins":[{"id":"warm","label":"Warm and clear","valence":"pos"},{"id":"harsh","label":"Harsh version","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"warm","b":"harsh","c":"warm","d":"harsh","e":"warm","f":"harsh"},"relearn":"The same limit can be said with warmth and clarity; harsh phrasing wounds without making the line any firmer.","persona":"Pooja","source":"warm vs harsh"},
  {"id":"fm-1009","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: holding a limit kindly under pressure, or caving to end the discomfort?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“We hear you; we'll decide together and tell you.”"},{"id":"b","text":"Saying yes just so the call ends"},{"id":"c","text":"“Give us a week to think, then we'll share.”"},{"id":"d","text":"Agreeing on the spot to stop the frown"},{"id":"e","text":"“We love you, and this stays our choice.”"},{"id":"f","text":"Folding the moment voices get raised"}],"bins":[{"id":"held","label":"Held kindly","valence":"pos"},{"id":"caved","label":"Caved to comfort","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"held","b":"caved","c":"held","d":"caved","e":"held","f":"caved"},"relearn":"You can buy time and hold the line warmly; caving to stop the discomfort trades your real choice for a moment's quiet.","persona":"Karthik","source":"held vs caved"},
  {"id":"fm-1010","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a boundary that still includes family, or one that walls them out?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“Come for dinner Sunday; we'll plan the rest.”"},{"id":"b","text":"Skipping every event out of spite"},{"id":"c","text":"“We'd love your recipes; cooked our way.”"},{"id":"d","text":"Refusing all contact over a slight"},{"id":"e","text":"“Visit anytime, just call ahead.”"},{"id":"f","text":"Going silent for months to make a point"}],"bins":[{"id":"includes","label":"Still includes them","valence":"pos"},{"id":"walls","label":"Needless wall","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"includes","b":"walls","c":"includes","d":"walls","e":"includes","f":"walls"},"relearn":"A kind boundary keeps people close; spite and total silence wall them out.","persona":"Pooja","source":"include not wall"},
  {"id":"fm-1011","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a respectful 'no' you can actually say, or a needlessly harsh refusal?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“Not this time, but thank you for thinking of us.”"},{"id":"b","text":"“Why do you always ask such things?”"},{"id":"c","text":"“We'd rather not, and we really appreciate the offer.”"},{"id":"d","text":"“Stop wasting our time with this.”"},{"id":"e","text":"“We've decided differently; we hope you understand.”"},{"id":"f","text":"“You never listen anyway, so no.”"}],"bins":[{"id":"respect","label":"Respectful no","valence":"pos"},{"id":"harsh","label":"Harsh refusal","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"respect","b":"harsh","c":"respect","d":"harsh","e":"respect","f":"harsh"},"relearn":"A respectful no declines the ask but honours the person; harsh refusals attack the person.","persona":"any","source":"kind no"},
  {"id":"fm-1012","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a healthy couple-boundary, or control dressed up as one?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“We'll plan visits together, fairly.”"},{"id":"b","text":"“You can't see your own parents.”"},{"id":"c","text":"“Let's handle money as a team.”"},{"id":"d","text":"“Hand me your phone to check.”"},{"id":"e","text":"“We'll share news when ready.”"},{"id":"f","text":"“You need my okay to go out.”"}],"bins":[{"id":"healthy","label":"Healthy limit","valence":"pos"},{"id":"control","label":"Control, not a limit","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"healthy","b":"control","c":"healthy","d":"control","e":"healthy","f":"control"},"relearn":"A boundary protects the couple; cutting off family, phone-checks and permission-to-leave are control.","persona":"Karthik","source":"limit vs control"},
  {"id":"fm-1013","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Your mother-in-law reorganises your cupboards while you're at work, every week.","options":[{"text":"Thank her warmly, then agree a gentle line: “I love the help; let me keep my own space my way.”","consequence":"She feels appreciated and you keep your space without a fight.","best":true,"outcome":"bounded"},{"text":"Snap that she should stop touching your things","consequence":"A sharp rebuke wounds her and hardens the conflict."}],"debrief":"Appreciate the care, then name the limit warmly; welcome help and still keep your space.","relearn":"Welcome the help, keep your space: thank her, then name the line kindly.","persona":"Pooja","source":"cupboard line"},
  {"id":"fm-1014","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Relatives keep asking when you two will have a baby, at every gathering.","options":[{"text":"Use a calm, repeatable line together: “We'll share happy news when there is some.”","consequence":"You deflect the pressure kindly and don't owe anyone an explanation.","best":true,"outcome":"held"},{"text":"Get visibly angry and storm off each time","consequence":"Storming off makes you the gossip and invites more."}],"debrief":"A warm, repeatable line closes the topic; your family timeline is the couple's own.","relearn":"Deflect baby pressure with one calm line; the timeline is yours.","persona":"Karthik","source":"baby pressure"},
  {"id":"fm-1015","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Your in-laws want to keep a key to your flat and let themselves in anytime.","options":[{"text":"Say it kindly together: “We love you visiting; we'd just like a call first so we're ready.”","consequence":"You get privacy and they still feel welcome and trusted.","best":true,"outcome":"bounded"},{"text":"Hand over the key to avoid any awkwardness","consequence":"Giving in erases your privacy and the resentment leaks out later."}],"debrief":"Asking for a heads-up isn't rejection; it protects the couple's space while keeping the welcome warm.","relearn":"A call before visits protects your space without shutting anyone out.","persona":"Pooja","source":"the key"},
  {"id":"fm-1016","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"A relative keeps phoning your partner to complain about you behind your back.","options":[{"text":"Gently redirect: “If something's bothering you, let's all talk together, kindly.”","consequence":"You refuse the back-channel and the couple stays a team.","best":true,"outcome":"bounded"},{"text":"Let it slide and quietly distrust both","consequence":"Silence lets the side-channel grow and poisons trust."}],"debrief":"Triangulation thrives in private complaints; an open, kind talk shuts the back-channel down.","relearn":"Refuse the back-channel: invite an open, kind talk instead.","persona":"Karthik","source":"back-channel"},
  {"id":"fm-1017","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Your father-in-law gives unasked advice on your job and how you should quit it.","options":[{"text":"Honour him, hold your choice: “I value your view, Papa; this career call is mine to make.”","consequence":"You respect him and keep your own decision intact.","best":true,"outcome":"held"},{"text":"Quit just to avoid disappointing him","consequence":"Surrendering a life choice to dodge guilt erodes your voice."}],"debrief":"You can listen warmly to an elder and still decide your own work; respect isn't obedience.","relearn":"Honour the advice, keep the choice: respect listens, it doesn't surrender your career.","persona":"Pooja","source":"job advice"},
  {"id":"fm-1018","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Your mother expects you both at her place every single weekend, no exceptions.","options":[{"text":"Offer a fair rhythm together: “We'll come two Sundays a month, and host you too.”","consequence":"You stay close and connected while keeping some weekends your own.","best":true,"outcome":"balanced"},{"text":"Show up every weekend, exhausted and resentful","consequence":"Saying yes to all of it drains you and breeds bitterness."}],"debrief":"A kind, regular rhythm keeps the bond strong and leaves the couple some room.","relearn":"Set a fair visiting rhythm; closeness needn't cost every weekend.","persona":"Karthik","source":"weekend rhythm"},
  {"id":"fm-1019","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"An aunt criticises how you dress in front of the whole family at dinner.","options":[{"text":"Stay warm but clear: “I dress in a way I'm comfortable with, Aunty — thanks for caring.”","consequence":"You hold your dignity without making a public scene.","best":true,"outcome":"held"},{"text":"Change your whole wardrobe to silence her","consequence":"Reshaping yourself to dodge one comment hands away your own choices."}],"debrief":"A calm, kind line holds your boundary in public without escalating; your choices stay yours.","relearn":"Hold your line warmly in public; you don't owe anyone a wardrobe to avoid a comment.","persona":"Pooja","source":"public comment"},
  {"id":"fm-1020","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Family wants to announce news of your move before you and your partner have decided.","options":[{"text":"Pause it kindly: “We haven't finalised anything; we'll share once we two have decided.”","consequence":"You keep the decision yours and avoid premature pressure.","best":true,"outcome":"held"},{"text":"Let them announce it to keep everyone happy","consequence":"An early announcement boxes you in before you've chosen."}],"debrief":"The couple decides first, then shares; that order keeps the choice yours.","relearn":"Decide first, announce later; don't let an early announcement box you in.","persona":"Karthik","source":"early announce"},
  {"id":"fm-1021","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Your sister-in-law borrows money from you often and never quite repays it.","options":[{"text":"Be kind and clear: “I can't lend this time, but I'd love to help you plan a budget.”","consequence":"You keep your finances safe and the relationship warm.","best":true,"outcome":"bounded"},{"text":"Keep lending to avoid seeming stingy","consequence":"Endless lending you can't sustain breeds quiet resentment on both sides."}],"debrief":"A warm no to a loan can still offer real help; your finances are a fair thing to protect.","relearn":"A warm no to lending can still offer help; protecting your finances isn't stingy.","persona":"Pooja","source":"the loan"},
  {"id":"fm-1022","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Elders insist you name your future child after a relative; you two prefer another name.","options":[{"text":"Honour the thought, keep the call: “We love that idea; we've chosen a name that's ours.”","consequence":"You respect the gesture and keep the couple's decision.","best":true,"outcome":"held"},{"text":"Use the name you don't want, for peace","consequence":"A name you didn't choose becomes a small daily ache."}],"debrief":"Naming your child is the couple's call; honour the wish, keep the choice.","relearn":"Naming your child is the couple's call; honour the wish, keep the choice.","persona":"Karthik","source":"the name"},
  {"id":"fm-1023","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"branch","hook":"Your mother-in-law shares your private marital matters with neighbours.","options":[{"text":"Address it gently and directly: “Ma, some things are just between us two; please keep them ours.”","consequence":"You protect the couple's privacy without a blow-up.","best":true,"outcome":"bounded"},{"text":"Stop telling her anything and grow cold","consequence":"Going cold punishes the bond instead of fixing the issue."}],"debrief":"Naming the limit kindly protects your privacy while keeping the bond intact.","relearn":"Name the privacy limit kindly; protect what's private without freezing the bond.","persona":"Pooja","source":"kept private"},
  {"id":"fm-1024","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"match","hook":"Match each harsh limit with its kinder, clearer version.","pairs":[{"left":"“Stop barging in.”","right":"“We'd love a quick call before you visit.”"},{"left":"“That's none of your business.”","right":"“This one's ours to decide, with love.”"},{"left":"“You're smothering us.”","right":"“We really need a little space of our own.”"},{"left":"“Stop telling us what to do.”","right":"“We'll ask when we'd like your advice.”"},{"left":"“Leave us alone.”","right":"“We'd love some quiet just the two of us tonight.”"}],"relearn":"Every harsh line has a warm, clear twin that holds the same limit without wounding the person.","persona":"any","source":"kinder version"},
  {"id":"fm-1025","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"match","hook":"Match each kind-boundary move with what it actually protects.","pairs":[{"left":"A call before visits","right":"The couple's privacy and prep time"},{"left":"“Our salary is our call”","right":"Financial independence as a team"},{"left":"“We'll decide and tell you”","right":"The couple's right to choose together"},{"left":"“We'd love your recipes, my way too”","right":"Your own space while welcoming help"},{"left":"A repeatable team line","right":"Both partners, from fresh fights each time"}],"relearn":"Each kind boundary protects something real — privacy, independence, choice, space, or the couple itself.","persona":"any","source":"what it protects"},
  {"id":"fm-1026","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"match","hook":"Match each over-stepping comment with a warm, boundary-holding reply.","pairs":[{"left":"“When's the baby coming?”","right":"“We'll share happy news when there is some.”"},{"left":"“You cook it all wrong.”","right":"“I'd love to learn your way, and keep mine too.”"},{"left":"“Why work so late?”","right":"“My job suits us; thanks for caring.”"},{"left":"“Visit us every weekend.”","right":"“We'll come often, and keep some weekends ours.”"},{"left":"“Tell me everything you two discuss.”","right":"“Some things stay just between us, Ma.”"}],"relearn":"A warm reply honours the person and still holds the couple's line.","persona":"Pooja","source":"warm reply"},
  {"id":"fm-1027","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"match","hook":"Match each phrase with whether it builds a bridge or a needless wall.","pairs":[{"left":"“Call before you drop by”","right":"A bridge: limit plus open door"},{"left":"Blocking them out of spite","right":"A wall: shuts the person out"},{"left":"“Join us Sunday, we plan the rest”","right":"A bridge: includes and still chooses"},{"left":"Months of cold silence","right":"A wall: punishes the whole bond"},{"left":"“We'll ask when we want advice”","right":"A bridge: holds the line, keeps the tie"}],"relearn":"Kind boundaries build bridges — they hold a line while keeping the door open; spite and silence build walls.","persona":"any","source":"bridge not wall"},
  {"id":"fm-1028","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"match","hook":"Match each couple-boundary with the family-team value it stands on.","pairs":[{"left":"“We'll decide together first”","right":"The couple is the first team"},{"left":"“Let's talk and get back to you”","right":"One united, repeatable answer"},{"left":"Refusing private side-complaints","right":"No triangulation between us"},{"left":"Backing your partner in the room","right":"Standing as a team, kindly"},{"left":"A warm, clear shared limit","right":"Honouring family and our decision"}],"relearn":"Every couple-boundary rests on a team value — deciding together, one answer, no side-deals, mutual backing.","persona":"Karthik","source":"team value"},
  {"id":"fm-1029","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"match","hook":"Match each blunt refusal with its respectful, relationship-keeping version.","pairs":[{"left":"“No, and stop asking.”","right":"“Not this time, but thank you for thinking of us.”"},{"left":"“That's a stupid idea.”","right":"“We see it differently; here's what we'd prefer.”"},{"left":"“We'll never agree to that.”","right":"“This one isn't for us, and we appreciate the offer.”"},{"left":"“You always interfere.”","right":"“We'd love to handle this part ourselves.”"},{"left":"“Forget it.”","right":"“Let's find a way that works for everyone.”"}],"relearn":"A respectful refusal declines the ask but honours the person.","persona":"Sneha","source":"respectful no"},
  {"id":"fm-1030","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"match","hook":"Match each warm boundary line with the moment it's made for.","pairs":[{"left":"“We'd love a call before you visit.”","right":"Unannounced drop-ins"},{"left":"“This one's ours to decide, with love.”","right":"Pressure on a couple's choice"},{"left":"“We'll ask when we want advice.”","right":"Unsolicited instructions"},{"left":"“We'll share news when there's news.”","right":"The baby question"},{"left":"“Some things stay just between us.”","right":"Private matters leaking out"}],"relearn":"Each warm line is matched to the moment it defuses — a kind boundary fits the situation it's made for.","persona":"Pooja","source":"line for the moment"},
  {"id":"fm-1031","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two that are cold cut-offs, not kind boundaries.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“We'd love a call before you come over.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Blocking their number after one disagreement","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“We'll decide this together and tell you.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Months of icy silence to teach them a lesson","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“Visit Sunday; we plan the rest ourselves.”","trick":false}],"why":"Blocking after one fight and long icy silence are cut-offs that punish the bond — not warm, open boundaries.","relearn":"A kind boundary stays warm and open; silent freeze-outs and spite-blocks are walls, not limits.","persona":"any","source":"cut-off vs limit"},
  {"id":"fm-1032","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two harsh lines that wound, not the kind ways to hold a limit.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“We'd love your recipes, and I'll cook my way too.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"“Stop barging into our kitchen.”","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“Thanks for caring; this one's ours to decide.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"“Mind your own business for once.”","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“We'll ask when we'd like your advice.”","trick":false}],"why":"“Stop barging in” and “mind your own business” attack the person; the others hold the same limit warmly.","relearn":"The same limit can be held with warmth; harsh phrasing wounds without making the line any firmer.","persona":"Pooja","source":"harsh vs warm"},
  {"id":"fm-1033","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two that are control, not a healthy couple-boundary.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“Let's plan both families' visits together, fairly.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"“You can't visit your own parents anymore.”","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“We'll tell family our news once we're ready.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"“Give me your phone; I decide who you talk to.”","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“Let's handle our money as a team.”","trick":false}],"why":"Cutting you off from your parents and policing your phone are control, not boundaries — that routes to help.","relearn":"A boundary protects the couple; isolating you or policing your phone is control, not a limit.","persona":"Karthik","source":"limit vs control"},
  {"id":"fm-1034","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two replies that just cave, not the ones that hold the line.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“We hear you; we'll decide and let you know.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Saying yes on the spot to stop the pushing","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“Give us a week, then we'll share.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Cancelling your plan because she frowned","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“We love you, and this stays our call.”","trick":false}],"why":"Saying yes to stop the pushing and cancelling because she frowned are caving — they trade your choice for quiet.","relearn":"You can hold a limit warmly under pressure; caving to end discomfort buries your choice.","persona":"Sneha","source":"hold vs cave"},
  {"id":"fm-1035","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that shut family out, not the ones that keep them close.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“Come for dinner Sunday; we'll plan the rest.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"“We're done with this family for good.”","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“Visit anytime, just give us a call first.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Skipping every event to punish them","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“We'd love your help, our own way too.”","trick":false}],"why":"“Done for good” and skipping everything to punish are walls; a kind boundary holds a line while keeping people close.","relearn":"A kind boundary keeps people in your life; total cut-offs and punishing absences wall them out.","persona":"Pooja","source":"close not cut"},
  {"id":"fm-1036","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two that are pressure dressed as 'love', not genuine care.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“Take your time; we just want you happy.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"“If you loved us, you'd obey without question.”","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“We're here whenever you'd like advice.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"“A good bahu never says no to family.”","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“Your choice; we'll support whatever you pick.”","trick":false}],"why":"“If you loved us, you'd obey” and “a good bahu never says no” use love as leverage to remove your choice.","relearn":"Real care leaves room for your no; love used to force obedience is pressure, not love.","persona":"any","source":"care vs pressure"},
  {"id":"fm-1037","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two triangulation moves, not the team-keeping ones.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“If something's wrong, let's all talk kindly together.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"“Don't tell your wife, but do this for me.”","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“We decide together, then answer as one.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"“Your husband's the problem; side with me.”","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“Let's get back to you once we've talked.”","trick":false}],"why":"Secret side-deals and “side with me against your partner” are triangulation; the rest keep the couple a team.","relearn":"Triangulation routes complaints around your partner; a team decides and answers as one.","persona":"Karthik","source":"triangulation"},
  {"id":"fm-1038","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a 'no' to one request isn't a 'no' to the whole person. You can decline and still love them. Sit with that?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["I can do that","No isn't rejection","Worth trying"],"affirm":"A kind no declines a behaviour, not the bond; you can hold a limit and keep loving the person fully.","relearn":"A no to one ask isn't rejection of the person; you can decline and still love them.","persona":"Pooja","source":"no isn't rejection"},
  {"id":"fm-1039","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: think of a limit you wish you'd set sooner. What stopped you was probably fear of seeming unkind, na?","prompt":"What comes up?","options":["Fear of unkindness","Wanting to keep peace","Habit of adjusting"],"affirm":"Whatever held you back is human; a kind limit is itself an act of care, not unkindness.","relearn":"What stops us setting limits is often fear of seeming unkind; a kind limit is care, not cruelty.","persona":"any","source":"what stops us"},
  {"id":"fm-1040","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: 'we'll decide together and get back to you' is one line you can reuse for years. Could that help you?","prompt":"How's that sit?","options":["I'll use it","One steady line","Saves a fight"],"affirm":"A repeatable team line lets the couple answer as one without a fresh argument every time.","relearn":"One reusable team line — 'we'll decide together and get back to you' — saves a fresh fight each time.","persona":"Karthik","source":"one steady line"},
  {"id":"fm-1041","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: receiving the love and declining the overreach can happen in the same warm breath. Picture it?","prompt":"What do you feel?","options":["I can picture it","Love and limit","Both at once"],"affirm":"You can thank someone for caring and still hold your line — warmth and a boundary aren't opposites.","relearn":"You can receive the love and decline the overreach in the same sentence; they aren't opposites.","persona":"Pooja","source":"love and limit"},
  {"id":"fm-1042","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a boundary that mildly disappoints someone isn't a failed boundary. You can't control every reaction. Agree?","prompt":"Your honest read?","options":["That's freeing","Not my fault","I'll allow it"],"affirm":"You're responsible for your kindness, not for someone's reaction; mild disappointment is allowed.","relearn":"A kind limit can still disappoint a little; you control your kindness, not their reaction.","persona":"Sneha","source":"reaction isn't yours"},
  {"id":"fm-1043","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: limits flex with the season — a 'just for now' boundary after a baby or a job change is completely real. Makes sense?","prompt":"What's your view?","options":["Makes sense","For-now is real","Seasons change"],"affirm":"A temporary boundary is honest, not weak; needs shift with newborns, jobs and health, and that's okay.","relearn":"A 'just for now' limit is real and valid; boundaries can flex with the season of life.","persona":"any","source":"for-now is real"},
  {"id":"fm-1044","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a kind boundary protects the relationship you want to keep — it's an act of staying, not leaving. Land for you?","prompt":"What lands?","options":["It lands","Staying, not leaving","Protects the bond"],"affirm":"Boundaries aren't a step toward the exit; they're how you protect a bond you want to keep for the long haul.","relearn":"A kind boundary is an act of staying, not leaving; it protects the bond you want to keep.","persona":"Pooja","source":"staying not leaving"},
  {"id":"fm-1045","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: backing your partner warmly in the room isn't choosing sides against family — it's being a team. Sit right?","prompt":"How's that?","options":["Sits right","Team, not sides","I'll back them"],"affirm":"Standing with your partner is teamwork, not betrayal of family; a united, kind front lowers conflict for everyone.","relearn":"Backing your partner in the room is being a team, not choosing sides against family.","persona":"Karthik","source":"team not sides"},
  {"id":"fm-1046","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"role-play","hook":"Your mother-in-law keeps rearranging how you run the house. You want warm but clear.","setup":"Say it kindly:","yourLine":[{"text":"“I love your help, Ma, and I'd like to run our home my own way too.”","best":true},{"text":"“Fine, do whatever you think is best.”"}],"relearn":"Welcome the help and keep your own way in one kind sentence; that's a warm, clear limit.","persona":"Pooja","source":"run our home"},
  {"id":"fm-1047","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"role-play","hook":"A relative asks you to keep a money decision secret from your partner.","setup":"Hold the team line:","yourLine":[{"text":"“I don't keep money secrets from her; let's talk about it together.”","best":true},{"text":"“Okay, I won't mention it to her.”"}],"relearn":"Refusing a secret side-deal keeps the couple a team and shuts triangulation down kindly.","persona":"Karthik","source":"no secrets"},
  {"id":"fm-1048","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"role-play","hook":"Relatives keep pressing you on when you'll “settle down” at every function.","setup":"Deflect warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"“I'm happy with my life right now; I'll share news when there's news.”","best":true},{"text":"“I don't know, maybe soon, I guess.”"}],"relearn":"A calm, warm line honours the asker and closes the topic without owing anyone your timeline.","persona":"Sneha","source":"settle down"},
  {"id":"fm-1049","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"role-play","hook":"Your father-in-law tells you to drop a friendship he doesn't approve of.","setup":"Honour, keep your call:","yourLine":[{"text":"“I respect your concern, Papa; my friendships are mine to choose.”","best":true},{"text":"“Alright, I'll stop seeing her if you say so.”"}],"relearn":"You can honour an elder's concern and still keep your own friendships; respect isn't obedience.","persona":"Pooja","source":"my friendships"},
  {"id":"fm-1050","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"role-play","hook":"Your mother insists you visit every weekend; you and your partner need some of your own.","setup":"Offer a fair rhythm:","yourLine":[{"text":"“We'll come two Sundays a month, Ma, and we'd love you to visit us too.”","best":true},{"text":"“Of course, we'll be there every weekend.”"}],"relearn":"A warm, fair rhythm keeps the bond close while leaving the couple some weekends of its own.","persona":"Karthik","source":"fair rhythm"},
  {"id":"fm-1051","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"role-play","hook":"An aunt keeps asking exactly how much you and your partner earn.","setup":"Keep it private, warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"“We keep our finances between us, Aunty — hope you understand.”","best":true},{"text":"“Um, well, it's around... let me tell you.”"}],"relearn":"Your earnings are the couple's own; a warm, private line holds that without offence.","persona":"Pooja","source":"our finances"},
  {"id":"fm-1052","cat":"kind-boundaries","type":"role-play","hook":"In front of family, a relative blames your partner for a decision you both made together.","setup":"Stand as a team:","yourLine":[{"text":"“Actually, we decided this together — it was both of us.”","best":true},{"text":"“...” (stay quiet and let it slide)"}],"relearn":"Backing your partner in the room is teamwork, not picking sides; silence leaves them exposed.","persona":"Karthik","source":"we decided"},
  {"id":"fm-1080","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A respectful son just stays quiet and never contradicts his parents.\"","myth":{"un":"A respectful son just stays quiet and never contradicts his parents.","re":"You can honour your parents and still voice a different view, kindly and clearly.","why":"Honouring isn't the same as having no voice of your own."},"relearn":"Respect lets you disagree with care; staying silent isn't the only way to honour parents.","persona":"Karthik","source":"respect not silence","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1081","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Elders never have to apologise; respect only flows upward.\"","myth":{"un":"Elders never have to apologise; respect only flows upward.","re":"Respect runs both ways across generations; elders can own a mistake too, and that models real respect.","why":"Respect owed in only one direction isn't respect, it's hierarchy."},"relearn":"Respect flows both ways; an elder owning a mistake teaches it better than demanding it one-way.","persona":"Razia","source":"respect runs both ways","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1082","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If you don't follow an elder's advice exactly, you've insulted them.\"","myth":{"un":"If you don't follow an elder's advice exactly, you've insulted them.","re":"You can thank an elder, weigh their advice sincerely, and still make a different choice.","why":"Taking advice seriously and obeying it are not the same thing."},"relearn":"Honour the advice, then decide for yourselves; choosing differently isn't an insult.","persona":"Pooja","source":"honour then choose","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1083","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Tradition can never change, so just do it the way it's always been done.\"","myth":{"un":"Tradition can never change, so just do it the way it's always been done.","re":"You can keep a tradition's meaning while adapting how you do it, with the family's blessing over time.","why":"Living traditions have always shifted; honouring one allows updating it."},"relearn":"Keep a tradition's meaning, adapt the form together; honouring it doesn't mean freezing it.","persona":"Sneha","source":"tradition you can shape","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1084","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"As long as everyone obeys, the family is respectful and happy.\"","myth":{"un":"As long as everyone obeys, the family is respectful and happy.","re":"Obedience driven by fear isn't respect; a home built on fear isn't the same as one built on respect.","why":"Respect is freely given; fear is extracted, and the two feel very different."},"relearn":"Fear-driven obedience isn't respect; a home on fear differs from a home on respect.","persona":"Pooja","source":"fear isn't respect","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1085","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"In any disagreement with an elder, the younger one is automatically wrong.\"","myth":{"un":"In any disagreement with an elder, the younger one is automatically wrong.","re":"Age doesn't decide who's right; a younger person can hold a fair point and still be respectful.","why":"Wisdom often comes with age, but being older doesn't make every view correct."},"relearn":"Age doesn't settle who's right; a younger person can be both correct and respectful.","persona":"Karthik","source":"both can be right","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1086","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Keeping your own beliefs after marriage disrespects your in-laws' ways.\"","myth":{"un":"Keeping your own beliefs after marriage disrespects your in-laws' ways.","re":"You can hold your own beliefs and still respect your in-laws'; mutual respect doesn't require erasing yours.","why":"Two sets of beliefs can sit side by side with respect on both sides."},"relearn":"You can keep your own beliefs and respect theirs; respect doesn't mean erasing yourself.","persona":"Razia","source":"keeping faith respectfully","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1087","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If you're truly respectful, you'll never push back on an elder's plan for you.\"","myth":{"un":"If you're truly respectful, you'll never push back on an elder's plan for you.","re":"Pushing back warmly on a plan you didn't choose is respectful; it honours both the elder and your own life.","why":"Real respect includes honesty about your own direction."},"relearn":"Warm pushback on a plan you didn't choose is still respect; it honours the elder and your life.","persona":"Sneha","source":"respect deflects pressure","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1088","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Disagreeing with an elder is always rude, no matter how you say it.\"","myth":{"un":"Disagreeing with an elder is always rude, no matter how you say it.","re":"It's how you disagree that matters; warm phrasing that honours the person keeps both the bond and your voice.","why":"Tone and care turn a disagreement into a respectful one."},"relearn":"Disagreeing respectfully, warmly and honouring the person, keeps both the bond and your voice.","persona":"any","source":"disagree warmly","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1089","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"You have to choose between respecting elders and ever saying no to them.\"","myth":{"un":"You have to choose between respecting elders and ever saying no to them.","re":"Respect and a kind boundary go together; respecting an elder can make your 'no' land more gently.","why":"A respected elder hears a limit better than a resented one."},"relearn":"Respect and a kind no aren't opposites; respect can make the boundary land softer.","persona":"Pooja","source":"respect aids the no","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1090","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Honouring your elders and obeying your elders mean exactly the same thing.\"","myth":{"un":"Honouring your elders and obeying your elders mean exactly the same thing.","re":"Honouring is about care, attention and respect; obeying is doing as told, and you can do the first without the second.","why":"You can deeply honour someone whose instruction you don't follow."},"relearn":"Honour is care and respect; obeying is doing as told; you can honour without obeying.","persona":"Razia","source":"honour without obeying","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1091","type":"branch","hook":"At every gathering, an aunt loudly asks when you'll finally settle down and marry.","options":[{"text":"Warmly: \"I know you care, Maasi; I'll get there in my own time.\"","consequence":"You honour her care and hold your own pace.","outcome":"deflected","best":true},{"text":"Snap back that it's none of her business","consequence":"A sharp retort wins the moment but starts a family rift."}],"debrief":"Honour the care, hold your pace; a warm line deflects pressure without a family war.","relearn":"Receive the care, keep your timeline; warmth deflects the pressure without rejecting her.","persona":"Sneha","source":"when will you settle","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1092","type":"branch","hook":"Your father assumed you'd join the family business; you've built a different career you love.","options":[{"text":"Thank him, explain your path warmly, and ask him to be proud of this one","consequence":"He feels honoured even as you keep your direction.","outcome":"honoured","best":true},{"text":"Quietly resent him and avoid the topic for years","consequence":"Avoidance lets the hurt fester and he never understands your choice."}],"debrief":"Thank him and own your path warmly; honouring him doesn't mean taking the path he planned.","relearn":"Honour his hope and keep your own career; gratitude plus clarity holds both.","persona":"Karthik","source":"father's career plan","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1093","type":"branch","hook":"Your mother-in-law expects you to keep a strict fast you don't observe.","options":[{"text":"Join the parts that mean something to you, opt out of the fast","consequence":"You share the day's spirit without forcing belief.","outcome":"warm-opt","best":true},{"text":"Keep the fast resentfully to avoid a fuss","consequence":"Going through the motions in resentment honours neither of you."}],"debrief":"Share what's meaningful, opt out kindly; you can honour the day and your own beliefs.","relearn":"Join the meaningful parts, decline the fast kindly; honour the bond and yourself.","persona":"Pooja","source":"fasting tradition","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1094","type":"branch","hook":"At dinner an elder waves away your opinion with \"children shouldn't speak on this.\"","options":[{"text":"Stay calm and warm: \"I hear you; I'd still love to share how I see it.\"","consequence":"You keep your voice without escalating into a fight.","outcome":"steady","best":true},{"text":"Go silent and swallow it to keep the peace","consequence":"Silence keeps a brittle peace but teaches that your view doesn't count."}],"debrief":"Hold your voice warmly; respect doesn't require swallowing your view to keep a fragile peace.","relearn":"Keep your voice calmly; you can honour the elder and still ask to be heard.","persona":"Razia","source":"elder dismisses your view","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1095","type":"branch","hook":"An elder demands respect from you but speaks to you with constant contempt.","options":[{"text":"Keep treating them with dignity and kindly name that respect goes both ways","consequence":"You model the mutual respect you're asking for.","outcome":"mutual","best":true},{"text":"Match their contempt to make a point","consequence":"Trading contempt just confirms the cycle and lowers you both."}],"debrief":"Hold dignity and name that respect runs both ways; modelling it beats matching contempt.","relearn":"Respect flows both ways; model dignity and name it, rather than mirroring the contempt.","persona":"any","source":"respect runs both ways","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1096","type":"branch","hook":"Relatives keep pitying you for being single and 'pray you'll be saved' by marriage soon.","options":[{"text":"Smile and say warmly that your life is full and you're happy as you are","consequence":"You hold your dignity and deflect the stigma kindly.","outcome":"grounded","best":true},{"text":"Argue heatedly that single life is superior","consequence":"Turning it into a debate just hands them the drama they expected."}],"debrief":"Hold your dignity warmly; you can honour relatives and still decline their pity for your choices.","relearn":"Deflect the pity with warmth; your life is yours to define, not theirs to rescue.","persona":"Sneha","source":"unmarried at family event","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1097","type":"branch","hook":"Your grandfather pushes for a baby soon; you two aren't ready.","options":[{"text":"Thank him for his love; say the timing is yours and your partner's","consequence":"He feels heard, the decision stays where it belongs.","outcome":"held","best":true},{"text":"Promise vaguely just to end it","consequence":"A hollow promise buys quiet now and a harder talk later."}],"debrief":"Receive his love, keep the timing as the couple's call; honour him without handing over the choice.","relearn":"Honour his eagerness, hold the decision; some choices stay the couple's, even with a beloved elder.","persona":"Karthik","source":"grandfather's strong opinion","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1098","type":"branch","hook":"Your mother-in-law insists every meal be her exact way; you'd like room to differ.","options":[{"text":"Cook her classics with care, ask to add a few of your own","consequence":"Her tradition is honoured, your kitchen has your touch too.","outcome":"shared","best":true},{"text":"Take over and dismiss her recipes","consequence":"Pushing her out of her kitchen reads as contempt, not change."}],"debrief":"Honour her recipes and add yours; respect both ways lets two cooks share one kitchen.","relearn":"Keep her classics, make room for yours; honour and your own voice can coexist.","persona":"Razia","source":"mother-in-law's cooking rules","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1099","type":"branch","hook":"An elder corrects you sharply in front of guests over something small.","options":[{"text":"Let it pass gracefully now and raise it privately and warmly later","consequence":"You keep the peace publicly and still get to be heard.","outcome":"graceful","best":true},{"text":"Defend yourself loudly right there in front of everyone","consequence":"A public defence wins the point but costs everyone face."}],"debrief":"Stay graceful in the room, speak privately later; respect and your voice both survive.","relearn":"Honour the moment publicly, address it privately; you can keep dignity and still be heard.","persona":"any","source":"public correction","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1100","type":"branch","hook":"Your in-laws ask your opinion on a decision, then act as if you never spoke.","options":[{"text":"Note warmly that you'd offered a view, and ask it be weighed too","consequence":"You ask for the two-way respect that asking you implied.","outcome":"weighed","best":true},{"text":"Decide your view never matters and stop offering it","consequence":"Withdrawing teaches them your voice really can be skipped."}],"debrief":"Ask for your view to count too; respect both ways means being heard, not just consulted.","relearn":"Name that you'd shared a view and ask it be weighed; respect runs both directions.","persona":"Sneha","source":"elders ask, then ignore","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1101","type":"branch","hook":"Your in-laws expect you to fully drop your own family's customs and adopt only theirs.","options":[{"text":"Warmly embrace many of their customs while keeping a few of your own alive","consequence":"Both heritages live on, and no one is erased.","outcome":"both-live","best":true},{"text":"Abandon all of yours to seem like the perfect bahu","consequence":"Erasing your own heritage to please them slowly hollows you out."}],"debrief":"Embrace theirs and keep some of yours; respect both ways means neither heritage gets erased.","relearn":"Adopt much of their way and keep some of yours; honouring them needn't erase you.","persona":"Pooja","source":"honour and your faith","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1102","type":"match","hook":"Match each nosy pressure question to a warm, dignified reply.","pairs":[{"left":"\"When are you getting married?\"","right":"\"When it's right for me, Maasi.\""},{"left":"\"Why no kids yet?\"","right":"\"That's between me and my partner.\""},{"left":"\"Aren't you too old now?\"","right":"\"I'm exactly where I want to be.\""},{"left":"\"What will people say?\"","right":"\"They'll find something either way.\""},{"left":"\"Don't you want to settle?\"","right":"\"My life already feels settled.\""}],"relearn":"Warm, dignified replies deflect nosy pressure without insulting the elder asking.","persona":"Sneha","source":"deflecting the pressure","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1103","type":"match","hook":"Match each moment to a line that honours the elder and keeps your voice.","pairs":[{"left":"Unwanted advice","right":"\"Thank you; we'll think it over.\""},{"left":"A real disagreement","right":"\"With respect, we see it differently.\""},{"left":"A choice that's yours","right":"\"We'd love to do this our way.\""},{"left":"A tradition you'll adapt","right":"\"We'll keep the heart of it, our version.\""},{"left":"Being talked over","right":"\"I'd still like to finish my thought.\""}],"relearn":"A respectful line exists for advice, disagreement, your own choices, adapting a custom, and being heard.","persona":"any","source":"honour-and-voice phrases","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1104","type":"match","hook":"Match each respectful move to what it honours.","pairs":[{"left":"Listening because you value them","right":"Honours their experience"},{"left":"Disagreeing warmly and kindly","right":"Honours your own voice"},{"left":"Weighing advice, then choosing","right":"Honours both at once"},{"left":"Caring for them when unwell","right":"Honours the bond"},{"left":"Thanking, then deciding for yourselves","right":"Honours the relationship"}],"relearn":"Respect can honour their experience, your voice, both at once, the bond and the relationship, all without obeying.","persona":"Razia","source":"respect vs obedience","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1105","type":"match","hook":"Match each thing an elder offers to the respectful way to receive it.","pairs":[{"left":"Hard-won life wisdom","right":"Listen closely, take what fits"},{"left":"An outdated demand","right":"Decline kindly, no scorn"},{"left":"A meaningful ritual","right":"Join in where it moves you"},{"left":"A worried warning","right":"Thank them, then decide"},{"left":"A generous offer of help","right":"Accept warmly or decline gently"}],"relearn":"You can listen to wisdom, decline the outdated, join rituals, weigh warnings and handle offers, all with respect.","persona":"Sneha","source":"receiving each offering","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1106","type":"match","hook":"Match each harsh line to its warmer version that still holds your ground.","pairs":[{"left":"\"You're so old-fashioned.\"","right":"\"Times have changed; help us find a middle way.\""},{"left":"\"Stop telling me what to do.\"","right":"\"I value your view; this call is mine.\""},{"left":"\"That's a stupid tradition.\"","right":"\"Help me understand what it means to you.\""},{"left":"\"You never listen.\"","right":"\"I'd love to feel heard on this.\""},{"left":"\"I don't care what you think.\"","right":"\"I hear you, and I see it differently.\""}],"relearn":"The same stance can be said warmly; respectful phrasing keeps both your point and the bond.","persona":"Karthik","source":"warm vs harsh phrasing","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1107","type":"match","hook":"Match each respectful act to who is showing it.","pairs":[{"left":"Asking the younger ones, then truly listening","right":"An elder respecting the young"},{"left":"Weighing an elder's advice sincerely","right":"A young one respecting elders"},{"left":"Owning a mistake to the younger ones","right":"An elder modelling humility"},{"left":"Disagreeing kindly, not rudely","right":"A young one keeping their voice"},{"left":"Deciding some things together","right":"Both sides sharing respect"}],"relearn":"Respect flows both ways: elders listen and own mistakes; the young weigh advice and disagree with care.","persona":"any","source":"respect both directions","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1108","type":"match","hook":"Match each elder request to a reply that honours them and keeps your choice.","pairs":[{"left":"\"Quit your job after marriage.\"","right":"\"I love that you care; I'm keeping my work.\""},{"left":"\"Have children right away.\"","right":"\"We'll choose our own timing.\""},{"left":"\"Move in with us for good.\"","right":"\"We'll visit often; we'll live our own place.\""},{"left":"\"Follow our every custom.\"","right":"\"We'll keep the ones that matter most.\""},{"left":"\"Let us pick your home.\"","right":"\"Your input matters; the choice is ours.\""}],"relearn":"Each request can meet warmth and a clear choice; honouring an elder isn't surrender.","persona":"Razia","source":"honour without surrender","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1109","type":"match","hook":"Match each piece of single-shaming to a kind, confident reply.","pairs":[{"left":"\"Such a waste, still single.\"","right":"\"I'm building a life I love.\""},{"left":"\"Who'll look after you later?\"","right":"\"I'm planning well for myself.\""},{"left":"\"Lower your standards.\"","right":"\"I'd rather wait for the right fit.\""},{"left":"\"People are talking.\"","right":"\"Let them; I'm fine.\""},{"left":"\"Don't you feel lonely?\"","right":"\"I have a full, connected life.\""}],"relearn":"Single-shaming meets a calm, confident reply; you can honour relatives and still decline their pity.","persona":"Sneha","source":"stigma-proof comebacks","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1110","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each one: real respect, or fear wearing respect's mask?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Listening because you value them"},{"id":"b","text":"Agreeing only because you're scared"},{"id":"c","text":"Disagreeing warmly and honestly"},{"id":"d","text":"Staying silent to avoid punishment"},{"id":"e","text":"Weighing advice, then choosing"},{"id":"f","text":"Hiding your real view in dread"}],"bins":[{"id":"respect","label":"Real respect","valence":"pos"},{"id":"fear","label":"Just fear","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"respect","b":"fear","c":"respect","d":"fear","e":"respect","f":"fear"},"relearn":"Valuing, disagreeing warmly and choosing is respect; silence and hidden views from dread are just fear.","persona":"Razia","source":"respect or fear","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1111","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: respect flowing both ways, or demanded only one way?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Elders' experience is valued"},{"id":"b","text":"Only the young must ever adjust"},{"id":"c","text":"The couple's choices count too"},{"id":"d","text":"The young may never disagree"},{"id":"e","text":"Both sides can say sorry"},{"id":"f","text":"Elders are above all questions"}],"bins":[{"id":"both","label":"Both ways","valence":"pos"},{"id":"one","label":"One way only","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"both","b":"one","c":"both","d":"one","e":"both","f":"one"},"relearn":"Valuing elders and the couple's choices, with apologies both ways, is mutual; all the adjusting on one side isn't.","persona":"any","source":"both ways or one way","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1112","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each reply: honours the elder and your voice, or surrenders your voice?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Thank you; we'll decide for ourselves.\""},{"id":"b","text":"Obeying silently to dodge any fuss"},{"id":"c","text":"\"I hear you, and I see it differently.\""},{"id":"d","text":"Saying yes you don't mean, every time"},{"id":"e","text":"Weighing the advice, then choosing"},{"id":"f","text":"Dropping every plan the moment they object"}],"bins":[{"id":"honour","label":"Honours both","valence":"pos"},{"id":"surrender","label":"Surrenders voice","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"honour","b":"surrender","c":"honour","d":"surrender","e":"honour","f":"surrender"},"relearn":"Thanking and deciding for yourselves keeps both; silent obedience and unmeant yeses surrender your voice.","persona":"Sneha","source":"honours or surrenders","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1113","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each line to an elder: respectful disagreement, or contempt?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"With respect, we see it differently.\""},{"id":"b","text":"\"That's a ridiculous idea.\""},{"id":"c","text":"\"Help me understand what it means to you.\""},{"id":"d","text":"\"You just don't get it.\""},{"id":"e","text":"\"Thank you; we'll think it over.\""},{"id":"f","text":"\"Stop living in the past.\""}],"bins":[{"id":"respectful","label":"Respectful","valence":"pos"},{"id":"contempt","label":"Contemptuous","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"respectful","b":"contempt","c":"respectful","d":"contempt","e":"respectful","f":"contempt"},"relearn":"You can disagree and ask to understand respectfully; mockery and put-downs cross into contempt.","persona":"Razia","source":"respectful or contemptuous","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1114","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each decision: clearly the couple's own to keep, or genuinely worth honouring elders on?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"When you two have children"},{"id":"b","text":"The menu for a shared festival"},{"id":"c","text":"How you spend your own salary"},{"id":"d","text":"A joint family ritual everyone shares"},{"id":"e","text":"Which career you pursue"},{"id":"f","text":"The date for a family puja together"}],"bins":[{"id":"couple","label":"Couple's call","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shared","label":"Honour together","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"couple","b":"shared","c":"couple","d":"shared","e":"couple","f":"shared"},"relearn":"Children, salary and career are the couple's call; shared festivals and pujas are worth deciding with the family.","persona":"any","source":"couple's call or shared","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1115","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each reply to 'when will you marry?': warm deflection, or escalation?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"When it's right for me, Maasi.\""},{"id":"b","text":"\"None of your business, ever!\""},{"id":"c","text":"\"I'm happy where I am, thanks.\""},{"id":"d","text":"Storming off in a huff"},{"id":"e","text":"\"I'll get there in my own time.\""},{"id":"f","text":"\"You ruined this whole party.\""}],"bins":[{"id":"deflect","label":"Warm deflection","valence":"pos"},{"id":"escalate","label":"Escalation","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"deflect","b":"escalate","c":"deflect","d":"escalate","e":"deflect","f":"escalate"},"relearn":"Warm, dignified lines deflect the pressure; snapping and storming off just escalate into a family scene.","persona":"Sneha","source":"deflect or escalate","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1116","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each one: honouring an elder, or simply obeying them?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Greeting them warmly and listening"},{"id":"b","text":"Doing exactly as told, against your judgement"},{"id":"c","text":"Caring for them when they're unwell"},{"id":"d","text":"Hiding your real choices to comply"},{"id":"e","text":"Thanking them for their concern"},{"id":"f","text":"Cancelling your plans on their command"}],"bins":[{"id":"honour","label":"Honouring","valence":"pos"},{"id":"obey","label":"Just obeying","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"honour","b":"obey","c":"honour","d":"obey","e":"honour","f":"obey"},"relearn":"Greeting, caring and thanking are how you honour an elder; doing as told against your judgement is just obeying.","persona":"Karthik","source":"honour or obey","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1117","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: respect means honouring and listening, not handing over every choice. Does that distinction land?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["It lands","Honour, not obey","Worth holding"],"affirm":"Respect honours and listens; it doesn't require surrendering every choice you get to make.","relearn":"Respect means honouring and listening, not obeying in everything.","persona":"any","source":"respect not obedience","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1118","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you don't owe anyone a timeline for marriage or kids; warmth and your own pace can coexist. See it?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["I see it","My own pace","No timeline owed"],"affirm":"You can be warm to relatives and still hold your own pace; their pressure isn't a deadline you owe.","relearn":"You owe no one a life timeline; you can stay warm and keep your own pace.","persona":"Sneha","source":"your own pace","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1119","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: respect that only ever flows upward isn't respect, it's hierarchy. Real respect runs both ways. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","Both ways","Not just upward"],"affirm":"Respect that only flows one way is hierarchy; genuine respect runs in both directions across generations.","relearn":"Respect runs both ways across generations, not in one direction only.","persona":"Razia","source":"both ways","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1120","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you can sincerely honour an elder's advice AND still make a different choice. Both are true at once.","prompt":"How does that sit?","options":["Both true","Honour and choose","Makes sense"],"affirm":"Honouring advice and following it aren't the same; you can value an elder's view and still choose your own way.","relearn":"You can honour an elder's advice and still make your own decision.","persona":"any","source":"honour and choose","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1121","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: an elder who feels respected is far more open to your boundaries; respect can actually aid your 'no'.","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["True","Respect aids it","Worth remembering"],"affirm":"Respect and a kind boundary reinforce each other; a respected elder hears your limit more openly.","relearn":"Respect and boundaries reinforce each other; respect can help your no land.","persona":"Pooja","source":"respect and boundaries","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1122","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a relationship built on fear isn't the same as one built on respect, even if it looks obedient. Resonate?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Resonates","Not the same","Fear isn't respect"],"affirm":"Obedience from fear can look like respect, but fear and respect are not the same relationship at all.","relearn":"Respect is not fear; a bond built on fear isn't one built on respect.","persona":"Razia","source":"respect not fear","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1123","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you can join a tradition warmly AND respectfully opt out of specific parts. Both can be true. See it?","prompt":"How does it land?","options":["I see it","Join and opt out","Both true"],"affirm":"Joining traditions warmly and opting out of specific parts respectfully can sit together; it isn't all-or-nothing.","relearn":"You can join traditions warmly and still opt out of specific things, respectfully.","persona":"Sneha","source":"warmly opt out","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1124","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: keeping your own voice and showing deep respect aren't opposites; the warmest homes hold both. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","Both at once","Not opposites"],"affirm":"Keeping your voice and showing respect aren't opposites; you can hold both in the same relationship.","relearn":"Keeping your own voice is compatible with deep respect; they aren't opposites.","persona":"any","source":"keep your voice","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1125","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two that are fear dressed up as respect, not the real thing.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Listening because you value their experience","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Agreeing only because you're scared to speak","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Disagreeing politely and staying warm","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Hiding your real view in dread of anger","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Weighing their advice, then choosing","trick":false}],"why":"Scared agreement and views hidden in dread are fear, not respect; the others are genuine respect.","relearn":"Real respect includes honest disagreement; agreement or silence driven by fear isn't respect.","persona":"Sneha","source":"fear masked as respect","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1126","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines where respect is demanded in one direction only.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"You'll respect me, but I owe you none.\"","trick":true},{"id":"b","text":"\"Let's both speak kindly to each other.\"","trick":false},{"id":"c","text":"\"Children must obey; elders need not explain.\"","trick":true},{"id":"d","text":"\"I'll listen to you as you listen to me.\"","trick":false},{"id":"e","text":"\"We can each own our mistakes.\"","trick":false}],"why":"The caught lines demand respect one-way only; respect that flows both ways sounds mutual, not top-down.","relearn":"Respect runs both ways across generations; respect demanded one-way only is just hierarchy.","persona":"Razia","source":"one-way respect","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1127","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two responses that surrender your voice instead of keeping it.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Thank you; we'll decide for ourselves.\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Obeying silently to avoid any friction","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Listening fully, then making your own call","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Saying yes you don't mean to keep the peace","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"With respect, we see it differently.\"","trick":false}],"why":"Silent obedience and unmeant yeses drop your voice; the others honour the elder and keep it.","relearn":"Honour the elder and keep your voice; silent obedience and unmeant yeses surrender it.","persona":"any","source":"respect vs surrender","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1128","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that cross from disagreement into contempt.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"With respect, we see it differently.\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"That's a ridiculous, backward idea.\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Help me understand what it means to you.\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"You're too old to get it.\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"Thank you; we'll think it over.\"","trick":false}],"why":"Mockery and 'too old to get it' are contempt; you can disagree firmly while still being respectful.","relearn":"You can disagree firmly and respectfully; mockery and put-downs cross into contempt.","persona":"Razia","source":"respectful vs contempt","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1129","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two replies to 'when will you marry?' that escalate into a scene.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"When it's right for me, Maasi.\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Mind your own life, always!\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"I'm happy where I am, thank you.\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"You've ruined the whole evening.\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"I'll get there in my own time.\"","trick":false}],"why":"The caught replies escalate into a fight; warm, dignified lines deflect the pressure without a scene.","relearn":"Warm, dignified lines deflect marriage pressure; snapping just escalates into a scene.","persona":"Sneha","source":"deflect vs escalate","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1130","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that are control, not honouring an elder.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Greeting them warmly and listening","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Doing as told against your own judgement","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Caring for them when they're unwell","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Cancelling your plans on their command","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Thanking them for their concern","trick":false}],"why":"Obeying against your judgement and cancelling on command are control; greeting, caring and thanking honour them.","relearn":"Greeting, caring and thanking honour an elder; obeying against your judgement is control.","persona":"Karthik","source":"honour vs control","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1131","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two that erase you, not the warm ways to honour a tradition.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Joining the parts that mean something to you","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Faking belief you don't hold to please them","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Keeping a custom's heart in your own version","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Dropping every belief of your own to fit in","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Opting out of one part, kindly and clearly","trick":false}],"why":"Faking belief and dropping all your own beliefs erase you; honouring a tradition can keep both it and you.","relearn":"Honouring a tradition can keep both it and you; faking belief or erasing yourself doesn't.","persona":"any","source":"tradition: join vs erase","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1132","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two that treat your voice as if it doesn't count.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Elders ask your view and weigh it","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Elders ask, then act as if you never spoke","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Your kind disagreement is heard out","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Your opinion is waved away as 'insolence'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"A decision the couple makes is respected","trick":false}],"why":"Being consulted then ignored, or waved off as insolence, skips your voice; real respect actually weighs it.","relearn":"Real respect weighs your view; being consulted then ignored skips your voice.","persona":"Razia","source":"heard vs ignored","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1133","type":"role-play","hook":"An aunt corners you at a wedding asking why you're still not married. Be warm and firm.","setup":"Respond warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I appreciate you caring, Maasi; I'll marry when it's right for me.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Stop asking me that, it's so annoying.\""}],"relearn":"A warm, clear line honours the elder and keeps your own voice at the same time.","persona":"Sneha","source":"marriage pressure","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1134","type":"role-play","hook":"Your father is hurt you didn't join the family firm. Honour him and hold your path.","setup":"Reply warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I'm grateful for everything you built, Papa; this work is the path I love.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"It's my life, not yours, so drop it.\""}],"relearn":"A warm, clear line honours the elder and keeps your own voice at the same time.","persona":"Karthik","source":"father's plan","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1135","type":"role-play","hook":"An elder insists you quit your job after marriage. Be respectful and clear.","setup":"Say it warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Thank you for caring about our home; my work matters to me and I'm keeping it.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"That's an outdated idea, I won't even discuss it.\""}],"relearn":"A warm, clear line honours the elder and keeps your own voice at the same time.","persona":"Razia","source":"elder's outdated demand","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1136","type":"role-play","hook":"Your mother-in-law wants you to keep a strict fast you don't observe. Honour her and yourself.","setup":"Respond warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I love being part of this day; I'll join the prayers, though I won't keep the fast.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"I don't believe in that, so I'm not doing it.\""}],"relearn":"A warm, clear line honours the elder and keeps your own voice at the same time.","persona":"Pooja","source":"opting out of a ritual","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1137","type":"role-play","hook":"At a family meeting an elder keeps cutting you off. Ask for space without rudeness.","setup":"Say it warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I really want to hear you; I'd love to finish my thought first, please.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Will you let me speak for once?\""}],"relearn":"A warm, clear line honours the elder and keeps your own voice at the same time.","persona":"any","source":"being talked over","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1138","type":"role-play","hook":"A relative says she 'prays you'll be saved by marriage soon'. Hold your dignity warmly.","setup":"Reply warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"That's kind of you; honestly, my life already feels full and happy.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"I don't need saving, please stop.\""}],"relearn":"A warm, clear line honours the elder and keeps your own voice at the same time.","persona":"Sneha","source":"pity for being single","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1139","type":"role-play","hook":"An elder demands respect while speaking to you with contempt. Name it kindly.","setup":"Say it warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I do respect you; I'd love for us to speak kindly to each other both ways.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You don't respect me, so why should I respect you?\""}],"relearn":"A warm, clear line honours the elder and keeps your own voice at the same time.","persona":"Razia","source":"one-way respect","cat":"respect-both-ways"},
  {"id":"fm-1170","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"Your mother-in-law keeps changing your child's diet behind your back. You want it to stop without a fight.","options":[{"text":"Agree one line with your partner, then say it to her together","consequence":"You speak as a team and she hears one clear answer.","outcome":"aligned","best":true},{"text":"Snap at her alone next time it happens","consequence":"A solo snap makes it your fight, not the couple's, and she digs in."}],"debrief":"Align as a couple first, then deliver one warm, united line — not a solo blow-up.","relearn":"Decide together, then say it together: one couple line beats a solo snap.","persona":"Pooja","source":"align then say it"},
  {"id":"fm-1171","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"Relatives ask, every single visit, when you'll have a baby. You're tired of the ambush.","options":[{"text":"Prep one warm, repeatable line with your partner before visits","consequence":"You both answer the same calm way and the topic loses its sting.","outcome":"repeatable","best":true},{"text":"Give a different awkward excuse each time","consequence":"New excuses invite follow-ups and keep you cornered."}],"debrief":"A rehearsed, repeatable line answers the recurring question as a team — no fresh scramble each visit.","relearn":"For a question that repeats, build one repeatable line together — don't improvise.","persona":"Karthik","source":"the repeatable line"},
  {"id":"fm-1172","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"You're moving cities for your job. Your in-laws expect to be told, not asked.","options":[{"text":"Decide together, then share warmly: 'We've decided, and we'd love your blessing'","consequence":"You honour them as family while keeping the couple's call.","outcome":"warm-and-firm","best":true},{"text":"Let them veto the move to keep the peace","consequence":"Handing them a veto trains everyone that the couple doesn't decide."}],"debrief":"Big life calls are the couple's; share them warmly and invite blessing — that honours both.","relearn":"The couple decides its big moves, then shares them with warmth — not a veto.","persona":"any","source":"decide then share"},
  {"id":"fm-1173","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"At dinner your father-in-law corrects your partner harshly in front of everyone. Your partner goes quiet.","options":[{"text":"Gently back them: 'We see it differently, but we'll talk it over'","consequence":"Your partner feels held and the table stays warm.","outcome":"backed","best":true},{"text":"Stay silent so you don't seem disrespectful","consequence":"Going silent leaves your partner exposed and erodes trust."}],"debrief":"Backing your partner warmly in the room isn't choosing sides against family — it's being a team.","relearn":"Hold your partner with a warm, united line; silence in the room exposes them.","persona":"Karthik","source":"back them in the room"},
  {"id":"fm-1174","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"A relative pulls you aside to 'tell you what your partner is really like'. Classic triangulation.","options":[{"text":"Decline it: 'I'd rather hear that with both of us here'","consequence":"You shut the wedge before it splits the couple.","outcome":"no-wedge","best":true},{"text":"Listen and quietly start doubting your partner","consequence":"Taking the secret in plants doubt, just as the wedge intends."}],"debrief":"Refuse triangulation by routing it back to the couple — no secret side-channels about your partner.","relearn":"When someone tries to pit you against your partner, decline the side-channel and keep it open.","persona":"any","source":"refuse the wedge"},
  {"id":"fm-1175","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"You and your partner disagree about a relative in private and it's getting heated.","options":[{"text":"Settle it the two of you, then face the family with one answer","consequence":"You stay a team and the family sees a united, calm front.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Each call your own parents to take your side","consequence":"Recruiting your parents turns two people into four camps."}],"debrief":"Resolve couple disagreements privately, then present one answer — don't outsource the fight to family.","relearn":"Hash out couple disagreements in private; never recruit relatives into them.","persona":"Pooja","source":"settle it privately"},
  {"id":"fm-1176","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"Your in-laws drop in unannounced and it keeps derailing your week. You want a kind fix.","options":[{"text":"Set a warm norm: 'A quick call first means we can host you properly'","consequence":"You get notice without shutting them out.","outcome":"heads-up","best":true},{"text":"Just stop opening the door sometimes","consequence":"Ignoring the door is a cold wall, not a boundary, and it wounds them."}],"debrief":"A kind 'please call first' is a boundary that limits a behaviour without shutting the person out.","relearn":"Ask warmly for a heads-up before visits — a clear norm beats a cold wall.","persona":"Pooja","source":"please call first"},
  {"id":"fm-1177","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"A festival ritual matters deeply to your in-laws but clashes with your work deadline.","options":[{"text":"Offer what you can: join the main puja, step out for the call","consequence":"You honour the tradition and keep your commitment.","outcome":"both-honoured","best":true},{"text":"Drop the work call entirely to avoid friction","consequence":"Erasing your commitment teaches that your work never counts."}],"debrief":"You can join a tradition warmly and opt out of one piece respectfully — a partial yes is a real tool.","relearn":"Honour what you can of a ritual and opt out of one piece kindly — not all-in or all-out.","persona":"Sneha","source":"join in part"},
  {"id":"fm-1178","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"Your partner's family wants to manage your joint savings 'for your own good'.","options":[{"text":"Thank them, keep the call yours: 'We've got a plan we're happy with'","consequence":"You receive the care and decline the overreach.","outcome":"care-not-control","best":true},{"text":"Hand over the passwords to keep everyone happy","consequence":"Giving away control of your money is how a couple loses its footing."}],"debrief":"Your salary and savings are the couple's call; receive the love, decline the overreach — warmly.","relearn":"Money is the couple's call: take the care, keep the control.","persona":"any","source":"care, not control"},
  {"id":"fm-1179","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"Your partner keeps caving to their parents and leaving you to argue alone. You want the pattern to change.","options":[{"text":"Name it kindly in private: 'I need us to decide and hold it together'","consequence":"You fix the team, not just one fight.","outcome":"team-repair","best":true},{"text":"Start caving to your own parents to even the score","consequence":"Matching the caving doubles the problem; nobody is steering."}],"debrief":"When a partner keeps caving, repair the team in private — the fix is alignment.","relearn":"If your partner keeps caving, name it gently and rebuild the team.","persona":"Karthik","source":"fix the team"},
  {"id":"fm-1180","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","hook":"Lensy: a relative keeps 'helping' by redoing your parenting choices. You want to redraw the line, kindly.","options":[{"text":"Affirm the love, hold the line: 'We love that you care — this one's ours'","consequence":"They feel valued and the parenting stays yours.","outcome":"loved-and-held","best":true},{"text":"Let them parent however they like to avoid upset","consequence":"Surrendering your parenting to dodge upset hands away your call."}],"debrief":"Decisions about your children are the couple's; hold that warmly and keep the bond.","relearn":"Your kids are your call — affirm the love and hold the line.","persona":"Pooja","source":"our call as parents"},
  {"id":"fm-1181","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each family moment to the tool that fits it.","pairs":[{"left":"Unsolicited advice you don't want","right":"A warm 'thanks, we'll think about it'"},{"left":"A recurring nosy question","right":"One repeatable team line"},{"left":"A surprise demand at a gathering","right":"'We'll decide and get back to you'"},{"left":"Heated couple disagreement","right":"Settle it privately first"},{"left":"Control, threats, or a dowry demand","right":"Reach a counsellor or Women Helpline 181"}],"relearn":"Each moment has its tool: a warm deflect, a repeatable line, the couple line, private alignment, or help.","persona":"Razia","source":"moment to tool"},
  {"id":"fm-1182","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each tool to exactly what it protects.","pairs":[{"left":"The warm 'no'","right":"Declining without rejecting the person"},{"left":"The pre-visit check-in","right":"Arriving aligned, not split"},{"left":"The repeatable team line","right":"Answering as one, every time"},{"left":"Knowing your family map","right":"Feeling placed, not powerless"},{"left":"The help routes","right":"Safety when friction becomes abuse"}],"relearn":"Each tool guards something: the bond, your alignment, your unity, your sense of place, or your safety.","persona":"any","source":"tool to what it guards"},
  {"id":"fm-1183","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match the family situation to whether it calls for a boundary or for help.","pairs":[{"left":"In-laws drop in unannounced","right":"A kind heads-up boundary"},{"left":"Pressure to host every weekend","right":"A warm, clear 'no' sometimes"},{"left":"Your money is being controlled","right":"A counsellor or Women Helpline 181"},{"left":"A dowry 'gift' is demanded","right":"Shut it down — it's illegal"},{"left":"Threats if you don't obey","right":"Emergency help on 112"}],"relearn":"Friction calls for a boundary; control, dowry demands, and threats call for help — match the right one.","persona":"Razia","source":"boundary or help"},
  {"id":"fm-1184","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each warm 'no' to the overreach it gently declines.","pairs":[{"left":"'We've picked our baby's name, thank you'","right":"Naming your child for you"},{"left":"'We'll holiday just the two of us this year'","right":"Joining every trip uninvited"},{"left":"'We'll manage our own budget'","right":"Taking over your finances"},{"left":"'We'll visit when we can, not weekly'","right":"Demanding a fixed weekly visit"},{"left":"'We'll decide schooling together'","right":"Enrolling your kid without asking"}],"relearn":"A warm 'no' names the overreach and the couple's call in one kind line — repeatable for each one.","persona":"any","source":"warm no to overreach"},
  {"id":"fm-1185","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each persona's moment to the tool that helps them most.","pairs":[{"left":"Pooja, swamped in a joint household","right":"A kind boundary on the load"},{"left":"Sneha, fielding 'settle down' pressure","right":"A warm, repeatable deflect"},{"left":"Karthik, leaving his partner exposed","right":"Backing her warmly in the room"},{"left":"Reshma, money and movement controlled","right":"A private route to a counsellor"},{"left":"A couple facing a surprise demand","right":"'We'll decide and get back to you'"}],"relearn":"The right tool fits the person and the moment — a boundary, a deflect, team-backing, help, or the couple line.","persona":"any","source":"persona to tool"},
  {"id":"fm-1186","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each early step to building your family map.","pairs":[{"left":"Learn who's who and how they relate","right":"See the whole web"},{"left":"Notice each in-law as a person","right":"Move past just roles"},{"left":"Spot which customs differ","right":"Learn, don't judge"},{"left":"Find your own fair space in it","right":"Take your place, don't shrink"},{"left":"Mark where friction tips into abuse","right":"Know when to reach for help"}],"relearn":"Mapping the family means seeing the web, the people, the customs, your place, and the line to help.","persona":"any","source":"build the map"},
  {"id":"fm-1187","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each check-in question to what it helps the couple agree before a visit.","pairs":[{"left":"'What topics might come up?'","right":"Anticipate the pressure points"},{"left":"'What's our line on each one?'","right":"Agree one united answer"},{"left":"'What's off the table today?'","right":"Decide what you won't discuss"},{"left":"'How long do we stay?'","right":"Set a shared exit plan"},{"left":"'What's our signal to leave?'","right":"A quiet cue between you two"}],"relearn":"A pre-visit check-in agrees the topics, the line, the limits, the timing, and a signal — so you arrive as one.","persona":"Pooja","source":"the check-in questions"},
  {"id":"fm-1188","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each unhelpful 'tool' to the healthy move that actually fits.","pairs":[{"left":"Silent treatment","right":"A spoken, warm 'no'"},{"left":"Cutting them off by default","right":"A boundary that keeps the bond"},{"left":"One huge blow-up","right":"Small, consistent limits"},{"left":"Venting to outsiders","right":"Aligning with your partner"},{"left":"Just enduring it forever","right":"Naming it kindly and clearly"}],"relearn":"Misapplied 'tools' damage the bond; the healthy move is warm, spoken, consistent, and aligned.","persona":"any","source":"swap the wrong tool"},
  {"id":"fm-1189","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"Your aunt insists you justify why you and your partner aren't 'settling down properly'. Stay warm and firm.","setup":"Use the line:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"We've thought it through and we're happy with our choices — thanks for caring about us.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Why does everyone keep interrogating me about this?\""}],"relearn":"A warm, firm, repeatable line closes the pressure without a fight — honour the care, hold your choice.","persona":"Sneha","source":"warm and firm"},
  {"id":"fm-1190","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"At a gathering a relative springs a demand on you both. You want the couple line, not a solo yes.","setup":"Say it as a team:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"That's a big one — we'll talk it over together and get back to you.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Um, okay, I guess we can do that.\""}],"relearn":"'We'll talk and get back to you' buys the couple time to decide as one — never a cornered solo yes.","persona":"Karthik","source":"talk and get back"},
  {"id":"fm-1191","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"Your mother-in-law asks you to host the whole family every weekend. You need a warm 'no'.","setup":"Say the warm no:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"We'd love to host once a month — every weekend is just too much for us right now.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Sure, whatever works for everyone, I'll manage somehow.\""}],"relearn":"A warm 'no' gives a kind reason and an alternative — clear, not rude, and never self-erasing.","persona":"Pooja","source":"the warm no"},
  {"id":"fm-1192","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"Your partner asks how you want to handle their family from here. Set the tone together.","setup":"Set the tone:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Let's stay warm with them, decide the big stuff together, and back each other every time.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's just handle each thing as it blows up.\""}],"relearn":"A shared tone — warm, aligned, mutually backed — beats lurching from one blow-up to the next.","persona":"Karthik","source":"set the tone"},
  {"id":"fm-1193","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"A relative tries to get you to gang up on your partner. Decline the side-channel out loud.","setup":"Decline it:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"If there's something about us, let's say it with both of us here — I won't do it behind their back.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Okay, tell me, but don't say I said anything.\""}],"relearn":"Saying 'with both of us here' out loud refuses triangulation and protects the couple's trust.","persona":"any","source":"both of us here"},
  {"id":"fm-1194","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"Your father-in-law gives advice you respect but won't follow. Honour him and keep your call.","setup":"Honour and hold:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Thank you, that really helps us think — we'll weigh it and decide what's right for us.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Fine, we'll do it your way then.\""}],"relearn":"You can honour an elder's advice and still make your own decision — gratitude plus your own call.","persona":"any","source":"honour and decide"},
  {"id":"fm-1195","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"You sense a 'small gift expected' dowry hint creeping in. Shut it down, calmly and clearly.","setup":"Shut it down:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"We're not doing any dowry — it's illegal, and our marriage isn't built on it. Let's drop it.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Maybe a little something would keep the peace?\""}],"relearn":"A dowry hint is shut down, never negotiated — giving, taking and demanding it are all illegal.","persona":"Razia","source":"no dowry, full stop"},
  {"id":"fm-1196","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","hook":"After a tense visit, you and your partner are raw. Open the debrief warmly, as teammates.","setup":"Open the debrief:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"That was a lot. What worked for us, and what do we want to do differently next time?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Your family is always like this, it's exhausting.\""}],"relearn":"A team debrief asks 'what worked, what's next' — it repairs the couple instead of importing the tension.","persona":"Karthik","source":"the team debrief"},
  {"id":"fm-1197","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each move: a tool that protects the bond, or a habit that quietly damages it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Agreeing your line privately before a visit"},{"id":"b","text":"A warm, clear 'no' with a reason"},{"id":"c","text":"Backing your partner in the room"},{"id":"d","text":"Giving the silent treatment for days"},{"id":"e","text":"Venting about in-laws to everyone but them"},{"id":"f","text":"Cutting them off at the first disagreement"}],"bins":[{"id":"tool","label":"Protective tool","valence":"pos"},{"id":"damage","label":"Quietly damaging","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"tool","b":"tool","c":"tool","d":"damage","e":"damage","f":"damage"},"relearn":"Aligning, the warm no and team-backing protect the bond; silence, gossip and snap cut-offs corrode it.","persona":"any","source":"tool or damage"},
  {"id":"fm-1198","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each situation: work it through with a tool, or reach for help?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"In-laws and you clash over festival plans"},{"id":"b","text":"Your partner forgot to back you up once"},{"id":"c","text":"Your phone and money are being controlled"},{"id":"d","text":"A dowry 'gift' is being demanded"},{"id":"e","text":"Disagreement over how often to visit"},{"id":"f","text":"You're threatened if you don't obey"}],"bins":[{"id":"tool","label":"Work it through","valence":"pos"},{"id":"help","label":"Reach for help","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"tool","b":"tool","c":"help","d":"help","e":"tool","f":"help"},"relearn":"Ordinary friction you work through; control, dowry demands and threats are abuse — reach for help.","persona":"Reshma","source":"work it or help"},
  {"id":"fm-1199","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each line: a warm 'no' that keeps the bond, or a harsh 'no' that wounds?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"'We'd love to, just not this weekend'"},{"id":"b","text":"'Stop bothering us about it'"},{"id":"c","text":"'We've decided, but thank you for caring'"},{"id":"d","text":"'Mind your own business'"},{"id":"e","text":"'That one's our call — we hope you understand'"},{"id":"f","text":"'Why can't you ever leave us alone?'"}],"bins":[{"id":"warm","label":"Warm no","valence":"pos"},{"id":"harsh","label":"Harsh no","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"warm","b":"harsh","c":"warm","d":"harsh","e":"warm","f":"harsh"},"relearn":"The same limit can be warm — reason given, person honoured — or harsh; warm keeps the bond intact.","persona":"any","source":"warm or harsh no"},
  {"id":"fm-1200","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each one: a couple's own call, or genuinely shared with the wider family?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"How you spend your salary"},{"id":"b","text":"Whether to have children, and when"},{"id":"c","text":"The date of a shared family festival"},{"id":"d","text":"How to raise your own kids"},{"id":"e","text":"Hosting a joint family ritual together"},{"id":"f","text":"Which city you live in for work"}],"bins":[{"id":"couple","label":"Couple's call","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shared","label":"Genuinely shared","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"couple","b":"couple","c":"shared","d":"couple","e":"shared","f":"couple"},"relearn":"Salary, kids, where you live are the couple's call; shared rituals and festival dates you decide together.","persona":"any","source":"couple or shared"},
  {"id":"fm-1201","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each habit: a green-flag pattern to keep, or one to change?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Talking issues through early and kindly"},{"id":"b","text":"Backing each other in front of family"},{"id":"c","text":"Debriefing gently after tense events"},{"id":"d","text":"Keeping score of every past slight"},{"id":"e","text":"Competing over whose family is 'right'"},{"id":"f","text":"Letting resentment fester in silence"}],"bins":[{"id":"keep","label":"Keep it","valence":"pos"},{"id":"change","label":"Change it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"keep","b":"keep","c":"keep","d":"change","e":"change","f":"change"},"relearn":"Talking early, backing each other and debriefing are keepers; scorekeeping, rivalry and festering need changing.","persona":"any","source":"keep or change"},
  {"id":"fm-1202","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each timing: a heads-up that prevents friction, or a silence that breeds it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Telling in-laws your visit plans early"},{"id":"b","text":"Springing a big decision on them last-minute"},{"id":"c","text":"Agreeing your line before the gathering"},{"id":"d","text":"Bottling up an issue for months"},{"id":"e","text":"Flagging a clash kindly when it's small"},{"id":"f","text":"Saying nothing until you explode"}],"bins":[{"id":"early","label":"Early heads-up","valence":"pos"},{"id":"silence","label":"Festering silence","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"early","b":"silence","c":"early","d":"silence","e":"early","f":"silence"},"relearn":"Early, warm heads-ups prevent friction; springing things late or bottling up breeds it — silence isn't kindness.","persona":"Pooja","source":"early or silence"},
  {"id":"fm-1203","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each one: a sustainable, repeatable move, or a one-off blow-up?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A short check-in before every visit"},{"id":"b","text":"One dramatic confrontation to 'fix it all'"},{"id":"c","text":"The same warm line, used each time"},{"id":"d","text":"Small limits kept consistently"},{"id":"e","text":"A furious group message at midnight"},{"id":"f","text":"Storming out of a function in anger"}],"bins":[{"id":"sustain","label":"Sustainable","valence":"pos"},{"id":"oneoff","label":"One-off blow-up","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"sustain","b":"oneoff","c":"sustain","d":"sustain","e":"oneoff","f":"oneoff"},"relearn":"Consistent check-ins, repeated lines and small limits last; dramatic blow-ups rarely fix a lifelong bond.","persona":"Sneha","source":"sustainable or blow-up"},
  {"id":"fm-1204","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each tool to the job it's actually for.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Pre-visit check-in"},{"id":"b","text":"The warm 'no'"},{"id":"c","text":"The repeatable team line"},{"id":"d","text":"The help routes"},{"id":"e","text":"The family map itself"},{"id":"f","text":"A team debrief after"}],"bins":[{"id":"before","label":"Before & during","valence":"tell"},{"id":"safety","label":"When it's serious","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"before","b":"before","c":"before","d":"safety","e":"before","f":"before"},"relearn":"Most tools shape the everyday — check-in, warm no, team line, map, debrief; help routes are for when it's serious.","persona":"any","source":"which job"},
  {"id":"fm-1205","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"There's nothing you can really do about family dynamics — you just have to endure them.\"","myth":{"un":"There's nothing you can really do about family dynamics — you just have to endure them.","re":"You have real tools — alignment, kind boundaries, repeatable lines and help routes — that shift the dynamic over time.","why":"Family dynamics are workable, not just endurable; you're not powerless in them."},"relearn":"You're not powerless: alignment, boundaries, repeatable lines and help routes genuinely shift the dynamic.","persona":"any","source":"not powerless"},
  {"id":"fm-1206","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Asking a counsellor for help means the family has failed.\"","myth":{"un":"Asking a counsellor for help means the family has failed.","re":"Bringing in a neutral third person is a tool strong families use early, not a verdict that they have failed.","why":"Outside help is a resource you reach for, not proof anything is broken."},"relearn":"Reaching for a counsellor or mediator is a smart tool, not a sign of failure.","persona":"Pooja","source":"help isn't failure"},
  {"id":"fm-1207","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A good couple should just absorb whatever the family throws at them.\"","myth":{"un":"A good couple should just absorb whatever the family throws at them.","re":"A strong couple decides together and answers as one — absorbing everything silently only stores up resentment.","why":"Standing as a team lowers conflict; silently absorbing it corrodes the couple from inside."},"relearn":"A couple isn't a sponge — deciding and answering as one beats silently absorbing everything.","persona":"Karthik","source":"not a sponge"},
  {"id":"fm-1208","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"The warm 'no' is just a polite way of being rude to your elders.\"","myth":{"un":"The warm 'no' is just a polite way of being rude to your elders.","re":"A warm 'no' is kind, clear and reasoned — it honours the person while declining the request, the opposite of rude.","why":"Saying no with warmth and a reason respects the elder and keeps your own voice."},"relearn":"A warm 'no' — kind, clear, reason given — is a learnable tool, not rudeness.","persona":"Sneha","source":"warm no isn't rude"},
  {"id":"fm-1209","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If you're having any family trouble, the tool is always a firmer boundary.\"","myth":{"un":"If you're having any family trouble, the tool is always a firmer boundary.","re":"Boundaries fix friction — but when behaviour is controlling or threatening, the right tool is help, not a bigger boundary.","why":"Abuse isn't a boundary problem; the fix is help and safety, not more adjusting."},"relearn":"Boundaries are for friction; when it's control or threats, the right tool is help, not a firmer boundary.","persona":"Razia","source":"right tool for the moment"},
  {"id":"fm-1210","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Cutting the family off is the cleanest way to protect your marriage.\"","myth":{"un":"Cutting the family off is the cleanest way to protect your marriage.","re":"Kind, consistent boundaries protect the marriage while keeping the family — cutting off by default loses a web worth keeping.","why":"A boundary holds the bond; estrangement is a last resort for real harm, not the everyday tool."},"relearn":"Kind boundaries protect the marriage and keep the family; cutting off isn't the default tool.","persona":"any","source":"boundaries, not cut-off"},
  {"id":"fm-1211","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A couple check-in before a family visit is overthinking it — just go and wing it.\"","myth":{"un":"A couple check-in before a family visit is overthinking it — just go and wing it.","re":"A two-minute check-in agrees your line on the likely topics, so you arrive aligned instead of split in the moment.","why":"Aligning before you face family prevents most blow-ups; winging it leaves you to be divided."},"relearn":"A quick pre-visit check-in isn't overthinking — it's how you arrive aligned instead of split.","persona":"Pooja","source":"check-in, not wing it"},
  {"id":"fm-1212","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you can't control how relatives behave, but your alignment, your boundaries and your warmth are yours. Enough to start with?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["That's enough to start","I can work with that","Those are mine to use"],"affirm":"You can't control relatives, but your alignment, boundaries and warmth are yours — and they're enough to start.","relearn":"Control what's yours — alignment, boundaries and warmth; that's enough to shift the dynamic over time.","persona":"any","source":"what's yours"},
  {"id":"fm-1213","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: which tool do you most want in your pocket for the next family gathering?","prompt":"Pick the one that fits you:","options":["The warm 'no'","The repeatable team line","The pre-visit check-in"],"affirm":"Whichever you pick, it's a real, learnable tool — and you can carry more than one into the room.","relearn":"The warm no, the team line and the check-in are all yours to carry — choose what fits the moment.","persona":"any","source":"pick your tool"},
  {"id":"fm-1214","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: picture saying a warm, firm 'no' to a relative — and the world not ending. How does that sit?","prompt":"How does it feel?","options":["Lighter than I expected","Still a little scary","Doable with practice"],"affirm":"A warm no feels lighter once you've said it — and it gets easier each time you use the same kind line.","relearn":"The warm no feels big the first time and ordinary by the tenth — it's a skill that grows with use.","persona":"Sneha","source":"saying the no"},
  {"id":"fm-1215","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: knowing one calm line, one trusted person and one helpline number is a kit you can carry into any hard family moment. Feel ready to pack it?","prompt":"What's your read?","options":["I'll pack it","One line, one person, one number","Carry it anywhere"],"affirm":"A steady line, a trusted person and a saved helpline are a small kit that travels with you into any tense moment.","relearn":"Your portable kit is one calm line, one trusted person and one saved helpline number.","persona":"any","source":"pack the kit"},
  {"id":"fm-1216","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: think of one thing you and your partner could agree to back each other on, every time. What comes up?","prompt":"What's on your mind?","options":["Our big decisions","Saying no to overreach","Not splitting in the room"],"affirm":"Whatever you name, agreeing to back each other on it is exactly what makes you a team family can rely on.","relearn":"Pick one thing to always back each other on — that agreement is the heart of the couple team.","persona":"Karthik","source":"back each other on"},
  {"id":"fm-1217","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a tool keeps a relationship healthy — but help is the tool when it turns harmful. Does that line feel clear to you?","prompt":"Where are you with it?","options":["It's clear","Clearer now","I'll hold onto that"],"affirm":"Boundaries and check-ins keep things healthy; when it's control or threats, reaching for help is the right move.","relearn":"Tools keep a relationship healthy; when behaviour is abusive, the right tool is help — not another boundary.","persona":"Reshma","source":"tool vs help"},
  {"id":"fm-1218","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: which feels harder for you right now — the warm 'no', or staying a united team in the room?","prompt":"Sit with it:","options":["The warm 'no'","Staying a team","Both, honestly"],"affirm":"Naming which is harder is the first step — and both get easier with a partner and a little practice.","relearn":"Whichever is harder, naming it lets you practise it on purpose, together.","persona":"any","source":"which is harder"},
  {"id":"fm-1219","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that quietly damage a lifelong family bond.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Small, warm boundaries kept consistently","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"One huge confrontation to 'sort it all out'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Aligning as a couple before each visit","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Giving relatives the silent treatment for weeks","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Assuming good intent where you can","trick":false}],"why":"A big blow-up and weeks of silent treatment damage the bond; warm boundaries and alignment sustain it.","relearn":"Sustainable family navigation is consistent warm boundaries and alignment — not blow-ups or silence.","persona":"Sneha","source":"two damaging moves"},
  {"id":"fm-1220","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that are a harsh 'no', not a warm one.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'We'd love to, just not this weekend'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'Mind your own business for once'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'That one's our call — thanks for caring'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'Stop nagging us about it, seriously'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'We've decided, but we hope you understand'","trick":false}],"why":"'Mind your own business' and 'stop nagging' wound the person; a warm no gives a reason and honours them.","relearn":"A warm no keeps the bond — reason given, person honoured; a harsh no just wounds.","persona":"any","source":"spot the harsh no"},
  {"id":"fm-1221","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that leave your partner exposed instead of backing them.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'We see it differently, but we'll talk it over'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Going silent while they're criticised at the table","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Quietly agreeing your line beforehand","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Siding with your parents against them","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Holding a united, warm front together","trick":false}],"why":"Going silent and siding with your parents leave your partner alone; backing them warmly keeps the team.","relearn":"Back your partner in the room — silence and taking the family's side break the team's trust.","persona":"Karthik","source":"spot what exposes them"},
  {"id":"fm-1222","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two situations that need help, not just another boundary.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"In-laws disagree with your festival plans","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Your money and phone are being controlled","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"A debate over how often you visit","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"A dowry 'gift' is being demanded","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Different cooking customs to get used to","trick":false}],"why":"Controlled money and a dowry demand are abuse — reach for help; the rest are ordinary friction to work through.","relearn":"Control over money and a dowry demand are abuse and need help; friction over plans and customs you work through.","persona":"Razia","source":"spot what needs help"},
  {"id":"fm-1223","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two 'tools' that are really triangulation traps to refuse.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Deciding privately, then answering as one","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Carrying a relative's secret complaint to your partner","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Asking to hear concerns with both present","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Letting a relative talk you against your partner","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Keeping side-channels out of the couple","trick":false}],"why":"Carrying secret complaints and being turned against your partner are triangulation; keeping it open refuses it.","relearn":"Refuse triangulation: no secret side-deals, no being turned against your partner — keep it open.","persona":"any","source":"spot the wedge"},
  {"id":"fm-1224","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that import family tension into the couple itself.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Debriefing gently: what worked, what's next","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Blaming each other for how the event went","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Assuming you're on the same side","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Keeping score of whose family behaved worse","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Repairing quickly after a clash","trick":false}],"why":"Blaming each other and keeping family score turn the family's tension into your own; debriefing repairs the couple.","relearn":"Debrief and repair as a team; blaming each other and family scorekeeping import the tension into the couple.","persona":"Pooja","source":"spot what imports tension"},
  {"id":"fm-1225","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two responses that mistake a warm 'no' for surrender.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'We'll host once a month, not every weekend'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'Sure, whatever everyone wants, I'll manage'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'We've picked our baby's name, thank you'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'Okay, I guess we'll just do it your way'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'We'll decide schooling together as parents'","trick":false}],"why":"'Whatever everyone wants' and 'we'll do it your way' erase the couple's call; a warm no keeps it while staying kind.","relearn":"A warm no holds the couple's call kindly; caving with 'whatever you want' just erases your own voice.","persona":"any","source":"spot the surrender"},
  {"id":"fm-1226","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two signs this has crossed from friction into something that needs help.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"You disagree about visiting frequency","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"You're isolated from your own friends and family","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"You're adjusting to new household customs","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"You're threatened if you don't comply","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"You're learning who's who in a big family","trick":false}],"why":"Isolation and threats are coercive control — abuse that needs help; the rest are ordinary friction.","relearn":"Isolation and threats are abuse — reach for help; disagreeing, adjusting and learning are friction.","persona":"Reshma","source":"spot the line crossed"},
  {"id":"fm-1260","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Marry the right person and the family part takes care of itself.\"","myth":{"un":"Marry the right person and the family part takes care of itself.","re":"You join their whole family too; those ties take real, ongoing effort, not luck.","why":"A good partner doesn't replace the work of building family relationships."},"relearn":"A loving partner is the start, not a shortcut past learning the wider family.","persona":"Pooja","source":"effort not luck"},
  {"id":"fm-1261","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Once you marry in, your own family stops being your family.\"","myth":{"un":"Once you marry in, your own family stops being your family.","re":"You gain a family without losing yours; both can stay part of your life.","why":"Joining a new web doesn't erase the one you came from."},"relearn":"Marriage adds a family to your web; it doesn't delete the one you grew up in.","persona":"Sneha","source":"keep both"},
  {"id":"fm-1262","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A daughter-in-law should know the family's ways from day one.\"","myth":{"un":"A daughter-in-law should know the family's ways from day one.","re":"Nobody arrives knowing a new family's rhythms; learning them takes time, and asking is fine.","why":"Customs are learned by living them, not absorbed instantly on the wedding day."},"relearn":"Learning a new family's ways takes time; not knowing on day one is normal, not a failing.","persona":"Pooja","source":"learning takes time"},
  {"id":"fm-1263","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A son-in-law is just a guest; he doesn't really join her family.\"","myth":{"un":"A son-in-law is just a guest; he doesn't really join her family.","re":"He joins her family too — building real ties there, not just visiting as a guest.","why":"Joining a family goes both ways; the husband joins her side as well."},"relearn":"A husband joins his wife's family for real; he's not a permanent guest there.","persona":"Karthik","source":"he joins too"},
  {"id":"fm-1264","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If you have to work at liking your in-laws, something's wrong.\"","myth":{"un":"If you have to work at liking your in-laws, something's wrong.","re":"Most family bonds are built, not instant; effort early on is normal, not a bad sign.","why":"Relationships grow through time and small gestures, not on first sight."},"relearn":"Warmth with in-laws is usually built over time; needing effort isn't a red flag.","persona":"any","source":"built not instant"},
  {"id":"fm-1265","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Your in-laws are just roles — the saas, the nanad — not people.\"","myth":{"un":"Your in-laws are just roles — the saas, the nanad — not people.","re":"Each in-law is an individual with their own story; the roles are only a starting label.","why":"Real relationships form with people, not with the titles they hold."},"relearn":"In-laws are individuals to get to know, not just roles to impress or fear.","persona":"any","source":"people not roles"},
  {"id":"fm-1266","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A close family means everyone always thinks the same way.\"","myth":{"un":"A close family means everyone always thinks the same way.","re":"Closeness holds plenty of differences; people can disagree and still belong together.","why":"Belonging isn't sameness; healthy families make room for different views."},"relearn":"You can join a close family and still hold your own views — closeness isn't sameness.","persona":"any","source":"closeness not sameness"},
  {"id":"fm-1267","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Both families have to drop their own customs and follow just one.\"","myth":{"un":"Both families have to drop their own customs and follow just one.","re":"Two families can keep their own ways and still celebrate together with respect.","why":"Different customs can sit side by side; one side needn't erase the other."},"relearn":"Different family customs are things to honour side by side, not to rank or replace.","persona":"any","source":"side by side"},
  {"id":"fm-1268","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Settling in means becoming exactly like your new family.\"","myth":{"un":"Settling in means becoming exactly like your new family.","re":"You take your fair place as yourself; fitting in isn't erasing who you are.","why":"A family web has room for your own personality, not just a copy of theirs."},"relearn":"Finding your place means taking your fair space as yourself, not dissolving into the family.","persona":"Pooja","source":"yourself in the web"},
  {"id":"fm-1269","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"In a joint family, the couple has no separate life of its own.\"","myth":{"un":"In a joint family, the couple has no separate life of its own.","re":"You can live within a joint family and still have a shared life that's yours as a couple.","why":"Belonging to the bigger household doesn't cancel the couple's own bond and choices."},"relearn":"Even inside a joint family, the couple gets a life and a few choices that are its own.","persona":"Karthik","source":"couple within the joint"},
  {"id":"fm-1270","cat":"web-you-join","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Your spouse's relatives are your problem to win over alone.\"","myth":{"un":"Your spouse's relatives are your problem to win over alone.","re":"You build those ties together; your partner helps you map and meet their family.","why":"Joining a family is a shared project, not a solo audition for approval."},"relearn":"You meet a new family together; winning everyone over isn't a solo job.","persona":"Pooja","source":"together not solo"},
  {"id":"fm-1271","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: in your everyday web, or a wider circle you'll meet rarely?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"In-laws you share a home or city with"},{"id":"b","text":"A distant relative abroad you've never met"},{"id":"c","text":"Your partner's sibling who visits often"},{"id":"d","text":"A great-uncle seen once a decade"},{"id":"e","text":"The cousin who lives next door"},{"id":"f","text":"A relative you meet only at big weddings"}],"bins":[{"id":"every","label":"Everyday web","valence":"pos"},{"id":"wider","label":"Wider, rarer circle","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"every","b":"wider","c":"every","d":"wider","e":"every","f":"wider"},"relearn":"Some in-laws are your daily web; others a wider circle you meet now and then — both real, but different effort.","persona":"any","source":"daily vs distant"},
  {"id":"fm-1272","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a fair way to learn a new family, or an unfair burden to put on yourself?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Asking your partner who's who"},{"id":"b","text":"Pretending you already know every name"},{"id":"c","text":"Learning one custom at a time"},{"id":"d","text":"Memorising every ritual before the wedding"},{"id":"e","text":"Letting some closeness grow slowly"},{"id":"f","text":"Being everyone's favourite by week one"}],"bins":[{"id":"fair","label":"Fair on yourself","valence":"pos"},{"id":"unfair","label":"Unfair burden","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"fair","b":"unfair","c":"fair","d":"unfair","e":"fair","f":"unfair"},"relearn":"Asking, learning slowly and letting closeness grow are fair; pretending to know it all or winning everyone instantly is an unfair load.","persona":"Pooja","source":"fair learning"},
  {"id":"fm-1273","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a sign you're building real ties, or just performing the 'perfect' new spouse?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Asking a relative about their life"},{"id":"b","text":"Saying yes to everything to be liked"},{"id":"c","text":"Remembering what matters to them"},{"id":"d","text":"Hiding your real opinions to seem ideal"},{"id":"e","text":"Sharing a little of yourself too"},{"id":"f","text":"Exhausting yourself to win approval"}],"bins":[{"id":"real","label":"Building real ties","valence":"pos"},{"id":"perform","label":"Just performing","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"real","b":"perform","c":"real","d":"perform","e":"real","f":"perform"},"relearn":"Curiosity and sharing yourself build real bonds; saying yes to everything and hiding your views is just performing.","persona":"any","source":"real vs perform"},
  {"id":"fm-1274","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: both partners joining each other's families, or the old one-way idea?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"He learns her parents' ways too"},{"id":"b","text":"Only she has to fit in"},{"id":"c","text":"He stays in touch with her siblings"},{"id":"d","text":"Her family is 'not really his'"},{"id":"e","text":"They visit both homes warmly"},{"id":"f","text":"Adjusting is the wife's job alone"}],"bins":[{"id":"both","label":"Both ways","valence":"pos"},{"id":"oneway","label":"Old one-way idea","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"both","b":"oneway","c":"both","d":"oneway","e":"both","f":"oneway"},"relearn":"Both partners join each other's families; the wife-only 'adjusting' idea is the outdated one.","persona":"Karthik","source":"both join"},
  {"id":"fm-1275","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a healthy way two families relate, or a sign someone's being erased?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Each family keeps its own festivals"},{"id":"b","text":"One side's customs are called 'wrong'"},{"id":"c","text":"They blend a few traditions by choice"},{"id":"d","text":"Your family's ways are mocked"},{"id":"e","text":"Both sides are spoken of with respect"},{"id":"f","text":"You're told to forget where you came from"}],"bins":[{"id":"healthy","label":"Healthy blend","valence":"pos"},{"id":"erased","label":"Someone erased","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"healthy","b":"erased","c":"healthy","d":"erased","e":"healthy","f":"erased"},"relearn":"Two families can stay distinct and respectful; mocking or erasing one side isn't 'becoming close'.","persona":"any","source":"blend not erase"},
  {"id":"fm-1276","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a tie that's genuinely yours now, or someone outside your family web?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Your partner's parents"},{"id":"b","text":"Your partner's old college friend"},{"id":"c","text":"Your sister-in-law"},{"id":"d","text":"A coworker of your spouse"},{"id":"e","text":"Your partner's grandmother"},{"id":"f","text":"A face from your partner's feed"}],"bins":[{"id":"yours","label":"Family now","valence":"pos"},{"id":"outside","label":"Outside the web","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"yours","b":"outside","c":"yours","d":"outside","e":"yours","f":"outside"},"relearn":"Your partner's close relatives become your family; their friends, coworkers and online faces don't.","persona":"any","source":"family vs friends"},
  {"id":"fm-1277","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a kind first move toward a new in-law, or a way to keep them at arm's length?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Asking about their day"},{"id":"b","text":"Only ever speaking when spoken to"},{"id":"c","text":"Offering to help in the kitchen"},{"id":"d","text":"Staying glued to your phone at visits"},{"id":"e","text":"Remembering a small thing they like"},{"id":"f","text":"Treating every visit as a chore"}],"bins":[{"id":"warm","label":"Warm first move","valence":"pos"},{"id":"distant","label":"Arm's length","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"warm","b":"distant","c":"warm","d":"distant","e":"warm","f":"distant"},"relearn":"Small, genuine gestures open a new tie; silence and distance keep it cold.","persona":"any","source":"warm openers"},
  {"id":"fm-1278","cat":"web-you-join","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a realistic timeline for a new family bond, or an instant-result fantasy?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Feeling at ease after many visits"},{"id":"b","text":"Being 'one of them' within a week"},{"id":"c","text":"Inside jokes forming over a year"},{"id":"d","text":"Total trust on the wedding night"},{"id":"e","text":"Trust deepening with shared moments"},{"id":"f","text":"Everyone confiding in you at once"}],"bins":[{"id":"realtime","label":"Real timeline","valence":"pos"},{"id":"instant","label":"Instant fantasy","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"realtime","b":"instant","c":"realtime","d":"instant","e":"realtime","f":"instant"},"relearn":"Ease, inside jokes and trust grow over months and years; instant belonging is a fantasy.","persona":"any","source":"timeline"},
  {"id":"fm-1279","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"At your first big family function, you barely know who's who.","options":[{"text":"Ask your partner to quietly point out the key people","consequence":"You start putting names to faces and feel more grounded.","outcome":"grounded","best":true},{"text":"Hide in a corner and avoid everyone all evening","consequence":"Hiding all night leaves you more of a stranger than when you arrived."}],"debrief":"A quiet who's-who from your partner turns a sea of strangers into a map you can read.","relearn":"Lean on your partner to learn the family web; you don't have to figure it out alone.","persona":"Pooja","source":"first function"},
  {"id":"fm-1280","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"Your wife's parents invite you to help with a ritual you don't fully know.","options":[{"text":"Join in and ask what each step means","consequence":"You join her family for real and they warm to your effort.","outcome":"joined","best":true},{"text":"Hang back, calling it 'her family's thing'","consequence":"Treating her family as not-yours keeps you a guest, not one of them."}],"debrief":"A husband joins his wife's family too; leaning in is how those ties become real.","relearn":"Both partners join each other's families; showing up at her family's rituals builds your place.","persona":"Karthik","source":"join her side"},
  {"id":"fm-1281","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"Your mother-in-law cooks differently from your mother, and you keep comparing.","options":[{"text":"Treat it as a new way to learn; ask her to teach you a dish","consequence":"Curiosity turns a difference into a shared moment.","outcome":"curious","best":true},{"text":"Decide your mother's way is 'right' and quietly judge","consequence":"Silent judging builds a wall where a warm question could build a bond."}],"debrief":"Different isn't wrong; asking to learn a new family's ways beats ranking them against your own.","relearn":"Different family customs are things to learn, not proof one side is better.","persona":"Pooja","source":"different cooking"},
  {"id":"fm-1282","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"You feel pressure to be everyone's instant favourite in your new joint family.","options":[{"text":"Let closeness grow at its own pace, one relationship at a time","consequence":"Real bonds form slowly and you stop running yourself ragged.","outcome":"paced","best":true},{"text":"Bend over backwards for everyone at once to win them all fast","consequence":"Chasing instant approval everywhere just burns you out, with shallow ties."}],"debrief":"Joining a family is built over time; you can't, and needn't, win everyone at once.","relearn":"Family bonds grow at their own pace; instant universal approval isn't the goal.","persona":"Pooja","source":"not instant favourite"},
  {"id":"fm-1283","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"A relative keeps calling you only 'the new bahu', never your name.","options":[{"text":"Warmly share a bit of yourself so they meet the person","consequence":"They start to see you, not just the role you walked in as.","outcome":"seen","best":true},{"text":"Decide that's all you'll ever be and stop trying","consequence":"Giving up keeps you a label; a little of yourself invites a real tie."}],"debrief":"You're an individual joining a family, not just a role; let them know the real you.","relearn":"In-laws meet you as a role at first; sharing yourself turns the label into a relationship.","persona":"any","source":"beyond the role"},
  {"id":"fm-1284","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"Your partner's family does festivals very differently from yours.","options":[{"text":"Honour both ways — theirs, with yours added in too","consequence":"Both families feel respected and you start a tradition that's yours.","outcome":"both","best":true},{"text":"Insist your family's way is the only proper one","consequence":"Insisting one side is 'proper' makes the other feel erased and picks a fight."}],"debrief":"Two families can keep their own ways and still celebrate together; blending beats ranking.","relearn":"Different customs can sit side by side; you can honour both families' ways.","persona":"any","source":"two festivals"},
  {"id":"fm-1285","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"In the joint family you've stopped speaking up at all to keep peace.","options":[{"text":"Gently take your fair space; share your view kindly","consequence":"You stay yourself and they get to know the real you.","outcome":"present","best":true},{"text":"Keep shrinking and silent so nobody is bothered","consequence":"Shrinking to vanish doesn't build a place; it just makes you smaller."}],"debrief":"Finding your place means taking your fair space, not disappearing to avoid all friction.","relearn":"Finding your place means taking up your fair space, not shrinking yourself to fit.","persona":"Pooja","source":"take your space"},
  {"id":"fm-1286","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"You realise you've been so busy impressing your in-laws you don't actually know them.","options":[{"text":"Get curious about them as people — their stories, what they love","consequence":"Real conversations start and the relationships finally feel two-way.","outcome":"curious","best":true},{"text":"Keep performing the flawless new spouse and hope it's enough","consequence":"Performing perfection exhausts you and still leaves you strangers."}],"debrief":"In-laws are individuals to know, not an audience to impress; curiosity builds real bonds.","relearn":"Get to know in-laws as people, not just roles to win over.","persona":"any","source":"know them"},
  {"id":"fm-1287","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"Your spouse's grandmother seems distant; you wonder if she dislikes you.","options":[{"text":"Keep showing up with small, patient warmth","consequence":"Over time she softens, on her own timeline, not forced.","outcome":"patient","best":true},{"text":"Push for closeness and read her reserve as rejection","consequence":"Forcing it and assuming rejection strains a tie that just needed time."}],"debrief":"Some bonds open slowly; patient, low-pressure warmth lets a reserved elder come around.","relearn":"New ties start best with patience and small gestures, not forced or instant closeness.","persona":"any","source":"reserved elder"},
  {"id":"fm-1288","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"You moved cities to your partner's family home and feel like an outsider.","options":[{"text":"Ask your partner to help you learn the household's rhythms","consequence":"You find your footing and a place that feels yours too.","outcome":"footing","best":true},{"text":"Wait silently for someone to make you feel at home","consequence":"Waiting in silence keeps you on the edge; learning draws you in."}],"debrief":"Finding your footing in a new household is built with your partner, not waited for.","relearn":"Map the home's rhythms with your partner; that's how an outsider joins the web.","persona":"Pooja","source":"new household"},
  {"id":"fm-1289","cat":"web-you-join","type":"branch","hook":"Your partner barely knows your family — 'they married you, not them'.","options":[{"text":"Invite them in warmly so they join your side too","consequence":"They build real ties with your people and your worlds connect.","outcome":"connected","best":true},{"text":"Agree it doesn't matter; keep your family distant","consequence":"Keeping your partner away leaves half your web unjoined."}],"debrief":"Both partners join each other's families; your spouse joining your side matters too.","relearn":"Both partners join each other's families; bringing your spouse into yours is part of the web.","persona":"Karthik","source":"your side too"},
  {"id":"fm-1290","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each new relative to a simple way to start knowing them.","pairs":[{"left":"A grandparent-in-law","right":"Ask them to share an old family story"},{"left":"A foodie aunt-in-law","right":"Ask her to teach you a family recipe"},{"left":"A cricket-loving uncle","right":"Watch a match together sometime"},{"left":"A shy teenage cousin","right":"Keep it light, no pressure to bond"},{"left":"A busy sister-in-law","right":"A short, warm message now and then"}],"relearn":"Each in-law opens up to a different small, genuine gesture suited to who they are.","persona":"any","source":"start with each"},
  {"id":"fm-1291","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each myth about joining a family to the truth that replaces it.","pairs":[{"left":"Only the wife adjusts","right":"Both partners join each other's families"},{"left":"You must love everyone at once","right":"Bonds are built slowly over time"},{"left":"Their way is just wrong","right":"Different customs are things to learn"},{"left":"Two families must become one","right":"They can stay distinct and still be close"},{"left":"In-laws are only roles","right":"They are individuals to get to know"}],"relearn":"Each tired myth about marrying into a family has a kinder, truer reality behind it.","persona":"any","source":"myth to truth"},
  {"id":"fm-1292","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each part of the wider web to roughly how often you'll really see them.","pairs":[{"left":"In-laws you live near","right":"Part of everyday life"},{"left":"A sibling-in-law in another city","right":"Calls and the big occasions"},{"left":"Festival-only relatives","right":"A few warm times a year"},{"left":"A cousin-in-law abroad","right":"Mostly weddings and video calls"},{"left":"A great-aunt you rarely meet","right":"The occasional respectful visit"}],"relearn":"The family web has near ties and far ones; knowing which is which sets fair expectations.","persona":"any","source":"near and far"},
  {"id":"fm-1293","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each warm habit to the new tie it helps build.","pairs":[{"left":"Remembering a birthday","right":"Shows a relative they matter to you"},{"left":"Asking about their health","right":"Turns a greeting into real care"},{"left":"Joining one family ritual","right":"Signals you want to belong"},{"left":"Sharing a bit of your own world","right":"Lets them know you back"},{"left":"A patient, unforced hello","right":"Opens a guarded relative gently"}],"relearn":"Small, repeated warmth — not grand gestures — is what slowly knits you into a family.","persona":"any","source":"warm habits"},
  {"id":"fm-1294","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each new term you'll hear to who it points to in the web.","pairs":[{"left":"Saas","right":"Your mother-in-law"},{"left":"Sasur","right":"Your father-in-law"},{"left":"Nanad","right":"Your husband's sister"},{"left":"Devar","right":"Your husband's younger brother"},{"left":"Jeth","right":"Your husband's elder brother"}],"relearn":"Learning who each family term points to is part of mapping the web you've joined.","persona":"Pooja","source":"who's who terms"},
  {"id":"fm-1295","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each realistic hope to why it's fair to expect.","pairs":[{"left":"Warmth growing over years","right":"Bonds are built, not instant"},{"left":"Mutual respect from the start","right":"Respect can be offered on day one"},{"left":"Learning customs slowly","right":"Nobody knows a new family at once"},{"left":"Keeping your own voice","right":"You take your fair space, not none"},{"left":"Honouring both families' ways","right":"Two sides can stay distinct and close"}],"relearn":"Fair hopes for a new family rest on truths: bonds are built, respect is mutual, you stay yourself.","persona":"any","source":"fair hopes why"},
  {"id":"fm-1296","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each thing to whose call it gently is as you join the family.","pairs":[{"left":"Whether you call an aunt 'didi'","right":"Yours, as you settle in"},{"left":"Learning a family festival","right":"Something you and your partner share"},{"left":"How fast you grow close to each in-law","right":"Set by the relationship's own pace"},{"left":"Which relatives are 'your web' now","right":"Your partner's close family, by marriage"},{"left":"Keeping ties to your own parents","right":"Always still yours to hold"}],"relearn":"Joining a family still leaves room for your own pace, your own ties and a few of your own calls.","persona":"any","source":"whose call"},
  {"id":"fm-1297","cat":"web-you-join","type":"match","hook":"Match each early in-law moment to a kind way to handle it.","pairs":[{"left":"You forget a relative's name","right":"Smile and ask again, warmly"},{"left":"A custom confuses you","right":"Quietly ask your partner later"},{"left":"An elder offers strong advice","right":"Thank them, decide together after"},{"left":"You feel shy at a big gathering","right":"Stay close to your partner at first"},{"left":"A relative tests you a little","right":"Stay warm; trust is built over time"}],"relearn":"Awkward early moments are normal; warmth, honesty and your partner's help carry you through.","persona":"any","source":"early moments"},
  {"id":"fm-1298","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: marrying someone means joining a whole web of relatives, and being joined to yours. Sit with that for a second.","prompt":"What comes up?","options":["A lot to take in","Kind of exciting","Makes sense"],"affirm":"You marry into a family, not just a person — and that web becomes part of your life either way.","relearn":"Marriage joins two families, not just two people; the web is real whichever way you feel about it.","persona":"any","source":"the whole web"},
  {"id":"fm-1299","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you don't have to love every new relative on day one. Warmth can grow slowly. How does that sit?","prompt":"Your honest reaction?","options":["Relieved","Still nervous","That's fair"],"affirm":"Family bonds are built over time; letting them grow slowly is normal, not a failing.","relearn":"Joining a family is building relationships over time, not instant, automatic love.","persona":"any","source":"grows slowly"},
  {"id":"fm-1300","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: both of you are joining a new family — it isn't a one-way, wife-only job. What do you think?","prompt":"How does that land?","options":["Long overdue","Agree","Hadn't framed it that way"],"affirm":"Both partners join each other's families; adjusting goes both ways, and that's healthy.","relearn":"Both partners join each other's families; adjusting isn't a one-way, wife-only job.","persona":"Karthik","source":"both of you"},
  {"id":"fm-1301","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: your new family's ways aren't 'wrong' just because they differ from yours — they're new things to learn. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","Worth trying","Easier said than done"],"affirm":"Different family customs are things to learn, not proof that one side is wrong.","relearn":"Different family ways are things to learn, not proof that one side is wrong.","persona":"any","source":"new to learn"},
  {"id":"fm-1302","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you can keep your own family ties and still fully join your partner's. You don't have to choose. Sound right?","prompt":"How do you feel?","options":["Reassuring","Yes, both","I needed to hear that"],"affirm":"You gain a family without losing your own; both can stay part of your web.","relearn":"Marriage adds a family to your web without deleting the one you grew up in.","persona":"Sneha","source":"keep both ties"},
  {"id":"fm-1303","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: two families can stay distinct, with their own ways, and still be genuinely close. Does that feel true to you?","prompt":"Your view?","options":["Feels true","Hope so","Refreshing"],"affirm":"Closeness doesn't need sameness; families can keep their own ways and still be close.","relearn":"Families can stay distinct and still be close; merging into sameness isn't the goal.","persona":"any","source":"distinct and close"},
  {"id":"fm-1304","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: each in-law is a person with a whole story, not just a title to manage. Worth getting curious about?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Definitely","Curious now","Hadn't thought of it"],"affirm":"In-laws are individuals to get to know, not just roles to impress.","relearn":"In-laws are individuals to get to know, not just roles to win over.","persona":"any","source":"people with stories"},
  {"id":"fm-1305","cat":"web-you-join","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you build your place in the new family with your partner — it's a shared project, not a solo audition. How's that?","prompt":"Your honest take?","options":["Less alone","Agree","Good to remember"],"affirm":"Joining a family is something you and your partner do together; you aren't auditioning alone.","relearn":"You meet a new family together; winning your place isn't a solo job.","persona":"Pooja","source":"shared project"},
  {"id":"fm-1306","cat":"web-you-join","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two unfair expectations someone might put on a new daughter-in-law.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Time to learn the family's ways","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Knowing every custom on day one","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"A warm welcome as she settles in","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Being everyone's favourite immediately","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Space to ask who's who","trick":false}],"why":"Knowing every custom at once and being an instant favourite are unfair loads; time, welcome and space are fair.","relearn":"Learning a new family takes time; instant mastery and instant adoration are unfair to expect.","persona":"Pooja","source":"unfair on the bahu"},
  {"id":"fm-1307","cat":"web-you-join","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two myths about marrying into a family — the lines that aren't true.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"You join their wider family too","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"You marry a person, not a family","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Both partners join each other's families","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Only the wife ever has to adjust","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"The relatives become part of your web","trick":false}],"why":"'You marry a person, not a family' and 'only the wife adjusts' are the myths; you join a family, both ways.","relearn":"You join a family, not just a person, and both partners adjust — those are the truths.","persona":"Karthik","source":"two myths"},
  {"id":"fm-1308","cat":"web-you-join","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that treat a different custom as 'wrong' instead of new.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Their festival has its own lovely rhythm","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Their way of doing it is just backward","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Worth asking what each step means","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Our family does it the only proper way","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"A new custom I can learn over time","trick":false}],"why":"Calling their way 'backward' or yours 'the only proper way' judges instead of learns; different isn't wrong.","relearn":"Different family customs are things to learn, not proof one side is wrong or backward.","persona":"any","source":"different not wrong spot"},
  {"id":"fm-1309","cat":"web-you-join","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that wrongly demand you erase yourself to fit the family.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Take your fair space in the home","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Forget where you came from now","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Share a little of yourself too","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Never voice your own opinion again","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Keep your own ties to your parents","trick":false}],"why":"'Forget where you came from' and 'never voice your opinion' demand erasure; finding your place isn't shrinking.","relearn":"Finding your place means taking your fair space, not erasing yourself to fit the family.","persona":"Pooja","source":"don't erase"},
  {"id":"fm-1310","cat":"web-you-join","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that mistake performing for actually building a bond.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Asking a relative about their life","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Saying yes to everything to be liked","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Remembering what matters to them","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Hiding all your real views to seem ideal","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Letting them know the real you","trick":false}],"why":"Saying yes to everything and hiding your views is performing; curiosity and honesty build the real tie.","relearn":"Real bonds come from curiosity and being yourself, not from performing the 'perfect' new spouse.","persona":"any","source":"perform vs build spot"},
  {"id":"fm-1311","cat":"web-you-join","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that wrongly expect instant closeness with new in-laws.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Warmth that grows over many visits","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Best friends with everyone by week one","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Trust deepening through shared moments","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Owed everyone's full confidence at once","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Patience with a reserved relative","trick":false}],"why":"'Best friends by week one' and 'owed full confidence at once' expect instant closeness; bonds are built slowly.","relearn":"Closeness with in-laws grows over time; instant friendship and instant trust aren't owed.","persona":"any","source":"instant closeness spot"},
  {"id":"fm-1312","cat":"web-you-join","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that reduce an in-law to a role instead of a person.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Asking your father-in-law about his work","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"She's just the saas, here to be managed","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Learning what your sister-in-law loves","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"He's only the sasur, nothing more to know","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Hearing a grandparent's old stories","trick":false}],"why":"Treating someone as 'just the saas' or 'only the sasur' flattens a person to a role; in-laws are individuals.","relearn":"In-laws are individuals to get to know, not just roles to manage or impress.","persona":"any","source":"role not person spot"},
  {"id":"fm-1313","cat":"web-you-join","type":"role-play","hook":"A new aunt-in-law asks what your own family's traditions are like. You want to honour both.","setup":"Answer warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"We do it a little differently at home — I'd love to share, and learn yours too.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Oh, ours don't really matter now.\""}],"relearn":"Honouring both families' ways — sharing yours and learning theirs — builds the bond without erasing you.","persona":"any","source":"both traditions"},
  {"id":"fm-1314","cat":"web-you-join","type":"role-play","hook":"You've forgotten a relative's name at a function and they've noticed. You want to recover kindly.","setup":"Say it warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I'm so sorry, I'm still learning everyone — remind me your name?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Uh… hi, you.\""}],"relearn":"A warm, honest 'I'm still learning everyone' turns a slip into a friendly moment.","persona":"Pooja","source":"forgot the name"},
  {"id":"fm-1315","cat":"web-you-join","type":"role-play","hook":"Your husband hasn't met your parents much. You want to bring him into your family too.","setup":"Say it warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Come, let me introduce you properly — they're your family now as well.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You don't really need to know them.\""}],"relearn":"Both partners join each other's families; inviting your spouse into your side is part of the web.","persona":"Karthik","source":"bring him in"},
  {"id":"fm-1316","cat":"web-you-join","type":"role-play","hook":"A mother-in-law makes a dish a new way to you. You want to show curiosity, not judgement.","setup":"Say it warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"This is new to me and it's lovely — would you teach me how you make it?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"We make it the proper way at my house.\""}],"relearn":"Curiosity treats a different custom as new to learn, not as wrong — and it opens the relationship.","persona":"any","source":"teach me the dish"},
  {"id":"fm-1317","cat":"web-you-join","type":"role-play","hook":"Your father-in-law starts telling a long story about the family's past. You want to connect.","setup":"Respond warmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I'd really like to hear it — tell me how it all started.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Maybe some other time, I'm busy.\""}],"relearn":"Listening to an elder's stories is a simple, genuine way to begin a real tie.","persona":"any","source":"hear his story"},
  {"id":"fm-1318","cat":"web-you-join","type":"role-play","hook":"At a gathering you feel shy and out of place. Your partner checks if you're okay.","setup":"Say it honestly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"A bit lost, honestly — could you stay close and tell me who's who?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"I'm fine, leave it.\""}],"relearn":"Asking your partner to help you read the room is how you find your footing, not a weakness.","persona":"Pooja","source":"who's who help"},
  {"id":"fm-1319","cat":"web-you-join","type":"role-play","hook":"A reserved sister-in-law has kept her distance. You want to open the door gently.","setup":"Say it lightly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"No rush at all — but I'd love to get to know you whenever you like.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Why are you always so cold to me?\""}],"relearn":"A patient, no-pressure invitation lets a guarded relative come closer in their own time.","persona":"any","source":"open the door"},
  {"id":"fm-1350","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Razia","source":"dowry demand is not negotiation","hook":"\"If in-laws ask for a fridge or a scooter, you just negotiate it down politely.\"","myth":{"un":"If in-laws ask for a fridge or scooter, you just negotiate it down politely.","re":"A demand for goods as a marriage condition is a dowry demand, which is illegal under the Dowry Prohibition Act 1961, not a price to haggle.","why":"You shut a demand down; you don't bargain over it."},"relearn":"A demand for goods tied to the marriage is an illegal dowry demand to refuse, not negotiate.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1351","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"control is not love","hook":"\"He checks my phone and decides who I meet because he loves me.\"","myth":{"un":"He checks my phone and decides who I meet because he loves me.","re":"Reading your phone and controlling who you see is coercive control, not love; love doesn't need to police you.","why":"Care respects your freedom; control removes it."},"relearn":"Monitoring your phone and choosing your friends is control, not a sign of love.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1352","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"economic control is abuse","hook":"\"Taking my whole salary and giving me an 'allowance' is just how our home runs.\"","myth":{"un":"Taking my whole salary and giving me an allowance is just how our home runs.","re":"Seizing your earnings and rationing money to you is economic abuse, not normal housekeeping.","why":"Sharing money is mutual; controlling all of it is not."},"relearn":"Taking your earnings and rationing an allowance is economic abuse, not housekeeping.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1353","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"a daughter-in-law's silence","hook":"\"A good bahu just bears the taunts about her dowry quietly.\"","myth":{"un":"A good bahu just bears the taunts about her dowry quietly.","re":"Repeated taunts and harassment over dowry are cruelty, not something to bear; you can name it and seek help.","why":"Enduring harm in silence protects the harm, not you."},"relearn":"Dowry taunts are harassment to name and get help for, not a test of being a good bahu.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1354","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"isolation is a red flag","hook":"\"They stopped me visiting my parents to help me 'settle into' the new family.\"","myth":{"un":"They stopped me visiting my parents to help me settle into the new family.","re":"Cutting you off from your own family and friends is isolation, an early sign of coercive control, not settling in.","why":"Joining a family adds people to your life; it doesn't subtract them."},"relearn":"Being cut off from your parents and friends is isolation and control, not 'settling in'.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1355","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Razia","source":"the home is not above the law","hook":"\"What a husband does inside his own house is nobody else's business.\"","myth":{"un":"What a husband does inside his own house is nobody else's business.","re":"Cruelty by a husband or his relatives is a crime; a closed door doesn't put harm beyond the law.","why":"Privacy protects a family's life, not its violence."},"relearn":"Cruelty at home is a crime; four walls don't place it above the law.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1356","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"threats are not discipline","hook":"\"He only threatens to throw me out when I 'push him too far'.\"","myth":{"un":"He only threatens to throw me out when I push him too far.","re":"Threats to abandon or harm you are abuse and never your fault, whatever was said before; they aren't discipline you earned.","why":"Nothing you do makes a threat your responsibility."},"relearn":"Threats to throw you out are abuse and never your fault, not something you provoked.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1357","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Razia","source":"the fix isn't more adjusting","hook":"\"If the abuse continues, she just needs to adjust a little harder.\"","myth":{"un":"If the abuse continues, she just needs to adjust a little harder.","re":"Abuse doesn't ease with more adjusting; the right response is help and safety, not a better boundary.","why":"You can't compromise your way out of someone else's control."},"relearn":"Abuse calls for help and safety, not more adjusting; that's not a flaw in your effort.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1358","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"asking for help is courage","hook":"\"Calling a helpline about your own family means you've failed at marriage.\"","myth":{"un":"Calling a helpline about your own family means you've failed at marriage.","re":"Reaching out about harm is courage, not failure; a marriage isn't a thing you alone have to hold up.","why":"Naming harm is strength, and you don't carry it alone."},"relearn":"Reaching a helpline about harm at home is courage, not a failed marriage.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1359","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"gifts with strings are a demand","hook":"\"They only 'suggest' what gifts our side should bring, so it isn't dowry.\"","myth":{"un":"They only suggest what gifts our side should bring, so it isn't dowry.","re":"A 'suggestion' that you owe goods as a condition of the match is a dowry demand, illegal under the Dowry Prohibition Act 1961, however softly it's put.","why":"Polite wording doesn't change what's being demanded."},"relearn":"A 'suggested' list of gifts owed for the match is still an illegal dowry demand.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1360","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"men face control too","hook":"\"A son-in-law can't really be controlled or harassed by his wife's family.\"","myth":{"un":"A son-in-law can't really be controlled or harassed by his wife's family.","re":"Coercion, threats and financial control can target anyone; harm isn't decided by which side you married into.","why":"Abuse is about the pattern of control, not the gender of who faces it."},"relearn":"Control and threats can target a son-in-law too; abuse isn't only one side's experience.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1361","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Razia","source":"laws give real protection","hook":"\"Dowry and cruelty laws only ruin families, so no one should use them.\"","myth":{"un":"Dowry and cruelty laws only ruin families, so no one should use them.","re":"These laws give real protection to people in genuine danger; that some cases are debated doesn't make the safety they offer false.","why":"A protection being imperfect isn't a reason to leave someone unprotected."},"relearn":"Dowry and cruelty laws offer genuine protection from serious harm, even where misuse is debated.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1362","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"one bad incident counts","hook":"\"It's only happened a couple of times, so it doesn't count as abuse yet.\"","myth":{"un":"It's only happened a couple of times, so it doesn't count as abuse yet.","re":"Harm doesn't need a long history to count; you can seek help and clarity after the very first time.","why":"You don't have to wait for it to get worse to deserve support."},"relearn":"You don't have to wait for a pattern; you can seek help after the first incident of harm.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1363","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Razia","source":"deny dowry, not your bride","hook":"\"Refusing to give dowry would shame our daughter on her wedding day.\"","myth":{"un":"Refusing to give dowry would shame our daughter on her wedding day.","re":"Declining a dowry demand protects your daughter; giving it is illegal and signals that demands will be met.","why":"Saying no to a demand is on the demander, never on her."},"relearn":"Refusing dowry protects your daughter; the shame belongs to the demand, not to her.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1364","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Reshma","source":"jealousy isn't proof of love","hook":"\"He gets angry if I talk to my brother, which just shows how much he cares.\"","myth":{"un":"He gets angry if I talk to my brother, which just shows how much he cares.","re":"Anger at your ordinary contact with family is controlling jealousy, not proof of love; it shrinks your world.","why":"Love widens the people you're allowed; control narrows them."},"relearn":"Anger over you talking to your own family is controlling jealousy, not a measure of love.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1365","type":"sort","persona":"Reshma","source":"friction or abuse","hook":"Sort: ordinary friction to work through, or harm that needs help?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"In-laws disagree about visit frequency"},{"id":"b","text":"He tracks your phone and where you go"},{"id":"c","text":"Tense words over a festival ritual"},{"id":"d","text":"They demand cash after the wedding"},{"id":"e","text":"You clash about chores"},{"id":"f","text":"Threatened if you don't hand over pay"}],"bins":[{"id":"friction","label":"Friction","valence":"pos"},{"id":"harm","label":"Harm, get help","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"friction","b":"harm","c":"friction","d":"harm","e":"friction","f":"harm"},"relearn":"Visit, ritual and chore clashes are friction; tracking, cash demands and threats are harm needing help.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1366","type":"sort","persona":"Reshma","source":"name the harm","hook":"Sort each behaviour into the kind of harm it is.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Stopping you seeing your parents or friends"},{"id":"b","text":"Taking your salary and rationing you money"},{"id":"c","text":"\"Tell your family to send a gold chain\""},{"id":"d","text":"Reading your phone, tracking your every move"},{"id":"e","text":"\"Where's the scooter your side promised?\""},{"id":"f","text":"Threatening to send you away if you refuse"}],"bins":[{"id":"isolate","label":"Isolation / control","valence":"neg"},{"id":"dowry","label":"Dowry demand","valence":"neg"},{"id":"threat","label":"Threats","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"isolate","b":"isolate","c":"dowry","d":"isolate","e":"dowry","f":"threat"},"relearn":"Cutting you off and controlling money is isolation; demands for gold or a scooter are dowry; 'I'll send you away' is a threat.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1367","type":"sort","persona":"Razia","source":"right help route","hook":"Sort each situation to the help route that fits.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"In-laws harassing you over dowry"},{"id":"b","text":"You're in danger right now"},{"id":"c","text":"You want to name a pattern, plan"},{"id":"d","text":"A girl about to be married off"},{"id":"e","text":"A woman who feels unsafe now"},{"id":"f","text":"You need someone to talk to"}],"bins":[{"id":"women","label":"Women Helpline 181","valence":"tell"},{"id":"emerg","label":"Emergency 112","valence":"tell"},{"id":"distress","label":"In distress 1091","valence":"tell"},{"id":"child","label":"Childline 1098","valence":"tell"},{"id":"counsel","label":"A counsellor","valence":"tell"}],"key":{"a":"women","b":"emerg","c":"counsel","d":"child","e":"distress","f":"counsel"},"relearn":"181 for dowry/in-law abuse, 112 for danger, 1091 in distress, 1098 for a girl married off, a counsellor to plan.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1368","type":"sort","persona":"Reshma","source":"yours to refuse or share","hook":"Sort: a demand to refuse, or an everyday matter to talk through?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Bring 5 lakh or the wedding's off\""},{"id":"b","text":"Whose parents to visit at Diwali"},{"id":"c","text":"\"Hand over your bonus or there's trouble\""},{"id":"d","text":"Agreeing a housewarming budget"},{"id":"e","text":"\"More gold must come from your side\""},{"id":"f","text":"Which relatives to invite over"}],"bins":[{"id":"refuse","label":"Demand: refuse","valence":"neg"},{"id":"talk","label":"Everyday: talk","valence":"pos"}],"key":{"a":"refuse","b":"talk","c":"refuse","d":"talk","e":"refuse","f":"talk"},"relearn":"Cash or gold tied to the marriage is illegal dowry to refuse; visits, budgets and guest lists are everyday talk.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1369","type":"sort","persona":"Reshma","source":"early signs","hook":"Sort each sign: a warning worth noticing, or normal newlywed life?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"He must approve every rupee you spend"},{"id":"b","text":"You're still learning each other's habits"},{"id":"c","text":"He gets cold if you message a friend"},{"id":"d","text":"You sometimes miss your old routine"},{"id":"e","text":"\"No one will believe you anyway\""},{"id":"f","text":"You're nervous meeting his big family"}],"bins":[{"id":"warn","label":"Warning sign","valence":"uhoh"},{"id":"normal","label":"Normal","valence":"pos"}],"key":{"a":"warn","b":"normal","c":"warn","d":"normal","e":"warn","f":"normal"},"relearn":"Controlling every rupee, punishing contact and 'no one will believe you' are warnings; settling in and nerves are normal.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1370","type":"sort","persona":"Reshma","source":"who carries it","hook":"Sort: whose fault is each thing, the person harmed, or the one doing the harm?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"He raised his hand when dinner was late"},{"id":"b","text":"They harassed her until her family paid"},{"id":"c","text":"She finally called a helpline for advice"},{"id":"d","text":"He cut her off from her sister"},{"id":"e","text":"She told a counsellor what was happening"},{"id":"f","text":"They threatened her over a 'small' gift"}],"bins":[{"id":"theirs","label":"On the one harming","valence":"neg"},{"id":"brave","label":"A brave, right step","valence":"pos"}],"key":{"a":"theirs","b":"theirs","c":"brave","d":"theirs","e":"brave","f":"theirs"},"relearn":"Violence, dowry harassment, isolation and threats are on the person harming; reaching for help is a brave, right step.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1371","type":"sort","persona":"Razia","source":"true or myth about the law","hook":"Sort each statement about the law: true, or a myth?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Giving dowry is also an offence"},{"id":"b","text":"A 'small' dowry is fine if both agree"},{"id":"c","text":"In-law cruelty can be a crime"},{"id":"d","text":"Abuse stops once you're married"},{"id":"e","text":"Economic abuse is a recognised harm"},{"id":"f","text":"You need injuries before anyone helps"}],"bins":[{"id":"true","label":"True","valence":"pos"},{"id":"myth","label":"Myth","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"true","b":"myth","c":"true","d":"myth","e":"true","f":"myth"},"relearn":"Giving dowry is an offence, in-law cruelty can be a crime, economic abuse counts; no 'small dowry' or injuries-required.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1372","type":"sort","persona":"Reshma","source":"safe next step","hook":"Sort: a step that builds safety, or a step that just keeps you stuck?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Quietly telling one trusted person"},{"id":"b","text":"Paying the demand to 'keep the peace'"},{"id":"c","text":"Saving a counsellor's number privately"},{"id":"d","text":"Promising to 'try harder' and saying nothing"},{"id":"e","text":"Noting down dates when things happened"},{"id":"f","text":"Waiting alone until it's 'bad enough'"}],"bins":[{"id":"safe","label":"Builds safety","valence":"pos"},{"id":"stuck","label":"Keeps you stuck","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"safe","b":"stuck","c":"safe","d":"stuck","e":"safe","f":"stuck"},"relearn":"Telling someone, saving help routes and noting dates build safety; paying off demands or waiting alone keep you stuck.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1373","type":"branch","persona":"Razia","source":"shut a hint down","hook":"At a family lunch, an aunt hints your parents 'should still send' a gold set.","options":[{"text":"Say plainly that dowry is illegal and your families won't be doing it","consequence":"You name it once, kindly and firmly, and close the door.","outcome":"named","best":true},{"text":"Laugh it off and quietly hope the hints stop","consequence":"Left unanswered, hints usually grow into demands."}],"debrief":"A dowry hint is shut down, not laughed off; naming it as illegal under the Dowry Prohibition Act 1961 ends it.","relearn":"Name a dowry hint as illegal and decline it plainly; laughing it off invites more.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1374","type":"branch","persona":"Reshma","source":"he controls the money","hook":"Your husband takes your whole salary and gives you a small 'allowance' you must justify.","options":[{"text":"Name it as economic control and reach a counsellor or 181","consequence":"You see it clearly and find a route to support.","outcome":"named","best":true},{"text":"Decide it's normal and stop questioning it","consequence":"Calling control 'normal' lets it keep tightening."}],"debrief":"Seizing your earnings and rationing money is economic abuse; a counsellor or Women Helpline 181 can help.","relearn":"Controlling all your money is economic abuse; name it and reach a counsellor or 181.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1375","type":"branch","persona":"Reshma","source":"cut off from family","hook":"Your in-laws keep finding reasons you can't visit or call your parents.","options":[{"text":"Keep your contact and confide in someone you trust","consequence":"You hold your link to family and aren't alone with it.","outcome":"connected","best":true},{"text":"Slowly drop all contact to avoid friction","consequence":"Dropping every link is what isolation needs to grow."}],"debrief":"Being steadily cut off from your family is isolation, not keeping the peace.","relearn":"Keep your link to family; being cut off is isolation, not peace-keeping.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1376","type":"branch","persona":"Razia","source":"a sister asks for help","hook":"Your sister says her husband threatens her and in-laws demand 'gifts'.","options":[{"text":"Believe her, say it's not her fault, share 181","consequence":"She feels backed and learns real help exists.","outcome":"supported","best":true},{"text":"Say every marriage is hard, she should adjust","consequence":"Naming threats and dowry as 'adjusting' leaves her stuck."}],"debrief":"Threats and dowry demands are abuse; believe her, say it's not her fault, share 181.","relearn":"Believe someone facing threats and dowry demands; share 181, don't say 'adjust'.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1377","type":"branch","persona":"Reshma","source":"unsure it counts","hook":"Nothing's 'bad enough' to name, but you feel watched, rationed and small at home.","options":[{"text":"Reach a counsellor or 181 anyway to make sense of it","consequence":"You get clarity and support without needing to be certain.","outcome":"reached","best":true},{"text":"Wait until something undeniable happens","consequence":"Waiting for proof often means waiting far too long."}],"debrief":"You don't have to be sure it 'counts'; a counsellor or 181 can help you name a pattern early.","relearn":"You can reach help while unsure; you needn't wait for it to get undeniable.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1378","type":"branch","persona":"Karthik","source":"his family pressures her side","hook":"You overhear your parents telling your wife's family they 'expect' a car.","options":[{"text":"Tell your parents plainly: no dowry will change hands","consequence":"You stand with your partner and stop an illegal demand.","outcome":"united","best":true},{"text":"Stay out of it; it's 'between the families'","consequence":"Silence lets your own side make an illegal demand in your name."}],"debrief":"A dowry demand from your side is yours to stop; stand with your partner and shut it down.","relearn":"If your own family demands dowry, step in; silence makes you part of it.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1379","type":"branch","persona":"Reshma","source":"threatened over salary","hook":"He says if you don't hand over your bonus, you'll 'regret it'.","options":[{"text":"Treat it as a threat, keep yourself safe, and note what was said","consequence":"You take a threat seriously and start a record.","outcome":"safe","best":true},{"text":"Hand it over and tell yourself he didn't mean it","consequence":"Excusing a threat teaches that threats work on you."}],"debrief":"'You'll regret it' over money is a threat, not a bad mood; take it seriously and reach help if it repeats.","relearn":"A threat tied to money is abuse to take seriously; don't explain it away.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1380","type":"branch","persona":"Razia","source":"friend wants to call it nothing","hook":"A colleague laughs that her mother-in-law 'only' threw out her things and screamed for hours.","options":[{"text":"Gently say that sounds frightening and ask if she's okay","consequence":"She feels seen and the harm isn't minimised.","outcome":"seen","best":true},{"text":"Agree it's 'just how saas-bahu is' and move on","consequence":"Calling intimidation 'just saas-bahu' normalises real harm."}],"debrief":"Screaming and destroying your things to frighten you is intimidation, not the usual saas-bahu tease.","relearn":"Intimidation isn't 'just saas-bahu'; name it gently and check the person is okay.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1381","type":"branch","persona":"Reshma","source":"keeping a quiet record","hook":"The control at home is worsening and you're not sure what to do first.","options":[{"text":"Quietly save a helpline, tell one trusted person, note incidents","consequence":"You build quiet support and a record, at your own pace.","outcome":"prepared","best":true},{"text":"Confront everyone loudly and hope it shocks them","consequence":"One loud confrontation can raise the risk before you're safe."}],"debrief":"Quiet steps, a saved number, a trusted person, notes, build safety better than one blow-up.","relearn":"Build safety quietly: a saved helpline, a trusted person, a record, not a blow-up.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1382","type":"branch","persona":"Reshma","source":"the demand returns","hook":"You refused a dowry demand once, but the in-laws raise it again, more insistently.","options":[{"text":"Repeat the same plain 'no' and bring in a counsellor or 181","consequence":"You hold the line and add real support behind it.","outcome":"held","best":true},{"text":"Give a little this time so they finally stop","consequence":"Giving in once tends to reset the demand, not end it."}],"debrief":"A repeated dowry demand is harassment; hold the same refusal and add help, don't pay to make it stop.","relearn":"Repeat your 'no' to a renewed dowry demand and add 181 or a counsellor; paying just resets it.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1383","type":"branch","persona":"Karthik","source":"asked to choose a side","hook":"Privately, your mother tells you to make your wife 'fall in line' or there'll be trouble.","options":[{"text":"Decline to police her; talk to your mother as a united couple","consequence":"You refuse to be a tool of control and stay a team.","outcome":"team","best":true},{"text":"Pass the pressure on and lean on your wife","consequence":"Relaying the pressure makes you the channel for control."}],"debrief":"Being asked to 'make her fall in line' recruits you into control; decline and stand as a couple.","relearn":"Don't relay pressure to 'make her comply'; refusing keeps you a team.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1384","type":"spot","persona":"Reshma","source":"spot the control","hook":"Spot the two lines that are control, not ordinary married life.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Let's plan our weekend together\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"You can't keep any money of your own\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"I'd like to meet your friends sometime\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Delete his number or face consequences\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"Can we share the chores this week?\"","trick":false}],"why":"Banning you from any money and ordering you to cut a contact under threat are control; the rest is normal.","relearn":"Controlling your money and forcing you to cut people off is coercive control.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1385","type":"spot","persona":"Razia","source":"spot the dowry demand","hook":"Spot the two lines that are illegal dowry demands.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"We'd love to host both families for dinner\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Your side must arrange a car before the wedding\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Bring whatever sweets you like\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"No gold set, no marriage\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"Let's split the function costs fairly\"","trick":false}],"why":"Demanding a car or gold as a condition of the marriage is an illegal dowry demand; dinners, sweets and fairly shared costs are not.","relearn":"Goods demanded as a condition of the marriage are illegal dowry; shared, freely given hospitality is not.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1386","type":"spot","persona":"Reshma","source":"spot the threat","hook":"Spot the two lines that are threats, not heated words.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"I'm upset and need a minute to cool down\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Say that again and I'll send you back to your parents\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Can we talk about this tomorrow?\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Cross me and you'll regret it\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"I disagree, but let's hear each other out\"","trick":false}],"why":"'I'll send you back' and 'you'll regret it' are threats meant to frighten and control; cooling off, pausing and disagreeing calmly are not.","relearn":"Words meant to frighten you into obeying are threats, not just a heated argument.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1387","type":"spot","persona":"Reshma","source":"spot the isolation","hook":"Spot the two moves that are isolation, not just a busy joint household.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"The family eats dinner together most nights","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"You're stopped from calling your parents","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Weekends are full of relatives visiting","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Your friends are forbidden, one by one","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Everyone pitches in for the festival","trick":false}],"why":"Being blocked from your parents and forbidden your friends cuts you off, that's isolation; shared meals and festivals are normal.","relearn":"Being blocked from your own family and friends is isolation; a busy household is not.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1388","type":"spot","persona":"Reshma","source":"spot crossing the line","hook":"Spot the two signs that friction has crossed into abuse.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"You argue sometimes about visiting schedules","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"You're punished with silence and locked rooms","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"You don't always like the same festivals","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"You're afraid to speak in your own home","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"You're still learning each other's habits","trick":false}],"why":"Punishment and living in fear are abuse; disagreeing about visits or festivals and still adjusting are ordinary friction.","relearn":"Living in fear and being punished are abuse; disagreement and adjusting are ordinary friction.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1389","type":"spot","persona":"Reshma","source":"spot the manipulation","hook":"Spot the two lines designed to keep you silent, not to make peace.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Let's both apologise and move on\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"No one will ever believe you\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"I was wrong earlier, I'm sorry\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Tell anyone and you'll lose everything\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"Can we start fresh tomorrow?\"","trick":false}],"why":"'No one will believe you' and 'you'll lose everything' are made to keep you silent and trapped; the apologies are not.","relearn":"Lines that make you feel unbelievable or that you'll lose everything are made to silence you.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1390","type":"spot","persona":"Reshma","source":"spot economic abuse","hook":"Spot the two money moves that are economic abuse, not shared budgeting.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"You both agree a monthly budget","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"He takes your pay, you beg for bus fare","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"You split bills in a way that suits you both","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"You're banned from any money of your own","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"You each save a little for your own goals","trick":false}],"why":"Seizing your pay and banning you from any money are economic abuse; agreeing budgets, splitting and saving are healthy.","relearn":"Seizing your earnings and banning you from any money of your own is economic abuse.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1391","type":"match","persona":"Razia","source":"route to the right help","hook":"Match each situation to the help route that fits it.","pairs":[{"left":"In-law or dowry harassment","right":"Women Helpline 181"},{"left":"Immediate danger right now","right":"Emergency / police 112"},{"left":"A woman in distress, unsafe","right":"Women in distress 1091"},{"left":"A girl about to be married off","right":"Childline 1098"},{"left":"Naming a pattern and planning","right":"A counsellor"}],"relearn":"181 for dowry/in-law abuse, 112 for danger, 1091 in distress, 1098 for a girl married off, a counsellor to plan.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1392","type":"match","persona":"Reshma","source":"name the behaviour","hook":"Match each behaviour to what it really is.","pairs":[{"left":"Banning you from your parents","right":"Isolation"},{"left":"Taking your salary, rationing you","right":"Economic abuse"},{"left":"\"Send a gold set or else\"","right":"Dowry demand"},{"left":"\"You'll regret crossing me\"","right":"A threat"},{"left":"Disagreeing over visit dates","right":"Ordinary friction"}],"relearn":"Blocking your family is isolation, controlling money is economic abuse, demanding gold is dowry, threats are threats, visit clashes are just friction.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1393","type":"match","persona":"Reshma","source":"friction vs abuse","hook":"Match each line to whether it's friction or abuse.","pairs":[{"left":"Clashing festival customs","right":"Friction to work through"},{"left":"Threats if you don't obey","right":"Abuse, get help"},{"left":"Different ideas on visits","right":"Friction to talk over"},{"left":"Money controlled by force","right":"Abuse, reach 181"},{"left":"Learning each other's habits","right":"Normal adjusting"}],"relearn":"Custom clashes, visit differences and adjusting are friction; threats and money controlled by force are abuse needing help.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1394","type":"match","persona":"Razia","source":"myth to truth","hook":"Match each myth to the truth that replaces it.","pairs":[{"left":"\"A little dowry is tradition\"","right":"Dowry is illegal, even a little"},{"left":"\"Home matters stay private\"","right":"Privacy never covers abuse"},{"left":"\"She should just adjust more\"","right":"Abuse needs help, not adjusting"},{"left":"\"It must be her fault\"","right":"Abuse is never the victim's fault"},{"left":"\"Asking for help is shameful\"","right":"Seeking help is courage"}],"relearn":"Dowry is illegal, privacy doesn't cover abuse, the fix is help not adjusting, it's never your fault, and asking for help is courage.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1395","type":"match","persona":"Reshma","source":"first safe steps","hook":"Match each safe first step to what it gives you.","pairs":[{"left":"Saving a helpline privately","right":"A route ready when you need it"},{"left":"Telling one trusted person","right":"You're no longer alone with it"},{"left":"Noting dates of incidents","right":"A quiet record you can rely on"},{"left":"Calling a counsellor","right":"Help making sense of the pattern"},{"left":"Keeping your own contacts","right":"A link to people outside the home"}],"relearn":"A saved number, a trusted person, a record, a counsellor and your own contacts are quiet first steps that build safety.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1396","type":"match","persona":"Razia","source":"the law in plain words","hook":"Match each plain fact to what the law says.","pairs":[{"left":"Giving or taking dowry","right":"An offence in India"},{"left":"Demanding dowry","right":"Also illegal"},{"left":"Cruelty by husband or in-laws","right":"Can be a crime"},{"left":"Economic, emotional abuse","right":"Recognised harms"},{"left":"A closed front door","right":"Doesn't beat the law"}],"relearn":"Giving, taking and demanding dowry are illegal, in-law cruelty can be a crime, and economic abuse counts.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1397","type":"match","persona":"Reshma","source":"who it's never about","hook":"Match each worry to the reassurance that meets it.","pairs":[{"left":"\"Maybe I provoked it\"","right":"Abuse is never your fault"},{"left":"\"It's my private shame\"","right":"There's no shame in being harmed"},{"left":"\"I should manage alone\"","right":"You don't have to carry it alone"},{"left":"\"It isn't bad enough yet\"","right":"You can seek help any time"},{"left":"\"No one will help me\"","right":"181, 112 and counsellors are real"}],"relearn":"It's never your fault, never your shame, never yours to carry alone; you can seek help any time, and real routes exist.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1398","type":"reflect","persona":"Reshma","source":"the clear line","hook":"Lensy: friction you work through kindly; control, threats or a dowry demand are abuse, not boundary problems. Sit with that?","prompt":"What lands for you?","options":["The line is clearer now","That's a real difference","Good to know"],"affirm":"Boundaries handle everyday friction; control, threats and dowry demands are abuse that needs help, not negotiation.","relearn":"Control, threats and dowry demands aren't boundary problems; they're abuse that needs help.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1399","type":"reflect","persona":"Reshma","source":"never your fault","hook":"Lensy: if someone controls, threatens or harms you, that is theirs to own, never something you caused. Hear it?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["I hear it","Not on me","Thank you"],"affirm":"Control, threats and harm are the choice of the person doing them; nothing you did makes that your fault.","relearn":"Abuse is on the person doing it; nothing you did makes their harm your fault.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1400","type":"reflect","persona":"Reshma","source":"help is courage","hook":"Lensy: reaching for help with a harmful home isn't failing at marriage, it's a brave, ordinary thing to do. Take that in?","prompt":"How does that sit?","options":["It helps to hear","It's brave, not failing","I'll remember it"],"affirm":"Asking for help with harm at home is courage, not failure, and not something you have to hold up alone.","relearn":"Seeking help with a harmful home is courage, not a failed marriage.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1401","type":"reflect","persona":"Reshma","source":"you can be unsure","hook":"Lensy: you don't have to be certain it 'counts' before you reach out, uncertainty is reason enough. Okay?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["That's a relief","I don't need proof","Makes sense"],"affirm":"You can seek help while still unsure; a counsellor or 181 can help you make sense of what's happening.","relearn":"You can reach out while unsure; you don't need proof it's 'serious enough' first.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1402","type":"reflect","persona":"Reshma","source":"your money, your link","hook":"Lensy: having your own money and your own people isn't selfish, it's part of a healthy life. Feel that?","prompt":"What comes up?","options":["I feel that","It's not selfish","Good reminder"],"affirm":"Holding some money of your own and keeping your own people are healthy and yours; losing them by force is a warning sign.","relearn":"Your own money and your own people are healthy to keep; losing them by force is a warning sign.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1403","type":"reflect","persona":"Razia","source":"dowry is never yours to owe","hook":"Lensy: no family owes another goods or cash for a marriage, a demand is on the one demanding, not on you. Clear?","prompt":"What's your read?","options":["Clear","It's their demand, not my debt","Noted"],"affirm":"You owe no dowry; a demand is illegal and rests with whoever makes it, never with the family it's aimed at.","relearn":"No family owes dowry; a demand is illegal and belongs to the one making it, not to you.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1404","type":"reflect","persona":"Reshma","source":"believe yourself","hook":"Lensy: if home leaves you small, watched and afraid, that feeling is worth trusting, not arguing down. Sit with it?","prompt":"What stands out?","options":["I can trust it","Worth listening to","Thanks for that"],"affirm":"Feeling watched, controlled and afraid at home is real information; you're allowed to trust it and seek support.","relearn":"Feeling watched, small and afraid at home is worth trusting, and worth seeking support for.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1405","type":"reflect","persona":"Reshma","source":"safety over keeping peace","hook":"Lensy: 'keeping the peace' should never cost your safety, your safety comes first. Take that with you?","prompt":"What lands?","options":["I'll take it","Safety first","That matters"],"affirm":"Keeping the peace is good for friction, but never at the price of your safety; when there's harm, safety and help come first.","relearn":"Keep the peace for friction, but never at the cost of safety; with harm, safety and help come first.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1406","type":"role-play","persona":"Razia","source":"refuse a dowry list","hook":"An uncle slides you a 'list' of what your family should bring. You want to decline, plainly.","setup":"Say it clearly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"Dowry is illegal, so there'll be no list, our families just celebrate together.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Oh, um, I'll pass it along and see, maybe.\""}],"relearn":"Naming dowry as illegal and declining the list plainly shuts the demand down without leaving a door open.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1407","type":"role-play","persona":"Reshma","source":"reclaim your money","hook":"Your husband says you must hand over your salary each month. You want to name it, calmly.","setup":"Say it steadily:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"My earnings stay mine to share; deciding our money together is fine, handing it all over isn't.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Okay, fine, take it, I don't want a fight.\""}],"relearn":"Sharing money together is healthy; handing all your earnings over on demand is control to name, not accept.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1408","type":"role-play","persona":"Reshma","source":"hold your link to family","hook":"You're told you may no longer visit your parents. You want to hold the line, warmly but firmly.","setup":"Say it kindly and clearly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I'll always stay in touch with my parents, that part isn't up for debate.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"I guess I'll just stop going, if it's easier.\""}],"relearn":"Keeping contact with your own parents isn't negotiable; quietly dropping them is what isolation needs.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1409","type":"role-play","persona":"Reshma","source":"name a threat","hook":"He says you'll 'regret it' if you don't obey. You want to name it, not absorb it.","setup":"Say it plainly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"That's a threat, and threats aren't how we talk to each other.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Sorry, sorry, I'll do whatever you want.\""}],"relearn":"Naming a threat as a threat is the assertive move; rushing to obey teaches that threats work.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1410","type":"role-play","persona":"Karthik","source":"back your partner","hook":"At dinner, relatives push your wife to accept a 'gift' demand. You want to stand with her, in the room.","setup":"Say it as a team:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"We've decided together: no dowry changes hands, and that's final for both of us.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's, uh, not get into it now, we'll see later.\""}],"relearn":"Backing your partner in the room with a united 'no' is a team move, not choosing sides against family.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1411","type":"role-play","persona":"Reshma","source":"ask for help out loud","hook":"You finally call a counsellor and your voice shakes. You want to start, even unsure.","setup":"Begin with the truth:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"I'm not sure it 'counts', but things at home don't feel safe and I need to talk.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Actually, never mind, it's probably nothing, sorry.\""}],"relearn":"You can ask for help while unsure; 'I'm not sure it counts, but I need to talk' is a brave, complete start.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
  {"id":"fm-1412","type":"role-play","persona":"Razia","source":"decline to police her","hook":"A relative tells you to 'control your wife'. You want to refuse, without a fight.","setup":"Say it calmly:","yourLine":[{"text":"\"She's my partner, not someone I control; we sort things out together.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Fine, I'll have a word and make her listen.\""}],"relearn":"Declining to 'control' your partner keeps you a team and refuses to be a channel for control.","cat":"when-it-turns-harmful"},
];

